var __index = {"config": {"lang": ["en"], "separator": "[\\s\\-\\.]+", "pipeline": ["stemmer"], "fields": {"title": {"boost": 1000.0}, "text": {"boost": 1.0}, "tags": {"boost": 1000000.0}}}, "docs": [{"location": "index.html", "title": "Product Introduction", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Product Introduction<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB = Max Knowledge Brain. It is a powerful and easy-to-use enterprise-grade agent platform dedicated to solving problems such as high technical barriers, high deployment costs, and long iteration cycles faced in enterprise AI adoption, helping enterprises gain an edge in the era of artificial intelligence.</p>\n<p>Guided by the design philosophy of \"Out of the box, growing with you,\" MaxKB enables enterprises to quickly connect mainstream large models and efficiently build dedicated Knowledge Bases. It provides a progressive upgrade path from basic knowledge Q&amp;A (RAG) and complex business process automation (Workflow) to Agents, effectively empowering a wide range of scenarios such as intelligent customer service and smart office.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Product Philosophy\" src=\"img/index/%E4%BA%A7%E5%93%81%E7%90%86%E5%BF%B5.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 How It Works<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<p><img alt=\"Overview\" src=\"img/index/%E6%9E%B6%E6%9E%84%E5%9B%BE.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Product Advantages<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>RAG Retrieval Augmented</strong> <br/>\n  Supports uploading documents directly / automatically crawling online documents, with automatic text splitting, vectorization, and RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation), effectively reducing LLM hallucination and providing an excellent interactive intelligent Q&amp;A experience;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Flexible Orchestration</strong> <br/>\n  A powerful built-in workflow engine, function library, and MCP tool invocation capability, supporting the orchestration of AI workflows to meet the needs of complex business scenarios;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Seamless Embedding</strong> <br/>\n  Supports quick zero-code embedding into third-party business systems, allowing existing systems to quickly gain intelligent Q&amp;A capability and improving user satisfaction;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Model Neutral</strong> <br/>\n  Supports connecting to various LLMs, including local private models (Llama 3 / Qwen 2, etc.), domestic public models (DeepSeek / SILICONFLOW / Qwen / Tencent Hunyuan / Doubao / Baidu Qianfan / Zhipu AI / Kimi, etc.), and international public models (OpenAI / Azure OpenAI / Anthropic / Gemini, etc.).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Interface Display<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<p><img alt=\"Page\" src=\"img/index/index1.gif\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Case Demonstration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Since its release, MaxKB has averaged more than 1,000 installs/downloads per day and is widely used in scenarios such as intelligent customer service, enterprise internal knowledge bases, academic research, and education. For details on typical use cases, see the following links:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/w6ZY9fQpdeQ0vQkKZA-DYA\">MaxKB Use Case: CITIC Securities</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/4g_gySMBQZCJ9OZ-yBkmvw\">MaxKB Use Case: China Agricultural University - Xiao Wu Ge</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/3BoxkY7EMomMmmvFYxvDIA\">MaxKB Use Case: Dongbei University of Finance and Economics - Little Ginkgo</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/8L4hIjdhzWOmpQXx2cW33g\">MaxKB Use Case: Chongqing Jiaotong University - Yu Xiao Jiao</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/83N9a_wWDce7z1NLIropEA\">MaxKB Use Case: Guangxi University</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/WUmAKYbZjp3272HIecpRFA\">MaxKB Use Case: Nanjing University of Chinese Medicine</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1yvBMYvEdy\">MaxKB Use Case: university administrative management AI little assistant</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/voNAddbK2CJOrJJs1ewZ8g\">MaxKB Use Case: China Railway Water</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/ETrZC-vrA4Aap0eF-15EeQ\">MaxKB Use Case: Chinese PLA General Hospital</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/CbKr4mev8qahKLAtV6Dxdg\">MaxKB Use Case: CNNC Xiyi Research Institute - Xiyi RuiDa</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/DSOUvwrQrxbqQxKBilTCFQ\">MaxKB Use Case: Xi'an International Medical Center Hospital - Guoyi Little Helper</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.nfnews.com/content/732YEYDPyW.html\">MaxKB Use Case: Shenzhen University Affiliated South China Hospital - medical \"knowledge database assistant\"</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV13JzvYsE3e\">MaxKB Use Case: biomedical AI customer service intelligent experience!</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV157wme9EgB\">MaxKB Use Case: turning medical industry knowledge into a knowledge base Q&amp;A assistant!</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/KEtM-bkqim5LLBc4yA9CmQ\">MaxKB Use Case: Shenzhen Futian Notary Office AI assistant</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/enfUFLevvL_La74PQ0kIXw\">MaxKB Use Case: Wuxi Municipal Data Bureau</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/JNOk8gMrcX1c70A_bX1pfQ\">MaxKB Use Case: Guangxi Quality Inspection Institute - AI Xiao Zhi</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/3DXghaIT1p1aTQ51D2FCVA\">MaxKB Use Case: Shenzhen United Property and Equity Exchange - Shen Xiao Lian AI assistant</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/L-2s_JlU5bta_qo5aa5NDQ\">MaxKB Use Case: Anhui Trading Group releases an AI tender document review system</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/SILN0GSescH9LyeQqYP0VQ\">MaxKB Use Case: Shenzhen Tong opens a new chapter in DeepSeek intelligent applications</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/WEC9UQ6msY0VS8LhTZh-Ew\">MaxKB Use Case: \"Changxing Nantong\" intelligent customer service</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/eFlbTpQtx0gDrlOlb5onbA\">MaxKB Use Case: Jinan Metro - fully integrated with DeepSeek! \"AI + Rail\" makes citizens' travel smarter</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/mZJx7bldKgL2wEQiORccWw\">MaxKB Use Case: Guangzhou Port - leveraging the DeepSeek open-source large language model to empower port equipment management</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/dVLwq33U2scggw6_skkvvQ\">MaxKB Use Case: Sichuan Airlines - the Sichuan Airlines AI assistant reports for duty!</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1hQtVeXEBL\">MaxKB Use Case: Wallace's intelligent AI customer service assistant is online!</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1J7BqY6EKA\">MaxKB Use Case: exhibition AI intelligent customer service experience</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1wKrhYvEer\">MaxKB Use Case: your child is starting kindergarten? The AI intelligent assistant is a great choice-hunting helper</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1Yz6gYtEqX\">MaxKB Use Case: a product usage guide AI assistant - even beginners can handle it easily!</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/Ts5FQdnv7Tu9Jp7bvofCVA\">MaxKB Use Case: Suzhou Thermal Engineering Research Institute Co., Ltd. - bulk materials solution drafting and review assistant</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/HNPc7u5xVfGLJr8IQz3vjQ\">MaxKB Use Case: State Nuclear Automation System Engineering Co., Ltd. - NuCON AI Help</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/OGcEkjh9DzGO1Tkc9nr7qg\">MaxKB Use Case: CSSC Power artificial intelligence \"Smart Power Cloud Assistant\" and the first batch of digital employees officially launched</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/SZstxTvVoLZg0ECbZbfpIA\">MaxKB Use Case: Nanning Mining Group smart mine AI assistant</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/Eczdx574MS5RMF7WfHN7_A\">MaxKB Use Case: DeepSeek deployed at Hongsheng Copper: a domestic large language model ignites a new engine for the \"lights-out factory\"</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/D5vBtlX2E81pWE3_2OgWSw\">MaxKB Use Case: embracing the intelligent era! China Minmetals empowers enterprise development with \"AI+\"</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/8m0vxGcWXNdZazziQrLyxg\">MaxKB Use Case: DeepSeek empowering MCC Wukan's AI agent</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/ZKmEU_wWShK1YDomKJHQeA\">MaxKB Use Case: big news! Shaanxi Broadcasting &amp; TV Network's \"Qinling Cloud\" platform achieves local DeepSeek deployment</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/tYp8al1RpE8mXsDDmPZMDA\">MaxKB Use Case: Yuyuan Inc. - Party-masses AI agent - E Jia Tong Zhi (beta) is here</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/2JbVp0-kr9Hfp-0whH4cvg\">MaxKB Use Case: Yuehai Group completes private DeepSeek deployment, supporting the group's intelligent management</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/HThGSnND3qDF8ySEqiM4jw\">MaxKB Use Case: the Building Materials Industry Information Center completes local DeepSeek deployment, driving new development in the industry's digital and intelligent transformation</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/m67e-H7iQBg3d24NM82UjA\">MaxKB Use Case: Let's DeepSeek! Fujian Design opens a new chapter with an AI large language model</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://dzb.henandaily.cn/html5/2025-07/25/content_10_1749478.htm?curr=\">MaxKB Use Case: Zhengzhou Customs launches an AI document-review agent</a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"5\">5 Learn More<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://fit2cloud.com/maxkb/download/introduce-maxkb_202507.pdf\">How to Introduce MaxKB to Your Team</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://edu.fit2cloud.com/index\">FIT2CLOUD Training and Certification Center</a> </li>\n<li><a href=\"https://space.bilibili.com/510493147/lists/3590204?type=season\">MaxKB Mini Course</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://kb.fit2cloud.com/categories/maxkb\">MaxKB Knowledge Base</a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "index.html#1", "title": "1 How It Works ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "index.html#2", "title": "2 Product Advantages ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "index.html#3", "title": "3 Interface Display ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "index.html#4", "title": "4 Case Demonstration ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "index.html#5", "title": "5 Learn More ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html", "title": "Changelog", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Changelog</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Release Notes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Version Description:</strong> Like other excellent open-source projects, MaxKB will keep releasing a new feature version every month; when an urgent or serious Bug is encountered in a feature version, a minor Bug-fix version will be released promptly.<br/>\n<strong>The MaxKB version numbering convention is:</strong> v Major.Feature.Bug-fix version, for example:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>v2.0.1 is a bug-fix release after v2.0.0</li>\n<li>v2.1.0 is a feature release after v2.0.0</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Update Content<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"v2105-lts\">v2.10.5-lts<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v2105-lts\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>August 6, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition warning\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Security Vulnerability Fixes</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the issue where the chat share link endpoint lacked owner checks, allowing chat tokens to share other users' conversation content.</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the unauthorized access issue where regular users could obtain workspace user information of other workspaces through API interfaces. (#6576)</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the unauthorized access issue where the API key of any user could be used to delete any file.</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the issue where regular users could obtain sensitive information such as other users' email addresses through API interfaces. (#6577)</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Fixed an issue where images returned by the Knowledge Base failed to load during chat;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where, when uploading a PDF document, if the title and body content in the document have the same content, the paragraph content is incorrect (#6543)</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where the \"Allow preview in knowledge source\" option was incorrectly displayed in the document import dialog of the Web knowledge base;</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where copied conversation content was truncated when the content was long (#6568).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where images in the AI reply could not be accessed when the agent was embedded in a third party.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where images generated by the agent's image generation node could not be accessed.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where an error prompt popped up after agent debugging, making it impossible to view the execution details.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where a simple agent could retrieve using unpublished knowledge base retrieval configurations (#6519).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where loading failed after extracting images from a file in the file content extraction node.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where agent trigger task execution failed.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the output content of the workflow tool node in the agent was not written to the conversation log.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the agent's opening message failed to pass user parameters using the sendMessage method, losing the user's question.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where users without permission failed to preview or download files in the knowledge source of the Q&amp;A interface.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, when multiple files were uploaded in an agent conversation, downloading the files from the conversation log prompted that some files had no permission.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, when clearing conversation logs, some data was not cleared, causing incorrect active user statistics in the overview.</li>\n<li>Role (X-Pack): fixed the issue where some features lacked permission bit control;</li>\n<li>Shared Resources (X-Pack): Fixed the issue where system administrators were redirected to the wrong page when clicking \"Upload Document\" in a shared knowledge base.</li>\n<li>Shared Resources (X-Pack): Fixed the issue where Hit Testing could be accessed for shared knowledge bases within a workspace.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v2104-lts\">v2.10.4-lts<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v2104-lts\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>July 16, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, after adding a vision model to the image understanding node of an advanced agent, it was not displayed in the model list in real time (#6402).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, after deleting the LLM configured in a simple agent, the prompt information during conversation was incorrect.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the agent failed to call a shared model and prompted \"Model does not exist\".</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where, when a Word document table has no blank line before the following content, the segmented text was mistakenly identified as table content (#6396);</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where dragging segments would contaminate all paragraph position data across documents (#6373);</li>\n<li>Home: Fixed the issue where the ranking details page could find, via name search, agents that the current user has no permission to access;</li>\n<li>Trigger: fixed the issue where tasks were displayed repeatedly in the task details of the scheduled trigger list;</li>\n<li>Trigger: fixed the issue where, in trigger scenarios, the default values of the Advanced Agent user input parameters were not passed and the parameters were empty (#6320);</li>\n<li>Trigger: fixed the issue where the trigger reported an error when passing parameters when the Agent user input contained a switch-type parameter;</li>\n<li>User Management: fixed the issue where the get-all-users API only returned the first 200 users, making it impossible to retrieve all users (#6375).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition warning\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Security Vulnerability Fixes</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Vulnerability: Fixed the issue where resources could be accessed anonymously due to a system file permission vulnerability;</li>\n<li>Vulnerability: Fixed the IDOR vulnerability in admin-side chat records, resolving the issues of application path authentication bypass and reading chat records across applications;</li>\n<li>Vulnerability: Added a dedicated authorization verification mechanism for agent and workflow tool scheduling;</li>\n<li>Vulnerability: Fixed the issue where UpdateStoreTool lacked host verification when fetching external app store URLs;</li>\n<li>Vulnerability: Fixed the issue where users could obtain or modify unauthorized document and segment data across knowledge bases beyond their permissions;</li>\n<li>Vulnerability: Fixed the issue where expired agent API keys could still be used on the /chat/api/mcp interface;</li>\n<li>Vulnerability: Fixed the horizontal privilege escalation vulnerability caused by a defect in MCP tool authorization;</li>\n<li>Vulnerability: Fixed the issue where the home page ranking leaked the application ID, which could lead to malicious calls to other users' application nodes;</li>\n<li>Vulnerability: Fixed the issue where model parameter forms could be viewed or modified across workspaces beyond permissions;</li>\n<li>Vulnerability: Fixed the prompt injection vulnerability, mitigating the risk of agent command execution;</li>\n<li>Vulnerability: Improved the internal IP verification mechanism of the web document import/sync crawler, fixing the SSRF security risk.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v2103-lts\">v2.10.3-lts<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v2103-lts\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>July 3, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Added a visual display of file upload progress, and files that fail to upload can be re-uploaded with one click;</li>\n<li>Agent: The cleanup policy for agent chat logs supports batch configuration (#6213);</li>\n<li>Agent (X-Pack): WeCom bot integration supports voice input.</li>\n<li>Agent: optimized the copy on the overview page and unified the visual style to be consistent with the Home page.</li>\n<li>Role Permissions (X-Pack): added a Home page viewing permission configuration item for Regular Users and Workspace Administrators.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Agent (X-Pack): fixed the issue where multiple agents connected to WeCom at the same time shared the same chat_session_id, causing a 500 error in the conversation (#6325).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the interface parameter variables in an advanced agent could not be assigned correctly during debugging (#6271).</li>\n<li>Agent (X-Pack): fixed the UI issue where, after enabling the disclaimer, the mobile input box obscured the Like and Dislike buttons (#6249).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the visibility control conditions of user-input external parameters did not take effect.</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where the style of video content in replies was rendered abnormally on mobile scenarios;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where uploading and parsing a PDF document containing special characters reported an error;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where, when the knowledge base contained video files, the export operation did not synchronize and export the video resources;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where regular users had no permission to read the tool list when operating the MCP call node of the workflow knowledge base;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where, after importing the knowledge base workflow, tools in the loop body did not generate associated references, causing the tool node to become invalid and unusable;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where the segment preview page occasionally displayed duplicate segment content after document upload was completed;</li>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where the Qwen3-VL-Reranker-8B rerank model under the vLLM provider reported an error when called in the multi-path recall node (#6321);</li>\n<li>System Settings (X-Pack): Fixed an issue where, after configuring a custom Logo, refreshing the page would briefly flash the default MaxKB Logo (#6295).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v2102-lts\">v2.10.2-lts<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v2102-lts\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>June 18, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Adjusted the voice input logic to append text (#6212);</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Added a clear-input-content function after entering content in the input box (#6212);</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: When switching to session 2 while session 1 is generating a reply, users can ask questions normally;</li>\n<li>Agent: Files submitted in forms can be downloaded within the chat log (#5271);</li>\n<li>Agent: In the html_rander tag of the Advanced Agent opening statement, the sendMessage method supports passing through the interface and user input parameters;</li>\n<li>Agent: The action menu of the tool node in the Advanced Agent adds a display of the tool source information;</li>\n<li>Agent (X-Pack): added a session sharing permission control configuration feature to Display Settings.</li>\n<li>Agent (X-Pack): when an application is connected to a third party, entering \"/new\" automatically starts a new session.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: The document list supports manually adjusting column widths;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Added a creator field to the document list; newly uploaded documents record the document creator (#5240);</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: When exporting a Knowledge Base, users can choose whether to export the original files, with two options (#6137);</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: optimized the tag management pagination logic to avoid front-end loading lag caused by excessive data for a single tag;</li>\n<li>Model: the Gemini provider adds support for the Imagen image generation model (#5234);</li>\n<li>Model: the Gemini provider adds support for the VEO video generation model (#5234);</li>\n<li>Model: updated the model provider dropdown list to the latest models;</li>\n<li>Permission management: users who only have permission to view tools are not allowed to open the tool's edit page;</li>\n<li>Workspace (X-Pack): Optimized lazy loading performance of the workspace list.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where the node execution progress display was not controlled by the \"Execution Details\" display toggle;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Node execution progress is not displayed when the AI response is paused, and the progress is shown again after clicking Continue;</li>\n<li>Agent (X-Pack): fixed the issue where PDF files in the knowledge source could not be previewed when chatting in third-party applications (#6202).</li>\n<li>Tool: The name input box lacks a required marker when creating a new MCP tool;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where, after upgrading from v2.3.1 to v2.10.1, downloading the original document of docx type resulted in file corruption (#6238);</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where the write to knowledge base node reported an error during workflow knowledge base debugging;</li>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where adding the qwen3-tts-flash model from the Alibaba Bailian provider reported an error (#6236);</li>\n<li>Login Settings: fixed the issue where community version users could bypass the verification code to complete login (#6214).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v2101-lts\">v2.10.1-lts<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v2101-lts\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>June 10, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where the template content was displayed incorrectly when downloading the QA pair template;</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where an agent with user input parameters could not send questions during debugging.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, when a switch parameter with a default value of false was set as an external parameter, asking a question directly in a conversation while keeping the default value reported a required-field error.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where clicking the \"More Parameters\" button during debugging / conversation affected the state of external switch parameters.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the Skill execution directory could be cleared in concurrent scenarios (#6185).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the variables referenced in the system prompts of the image understanding and video understanding nodes were not parsed (#6180).</li>\n<li>Tool: Fixed the issue where using pymysql in Python scripts reported a missing dependency (#6182).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v2100-lts\">v2.10.0-lts<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v2100-lts\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>June 4, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition warning\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Security Vulnerability Fixes</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the Post-Auth RCE vulnerability in MaxKB caused by an MCP permission bypass.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">New Features <img alt=\"🌟\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f31f.png\" title=\":star2:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>System: Added a statistics feature for the workspace home page;</li>\n<li>System: Internationalization supports custom extended language packs (#5120);</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Knowledge Base supports custom terminology libraries (#5031);</li>\n<li>Agent: the agent's AI chat node supports multimodal input (#5276).</li>\n<li>Agent: User input in the Advanced Agent adds support for external parameter setting and show/hide setting.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: User input parameters are no longer displayed when creating a new session (#5298);</li>\n<li>Agent: The Q&amp;A page shows the name of the node currently executing when the AI answers (#5092);</li>\n<li>Agent: Added a show/hide setting for the parameters of the form collection node;</li>\n<li>Agent: added the \"List of Results Satisfying Direct Answer\" parameter to the output parameters of the multi-path retrieval node.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: the action buttons are pinned to the upper right corner in the document segmentation preview after uploading a document (#965);</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: the display style of segment content in the document segmentation preview after uploading a document is optimized to Markdown format;</li>\n<li>Model: the MiniMax provider adds support for text-to-image, text-to-video, and image-to-video models;</li>\n<li>Model: The Alibaba Bailian provider now supports multimodal embedding models (#5142);</li>\n<li>Model: The Alibaba Bailian provider supports the Wan2.7 image-to-video model (#5232);</li>\n<li>Model: the rerank models of all providers support model parameter settings;</li>\n<li>Role Management (X-Pack): control the creation and copy permissions of Agents with different permission bits (#5284).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where documents could not be uploaded without workflow permissions in the workflow knowledge base (#5296);</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue of abnormal mobile mode, floating widget mode, and share style when embedded in a third party (#6130).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, when a conversation generated multiple ECharts charts, all charts were overwritten by the first chart after refreshing.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, when a file was uploaded during an advanced agent conversation, the uploaded file was no longer displayed after the conversation interface was refreshed (#5253).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, after exporting historical conversation logs, the chat user only showed the Username field and not the full-name field, making user matching inconvenient.</li>\n<li>Shared Knowledge Base (X-Pack): Fixed the issue where importing to create a shared knowledge base resulted in an empty import (#5274).</li>\n<li>User Management: fixed the validation error when changing the password of a user in System Management (#5301);</li>\n<li>System Login (X-Pack): Fixed an issue where no Operation Log was generated when third-party users logged in to the system.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v292\">v2.9.2<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v292\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>May 20, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where content was displayed repeatedly in the execution details of the image understanding and video understanding nodes (#5269).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where using the doubao-seedance-2-0-260128 model to generate video took a long time and caused an error (#5260).</li>\n<li>System: Fixed an issue where an error occurred when switching the internationalization language.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v291\">v2.9.1<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v291\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>May 14, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition warning\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Security Vulnerability Fixes</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the high-risk security vulnerability where the MaxKB reset_password interface transmitted passwords in plaintext. (#CVE-2026-45413)</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the authenticated SSRF risk caused by missing validation of callback URLs in the workflow template import/update process. (#CVE-2026-45412)</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, in an agent with an infinite loop, after the number of loops exceeded the maximum limit, the reply information was cleared and a network error was displayed.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, when calling an agent with an infinite loop node via API, the interface returned no information and reported a readtime out error when stream=false.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where image generation failed after adding parameters to the Gemini image generation model (#5233).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the error in the copy description of the image understanding node, and the issue that the last-frame image of the image-to-video node should be set as optional.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where creating an agent failed when importing one from the template center (#5231).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, after unchecking an associated knowledge base in the knowledge base retrieval node, selecting another knowledge base and saving still retained the unchecked knowledge base.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, when multi-path retrieval used a rerank model, the associated agent was not shown in the model's depended-on resources list (#5249).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where holding Ctrl + clicking the agent panel did not open a new tab when entering the agent page.</li>\n<li>Tool: Fixed the issue where the startup parameters of newly created tools had to be manually saved before the default values could be used;</li>\n<li>Workspace: Fixed the issue where users not displayed could not be searched when adding members in workspaces with many users;</li>\n<li>Resource Management: Fixed an issue where resources could not be searched by creator.</li>\n<li>Shared Resources: Fixed the issue where resources could not be searched by creator.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v290\">v2.9.0<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v290\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>May 7, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition warning\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Security Vulnerability Fixes</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the vulnerability where the Webhook Trigger endpoint lacked authentication, allowing unauthenticated requests to bypass authorization and trigger arbitrary tasks.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">New Features <img alt=\"🌟\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f31f.png\" title=\":star2:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Agent: added a long-term memory feature that generates memories by conversation rounds and time periods and injects them into prompts through variable references, improving the personalization and continuity of conversations.</li>\n<li>Agent: Nodes in the Advanced Agent workflow support enable/disable, so you can debug and temporarily bypass the flow logic without deleting nodes;</li>\n<li>Agent: added the ability to view associated resources, including dependent resources and depended-on resources (#4859, #4872).</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Added the ability to view related resources, supporting bidirectional tracing of dependencies and dependents;</li>\n<li>Tool: Added related resource viewing, supporting bidirectional tracing of dependency and dependent relationships;</li>\n<li>Tool: Nodes in workflow tools support enable/disable, so you can debug and temporarily mask process logic without deleting nodes;</li>\n<li>Model: added support for integrating MiniMax large language models and text-to-speech models (#4876);</li>\n<li>Model: Alibaba Cloud Bailian now supports the MiniMax Speech voice model integration (#4950).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Agent: New support for a tree selector component in the user input and form collection nodes (#4903);</li>\n<li>Agent: the variable assignment node supports explicitly assigning a variable to empty (null) (#4964, #5107).</li>\n<li>Agent: The judge node of the Advanced Agent adds regular expression and wildcard matching modes (#4975);</li>\n<li>Agent: The Advanced Agent and workflow orchestration canvas nodes support batch copy-paste to and from each other;</li>\n<li>Agent: nodes in a loop body support batch copy and paste across loop bodies (#5128).</li>\n<li>Agent: The \"Publish\" permission of the Advanced Agent is split out from the edit permission and can be authorized independently;</li>\n<li>Agent: added hint guidance for the variable parameter format of built-in nodes.</li>\n<li>Model: the model selection box displays only the supplier icon and model name, streamlining the interface display;</li>\n<li>Model: all model providers support custom API Base URLs, adapting to private deployment scenarios;</li>\n<li>Model: automatically syncs to all associated referenced resources after model parameter changes (#5134);</li>\n<li>Tool: ZIP packages uploaded for Skills tools can be downloaded;</li>\n<li>System: Optimized the browser lag caused by too many file directories;</li>\n<li>System: Optimized the front-end lag when adding a large number of members to a role.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where subsequent nodes had no output after a loop body nested a sub-agent node (#5197).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where refreshing the page during a simple agent's streaming reply caused the Q&amp;A records to be lost (#5156).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where searching the agent list by creator was invalid (#5177).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where an agent in an unpublished state could create triggers (#5146).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the workflow tool icon in a skill tool was displayed abnormally.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where deleting the associated knowledge base configuration in the knowledge base retrieval node did not take effect (#5173).</li>\n<li>Model: fixed the abnormal parameter configuration issue of the Volcano Engine image generation model (#5089);</li>\n<li>Model: fixed the error with the Volcano Engine multimodal embedding model and supports custom model parameters;</li>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where the model Base URL was displayed in the wrong position;</li>\n<li>Model: fixed the occasional NaN error in rerank models.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v281\">v2.8.1<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v281\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>April 17, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition warning\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Security Vulnerability Fixes</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the permission bypass and SSRF security issues in the OSS file service URL retrieval interface, and strengthened application permission validation, DNS resolution validation, and URL parsing consistency to prevent unauthorized access and internal network request forgery.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where setting the ending frame caused an error when using the wan model from the Alibaba Cloud Bailian provider for image-to-video (#5111);</li>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where the image quantity setting in the parameter configuration of the Volcano Engine image generation model did not take effect (#5089);</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where adjusting the document order after document segment migration would result in a wrong document order (#5106);</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where, during intelligent segmentation, the segmentation rules did not exclude # comments in code blocks, causing abnormal segmentation;</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, after enabling the thinking process on the AI Chat node and configuring an agent in a skill, calling the model skill in a conversation reported an error.</li>\n<li>API Documentation: fixed the issue of the missing sync_type parameter in the Web knowledge base synchronization interface documentation;</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v280\">v2.8.0<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v280\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>April 10, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition warning\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Security Vulnerability Fixes</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the SSRF vulnerability that bypassed the sandbox connect() hook via socket.sendto()+MSG_FASTOPEN, preventing access to internal restricted services (#CVE-2026-39418).</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the remote code execution vulnerability that achieved sandbox escape by clearing environment variables via env -i LD_PRELOAD (#CVE-2026-39420).</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the sandbox bypass vulnerability that bypassed sandbox result verification via sys.exit(0) to spoof results (#CVE-2026-39419).</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the critical remote code execution vulnerability that achieved sandbox escape via ctypes and the unhooked SYS_pkey_mprotect (#CVE-2026-39421).</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the remote code execution vulnerability where missing validation of MCP server configuration allowed Shell commands to be injected through malicious configuration (#CVE-2026-39417).</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the general stored cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability and strengthened user input security validation in all scenarios (#CVE-2026-39422).</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the stored cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability in iframe_render caused by unfiltered user input (#CVE-2026-39426).</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the stored cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability in Markdown rendering caused by html_rander not filtering HTML tags (#CVE-2026-39425).</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the stored cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerability where the echarts_rander component injected malicious code via Eval (#CVE-2026-39423).</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the CSV injection vulnerability caused by unescaped special characters when exporting app chat to CSV (a CVE-2025-4546 variant) (#CVE-2026-39424).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">New Features <img alt=\"🌟\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f31f.png\" title=\":star2:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tool: Added workflow-type tools;</li>\n<li>Tool: Supports automatic Python code generation;</li>\n<li>Tool: Supports batch selection, then moving items to other folders or performing batch deletion;</li>\n<li>Model: The Baidu Qianfan provider now supports the Rerank Model (#4927);</li>\n<li>System: Unified the fields that display usernames to instead display users' names;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Supports importing and exporting all metadata of a Knowledge Base;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Supports batch selection, after which items can be moved to other folders or batch deleted;</li>\n<li>Agent: supports selecting a model and a knowledge base during conversation.</li>\n<li>Agent: supports batch selection, then moving the items to other folders or performing batch deletion.</li>\n<li>Agent: The \"Image Understanding\" and \"Video Understanding\" nodes in the Advanced Agent add a thinking process switch setting;</li>\n<li>Agent: The \"Variable Aggregation\" node in the Advanced Agent supports aggregating into a dict type variable (#4904);</li>\n<li>Agent: optimized the split expression component of the \"Variable Split\" node in the advanced agent (#4961).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where there was no error message when using the Alibaba Bailian rerank model when Tokens were exceeded or the balance was insufficient (#4928);</li>\n<li>Model (X-Pack): fixed the issue where clicking a shared model as a Regular User reported a no-permission error;</li>\n<li>Role (X-Pack): fixed the issue where other permissions were automatically selected when granting the \"About\" permission to a custom Regular User (#4954);</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where user questions reported an error when the vLLM model, a system prompt, and a skill MCP tool were configured in the AI Chat node.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the vLLM model was incompatible with the thinking process field (reasoning).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where retrieval results were incorrect when using the document label retrieval node (#4942).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the collapsed state of loop nodes in advanced orchestration was not saved (#4996).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, in a multi-turn conversation, if the image understanding node did not receive an image midway and then received one again, asking a question reported an error (#4999).</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where a blank screen appeared when rendering with ECharts (#4966).</li>\n<li>Agent (X-Pack): fixed the issue where images sent as questions in WeCom could not be opened after being downloaded from the MaxKB conversation log.</li>\n<li>Agent (X-Pack): fixed the issue where authentication was not performed during conversation after a sub-application in an advanced agent enabled authentication.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where the description \"Allow preview in knowledge source\" in the Web site knowledge base was inaccurate;</li>\n<li>Resource Management (X-Pack): Fixed an issue where user roles were not displayed when authorizing resources in Resource Management.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v271\">v2.7.1<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v271\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>March 20, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where using the Ollama provider's Embedding model reported an error;</li>\n<li>Installation &amp; Deployment: Fixed the issue where dependency package versions were incompatible with some older machines, causing errors during upgrades.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the tool call data in the execution details had no display style.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v270\">v2.7.0<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v270\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>March 19, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">New Features <img alt=\"🌟\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f31f.png\" title=\":star2:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tool: Added Skills management capabilities;</li>\n<li>Agent: supports autonomously calling Skills.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Optimized the Tag Management feature;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Conversation records support sharing;</li>\n<li>Login Authentication (X-Pack): supports configuring the login method.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model: added support for the Gemini provider's image generation model;</li>\n<li>Model: added support for the SiliconFlow provider's vision model;</li>\n<li>Agent: added a search/locate node feature to the workflow orchestration page of an advanced agent.</li>\n<li>Agent: added model search support to the model selection dropdown.</li>\n<li>Agent: in the dialog for selecting knowledge bases, tools, and agents, hovering the mouse over a resource displays more information about the resource.</li>\n<li>Agent: in the condition node of an advanced agent, the condition supports the \"not equal to\" option.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Added a \"Tag\" column to the document list, and supports adding tags to documents in the tag column;</li>\n<li>Trigger: scheduled triggers now support configuration via Cron expressions;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Optimized the UI style of tool calls.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where adding the Volcano Engine image generation model reported an error;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where documents were not exported in segment order when exporting;</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, when embedded in a third party and full-screen embedding was selected, the popup was not fully displayed when the user gave a Like/Dislike on the AI reply.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the AI node was not fully executed but was shown as completed in the execution details.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where conversations could still be conducted when the same application was called via API Keys from different applications.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the question optimization node did not work.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where, after moving a file in a simple agent, the AI model and the associated knowledge base in the settings were cleared.</li>\n<li>Agent (X-Pack): fixed the issue where output content was not formatted with Markdown when chatting in the Feishu client.</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where the style was displayed incorrectly when there was form-collected content during a conversation;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where the conversation content was not internationalized when users gave a thumbs-up/thumbs-down feedback after the AI reply content;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page (X-Pack): Fixed an issue where chat users created by third parties could not change their password after logging into the application using account login.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v261\">v2.6.1<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v261\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>February 10, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where executing a tool reported an error in some cases in the agent's workflow.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the history of the AI Chat node was retrieved incorrectly when parallel nodes existed in the agent's workflow.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the frontend reported an error when the AI replied after a question, because the data stream returned by the backend was too large.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where, after selecting intelligent segmentation when uploading a document, the segmentation identifiers using blank lines and carriage returns did not take effect.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v260\">v2.6.0<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v260\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>February 5, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">New Features <img alt=\"🌟\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f31f.png\" title=\":star2:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tool: Added trigger capabilities;</li>\n<li>Agent: added trigger capability.</li>\n<li>Agent: added the \"IP Address\" and \"Source\" attributes to the conversation log list.</li>\n<li>Agent: the conversation log supports separately setting the cleanup policy for uploaded files.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Supports conversion to Workflow Knowledge Base;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Added support for batch export of documents in the document list;</li>\n<li>Trigger: Workspace Administrators now support the trigger management feature;</li>\n<li>Agent (X-Pack): the agent's API Key supports setting a validity period.</li>\n<li>Shared Tools (X-Pack): Added the feature to view the execution records of tools.</li>\n<li>System API Key (X-Pack): supports setting a validity period.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>System: Optimized internationalization copy and parts of the UI;</li>\n<li>Model: The video models and speech recognition models of Alibaba Cloud Bailian support the input of the \"API URL\" parameter;</li>\n<li>Model: The Volcano Engine provider's Embedding Model supports connecting multimodal Embedding Models;</li>\n<li>Model: The Volcano Engine provider's speech recognition model supports the recording-file speech recognition connection method;</li>\n<li>Model: the model parameters of the OpenAI provider's image generation model support setting a \"Return Type\" parameter such as response_format=b64_json;</li>\n<li>Agent: the \"Go to Chat\" button has been moved to the agent panel.</li>\n<li>Agent: The default value for the date type parameter of user input now includes a \"Now\" setting, so that the parameter dynamically fetches the current time in the Q&amp;A page.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where the slm Chinese-English speech recognition model of iFlytek Spark could not convert speech into text;</li>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where editing the iFlytek Spark IAT model reported an error;</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the \"Citation Segment Count\" and \"Segment Title + Content\" fields were missing when exporting conversation logs.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the tool invocation process was not displayed when the AI model called a tool in a skill and the tool had no input parameters.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the AI reply content was garbled when the sub-application in a loop body also had loop nodes.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the AI reply content did not automatically scroll to the bottom during agent debugging.</li>\n<li>Folders: Fixed the issue where users with only folder view permission could still create subfolders;</li>\n<li>Login Authentication (X-Pack): fixed the issue where the login failure count for displaying the verification code could not be set to 0.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v250\">v2.5.0<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v250\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>January 8, 2026</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">New Features <img alt=\"🌟\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f31f.png\" title=\":star2:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tool: Added JSON text box and slider components to the component types in the Add Parameter dialog;</li>\n<li>Resources: Added a 'View Associated Resources' feature for knowledge base, tool, and model resources.</li>\n<li>Agent: the \"Application\" module has been upgraded to the \"Agent\" module.</li>\n<li>Agent: All AI capability nodes in the Advanced Agent add exception branch output;</li>\n<li>Agent: the conversation log details support displaying the feedback information filled in by the user.</li>\n<li>Agent: the user input parameter components in the basic information node support multi-line text box, single-line single-choice, and single-line multi-choice components.</li>\n<li>Agent: Input parameters in the custom tool node support the boolean type;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Added import/export workflow functionality for Workflow Knowledge Bases;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: The document import process for Workflow Knowledge Bases now supports cancellation;</li>\n<li>Folders: Supports sorting by name, creation time, and custom drag order;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Users can fill in feedback information when submitting feedback;</li>\n<li>Template Center: Provides agent and knowledge base workflow templates, covering typical application scenarios;</li>\n<li>User Management: supports default resource permission settings when creating a user;</li>\n<li>User Management (X-Pack): supports adding roles in batch and deleting users in batch;</li>\n<li>System Settings: Login settings support default role assignment for third-party users and a login-failure lockout mechanism (X-Pack).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>System: Optimized the system UI;</li>\n<li>Agent: The Start Node in the Advanced Agent adds the chat user group {{global.chat_user_group}};</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: optimized the hit testing API to a POST request;</li>\n<li>Folders: Folders support authorization by user role;</li>\n<li>API Key: system API Keys have been optimized to be isolated per user;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Removed the limit of viewing only 20 chat history records;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: The last question can be edited and re-asked;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page (X-Pack): Third-party chat users can all log out after logging into the Q&amp;A page.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tool: Fixed the issue where emails sent via the SMTP protocol were mistakenly blocked;</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where the scrollbar of the tool dropdown in the MCP node could not scroll.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the style issue where the execution details of the MCP call and the tool node went off the screen.</li>\n<li>Agent: fixed the issue where a sub-agent could not receive video files from the parent agent.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the style issue where the video component in the segment details would exceed the segment details area;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where all videos would automatically play when opening the segment details page;</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the issue where uploading files could cause XSS vulnerabilities.</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the issue where Python code in the Tool module could load dynamic link libraries to bypass security restrictions.</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the RCE issue that could be caused by pickle deserializing untrusted objects in Celery.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v242\">v2.4.2<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v242\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>December 18, 2025</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Fixed an issue where clicking [Go to Chat] on the workflow orchestration page jumped to an incorrect path when the system's secondary path had been modified.</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where referenced variables could not be deselected in the tool node of advanced orchestration applications;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where the workflow was not interrupted after a node error in the loop body;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed an issue where the node order in the Add Component dialog was inconsistent with the node order in the loop body.</li>\n<li>Application (X-Pack): Fixed the issue where the login page was redirected when chat users logged in by scanning a WeCom QR code;</li>\n<li>Tool: Fixed the issue where data source tools lacked the parameters set during debugging;</li>\n<li>Tool: Fixed the issue where IPv6-mapped IPv4 addresses were not blocked;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where, when returning from the segment details page to the document list page, the previous page was not remembered;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where, in the designated reply node of the workflow knowledge base, inputting a global variable caused parsing to fail;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Removed the conversation history feature from image understanding, video understanding, and AI chat nodes in Workflow Knowledge Bases;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where, when creating a new embedding model in the knowledge base creation interface, the newly created embedding model was not displayed in the embedding model list;</li>\n<li>Resource list: Fixed an issue where the resource list displayed incorrectly after moving a resource into a folder under the root directory of applications/knowledge bases/tools.</li>\n<li>API Documentation: fixed the issue of incorrect parameter types in the document segmentation API.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v241\">v2.4.1<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v241\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>December 12, 2025</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Fixed an issue where the \"Submit\" button could not be clicked when the Form Collection node was executed.</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where retrieval results were incorrect when the tag value was None in the document tag retrieval node;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where the Input parameter was not fully output when AI models called MCP;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Fixed an issue where image understanding in Knowledge Base workflows failed to execute;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where files containing images uploaded in zip format could not be written into the knowledge base;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the case-sensitivity issue of the custom file format input in the local file of the data source node;</li>\n<li>Tool: Fixed the issue where the tool editor reported console errors in some cases;</li>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where adding a local rerank model caused a cache_dir error.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v240\">v2.4.0<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v240\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>December 11, 2025</p>\n<div class=\"admonition warning\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Security Vulnerability Fixes</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the permission bypass issue caused by overwritten system files (<a href=\"https://github.com/1Panel-dev/MaxKB/security/advisories/GHSA-5xx2-3q9w-jpgf\">CVE-2025-66446</a>).</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the permission bypass issue that occurred under specific concurrency conditions (<a href=\"https://github.com/1Panel-dev/MaxKB/security/advisories/GHSA-f9qm-2pxq-fx6c\">CVE-2025-66419</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We would like to thank GitHub users (<a href=\"https://github.com/yck99\">@yck99</a>), (<a href=\"http://github.com/NikoCat233\">@NikoCat233</a>) (<a href=\"https://github.com/Threonine\">@Threonine</a>) for discovering and promptly reporting the above vulnerabilities to the MaxKB open-source community.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">New Features <img alt=\"🌟\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f31f.png\" title=\":star2:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tool: Added support for data source tools;</li>\n<li>Model: added support for the Docker AI model provider;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Added support for Workflow Knowledge Bases;</li>\n<li>Login Authentication (X-Pack): supports SAML2 single sign-on.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Added a \"URL address\" method to the upload methods in the File Upload Settings feature.</li>\n<li>Application: Added ranking statistics for \"User Tokens Consumed\" and \"User Question Count\" to the monitoring statistics on the Overview page.</li>\n<li>Application: The generated prompt of the AI Chat node in Advanced apps no longer carries the application name and description.</li>\n<li>Application: Supports outputting the request parameter when AI models call MCP tools;</li>\n<li>Tool: Importing supports three types: tool, MCP, and data source;</li>\n<li>Tool: The tool store entry was moved to the tool list;</li>\n<li>Tool: Removed system built-in tools; built-in tools were moved to the tool store;</li>\n<li>Tool: Tools in the tool store are divided into two types: Tool and Data Source;</li>\n<li>Model: the AWS provider adds the vision model and rerank model;</li>\n<li>Model: the vision models of the OpenAI, Ollama, vLLM, Xinference, and Zhipu AI providers support video understanding;</li>\n<li>Resource Authorization: When authorizing applications, knowledge bases, tools, and models to users by resource, supports filtering users by role.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where the execution time of the loop node was displayed incorrectly in execution details;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where retrieval results were incorrect when the variable value was empty in the document tag retrieval node;</li>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where the qwen-image model from the Alibaba Cloud Bailian provider reported an error during generation;</li>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where adding the gpt-5-codex model from the Azure OpenAI provider reported an error;</li>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue of incorrect parameter settings for some vLLM models;</li>\n<li>Role: fixed the issue where the \"About\" permission granted to Workspace Administrator and Regular User roles did not take effect;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where, after replacing the original document, the downloaded original document could not be opened;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where the retrieval results of the knowledge base retrieval node within the loop were not displayed in the knowledge source;</li>\n<li>Chat User (X-Pack): Fixed the issue where the chat user query interface displayed unnecessary information.</li>\n<li>API Documentation (X-Pack): revised several inaccurate API documentation descriptions.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v231\">v2.3.1<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v231\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>November 13, 2025</p>\n<div class=\"admonition warning\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Security Vulnerability Fixes</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the vulnerability where Python code in tools could access local services (<a href=\"https://github.com/1Panel-dev/MaxKB/security/advisories/GHSA-9287-g7px-9rp4\">CVE-2025-64511</a>).</li>\n<li>Security Vulnerability: Fixed the vulnerability where Python code in tools could obtain system configuration information (<a href=\"https://github.com/1Panel-dev/MaxKB/security/advisories/GHSA-qwvm-x4xh-g2qq\">CVE-2025-64703</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We would like to thank Tencent Xuanwu Lab's XlabAI team (<a href=\"https://github.com/XlabAITeam\">@XlabAITeam</a>) for discovering and promptly reporting the above vulnerabilities to the MaxKB open-source community.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>System: Through code refactoring and architecture optimization, significantly reduced CPU and memory usage, comprehensively improved system resource utilization, stability, and concurrent processing capability, delivering a lighter and more efficient running experience;</li>\n<li>System: Optimized so that after a user logs in, their name is displayed in the top-right corner;</li>\n<li>Application: Users granted the \"View\" permission can now view the \"Settings\" page of an application.</li>\n<li>Folders: Folders in the application, knowledge base, and tool lists support moving and drag-and-drop moving;</li>\n<li>Folders: Folders in the application, knowledge base, and tool lists are no longer limited by level;</li>\n<li>User Management: the maximum length of the username and name is adjusted to 64 characters;</li>\n<li>Chat User (X-Pack): The maximum length for usernames and names has been adjusted to 64 characters.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where multiple form collection nodes were displayed during a chat when a form collection node existed in the loop body;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where the output directly displayed the \"context\" error message during a chat when a form collection node existed in the loop body;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where the output parameters of the loop node became \"None\" when a form collection node existed in the loop body;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed an issue where the last folder was not displayed when adding a tool node.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where document vectorization occasionally failed;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where the association relationship between segments and questions was not deleted when deleting a document;</li>\n<li>Resource Authorization: Fixed an issue where the folder automatically collapsed when authorizing resources under it.</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where chat users could not use WeCom scan login when using the Safari browser.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v230\">v2.3.0<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v230\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>November 3, 2025</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">New Features <img alt=\"🌟\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f31f.png\" title=\":star2:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Added the \"Document Tag Retrieval\" node to Advanced Orchestration apps.</li>\n<li>Application: Added the \"Video Understanding\" node to Advanced Orchestration apps.</li>\n<li>Application: Added the \"Variable Split\" node to Advanced Orchestration apps.</li>\n<li>Application: Added the \"Variable Aggregation\" node to Advanced Orchestration apps.</li>\n<li>Application: Added the \"Parameter Extraction\" node to Advanced Orchestration apps.</li>\n<li>Application: Added a \"Video\" file type option to File Upload Settings.</li>\n<li>Application: Added \"startwith\" and \"endwith\" conditions to the Judger node.</li>\n<li>Application: Added the Conversation History {history} parameter to the output parameters of the AI Chat node;</li>\n<li>Application: The retrieval scope of the Knowledge Base Retrieval node now supports two methods: manually selecting a knowledge base or referencing a variable.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Added the \"Tag Management\" feature;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Documents in the Knowledge Base added the \"Tag Settings\" feature;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: General Knowledge Base added the \"Replace Original Document\" feature;</li>\n<li>Resource Authorization: Supports authorizing folder resources by user.</li>\n<li>Resource Authorization: Supports folder-level resource authorization for applications, knowledge bases, and tools in a workspace.</li>\n<li>System Management (X-Pack): Operation Log now supports clearing policies, helping administrators manage log data efficiently.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Uploaded files support video file types;</li>\n<li>Application: The file selection parameter of the Image Understanding, Image-to-Video, and Video Understanding nodes now supports setting a URL address.</li>\n<li>Application: The Variable Assignment node can now be used as an End node.</li>\n<li>Application: The workflow orchestration page now supports batch node selection.</li>\n<li>Application: Added a description field to API parameters.</li>\n<li>Application: Adjusted the maximum value of the \"Per-client question limit\" option in \"Access Limits\" to 10 million times/day.</li>\n<li>Application: The multi-select component in the Form Collection node now supports custom input.</li>\n<li>Application: The root directory now displays all applications in the current workspace and supports global search.</li>\n<li>Application (X-Pack): After integrating with WeCom, Feishu, or DingTalk, apps support password-free login for users;</li>\n<li>Tool: The root directory displays all tools in the current workspace, with global search support;</li>\n<li>Tool: Custom-type parameters support variable resolution;</li>\n<li>Role: adjusted the \"About\" permission to the Regular User role;</li>\n<li>Model: embedding models support setting model parameters;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: The root directory displays all Knowledge Bases under the current workspace and supports global search.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where tool nodes in the loop body were not exported during application export;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where nodes after the form collection node in the loop body could not output loop variables;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where modifying the second parameter in the MCP Call node cleared the first parameter;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where Tokens displayed as 0 during a chat when the Zhipu large language model was used with the tool feature enabled in the AI Chat node;</li>\n<li>Application (X-Pack): Fixed the issue where the history setting option in Display Settings did not take effect;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where the uploaded file was lost when clicking \"Get Another Answer\" after asking a question by uploading a file on the Q&amp;A page;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where adjusting the conversation window size while asking a question on the Q&amp;A page caused conversation records to be lost.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v221\">v2.2.1<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v221\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>October 11, 2025</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tool: Added a parameter hint description field to input parameters;</li>\n<li>Tool: Clicking the panel of a tool added from the tool store opens the tool details;</li>\n<li>Model: The Alibaba Cloud Bailian provider's vision model supports qwen-vl-ocr.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Fixed an issue where dragging the MCP Call node displayed abnormally when adding a component.</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where different branches of a conditional node could not connect to the same subsequent node;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed an issue where adding multiple loop nodes could occasionally result in redundant standalone loop bodies.</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where the icon of the preceding node was displayed incorrectly in the Select Variable dropdown;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where the conditional node reported an error when checking whether a variable was empty;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed an issue where copying the Knowledge Base Retrieval node after selecting a knowledge base caused missing parameters.</li>\n<li>Tool: Fixed the issue where tools in the tool store did not display descriptions;</li>\n<li>Tool: Fixed the issue where repeatedly clicking the Create button when creating a tool created multiple tools;</li>\n<li>System: Fixed an issue where the prompt message for a verification code error was not correctly internationalized;</li>\n<li>System: Fixed an issue where built-in roles did not take effect after switching the language to English.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v220\">v2.2.0<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v220\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>September 30, 2025</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">New Features <img alt=\"🌟\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f31f.png\" title=\":star2:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tool: Added the tool store;</li>\n<li>Workflow: Added a loop node;</li>\n<li>Workflow: Added an intent recognition node;</li>\n<li>Workflow: Added text-to-video and image-to-video nodes;</li>\n<li>Application: Added support for MCP and tool calls to Simple Applications.</li>\n<li>Application: Added support for prompt generation to Simple Applications.</li>\n<li>Application: Added an \"Output MCP/Tool execution process\" toggle setting to applications.</li>\n<li>Application: Added bool as a supported data type when assigning values in the Variable Assignment node.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Supports parameter configuration for the model that handles the question generation task;</li>\n<li>Model: The Alibaba Cloud Bailian provider now supports text-to-video and image-to-video models;</li>\n<li>Model: The Volcano Engine provider now supports text-to-video and image-to-video models;</li>\n<li>Model: Speech recognition models support model parameter settings;</li>\n<li>Login: upgraded the login verification code to an authentication mechanism with user isolation.</li>\n<li>Login Authentication: added the default login method setting (X-Pack);</li>\n<li>Chat User: Added a setting to enable verification code validation after a specified number of failed login attempts (X-Pack).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Optimized the display style of Add Component for advanced orchestration applications;</li>\n<li>Application: Optimized the descriptions of the system prompt and user prompt;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: The question list supports the \"Show 1,000 items\" option setting;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Added the \"Back to Bottom\" quick action;</li>\n<li>Resource Management: The resource list filter now supports filtering by type (X-Pack).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where the parameter settings of the SiliconFlow provider's speech synthesis model did not take effect;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where the reasoning process was not returned when chatting via the application API;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed an issue where the display order of login methods in Access Limits was not sorted by category.</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed an issue where the \"Per-client question count limit\" option in Access Limits did not take effect.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Fixed an issue where exporting a Knowledge Base would time out when the Knowledge Base contains a large amount of data;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where the send button was not displayed in some iOS browsers;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where refreshing the browser on the Q&amp;A page opened the application list page after the application configured the question API parameter;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where the font style of the thinking process was incorrect.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v212\">v2.1.2<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v212\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>September 23, 2025</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Fixed an error when executing a newly created \"MCP Call\" node.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Fixed an issue where the \"Maximum files per upload\" setting in Knowledge Base settings did not take effect.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v211\">v2.1.1<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v211\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>September 11, 2025</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: The MCP settings of the AI Chat node support selecting multiple MCP tools.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tool: Fixed the vulnerability that allowed tools to execute arbitrary system commands;</li>\n<li>Tool: Fixed the abnormal style display on the MCP editing page;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where multiple session variables could not be added in the basic information node;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where the timezone of the global variable Current Time was incorrect;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where pressing Enter in the User Input Title settings dialog opened a new web page;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where exporting a knowledge base did not export the image content in the knowledge base;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where the file name of the exported knowledge base was not the knowledge base name;</li>\n<li>Role Management (X-Pack): fixed the issue where the internationalized display of the Role Management feature was incorrect.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v210\">v2.1.0<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v210\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>September 4, 2025</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">New Features <img alt=\"🌟\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f31f.png\" title=\":star2:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tool: Added MCP tool management;</li>\n<li>Application: Added tool settings to the AI Chat node; after users select custom tools, the model can decide on its own whether to call the configured tools;</li>\n<li>Application: The parameters of the Form Collection node now support referencing variables.</li>\n<li>Application: Added multi-line text box, file upload, and single-line multi-select components to the Form Collection node.</li>\n<li>Application (X-Pack): App integration supports connecting WeCom intelligent robots, enabling users to efficiently link AI capabilities with the WeCom office ecosystem;</li>\n<li>Application (X-Pack): Added a Show Conversation History setting option in Display Settings;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Supports exporting the current conversation records to PDF and PNG image formats;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Added the \"Allow download in knowledge sources\" setting option for documents in General Knowledge Base and Feishu Knowledge Base;</li>\n<li>Resource Authorization: Added a resource-dimension authorization feature that supports authorizing core resources such as applications, knowledge bases, tools, and models to specified users.</li>\n<li>Resource Authorization: When authorizing resources by user in System Management, supports setting different permissions for each resource.</li>\n<li>Model: the vLLM provider adds support for rerank models and speech recognition models;</li>\n<li>Model: The Tencent Hunyuan provider now supports speech recognition models;</li>\n<li>Model: The iFlytek Spark provider's speech recognition model now supports the Chinese speech large model;</li>\n<li>Model: The Alibaba Cloud Bailian provider's speech recognition model now supports qwen-omni-turbo, qwen2.5-omni-7b, and ASR models;</li>\n<li>Model: The Baidu Qianfan large model provider now supports the connection method with API version V2.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Added the ability to query the Chat Log list by user.</li>\n<li>Application (X-Pack): After integrating with Feishu, AI replies are presented in Markdown format;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: A new conversation is automatically created by default when entering the Q&amp;A page;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Optimized the issue where a default question was not automatically generated when uploading a file or an image;</li>\n<li>Tool: Added a confirmation prompt when clicking the Close or Cancel button while creating or editing a tool;</li>\n<li>Login: after a user logs in with the default password, the password must be changed before continuing to use it.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Fixed an issue where the MCP node in Advanced Orchestration apps was not internationalized.</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed an issue where session variable values could not be read when using session variables after the Form Collection node.</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page (X-Pack): Fixed an issue where the custom application Logo was not displayed in the browser tab;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page (X-Pack): Fixed an issue where the existing authentication information still took effect when switching the application's authentication method in the \"Access Restriction\" feature;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where the content display style was disordered when clicking the \"Collapse\" button in the left navigation area;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where a missing-parameter message was prompted when chat users asked a question after re-logging in;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where the conversation record area did not display records when viewing history data;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where uploading an empty file caused an extraction exception;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where the label was displayed abnormally when the content of quick questions was too long;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Fixed an issue where input fields on the Hit Testing interface displayed incompletely when the system had no License authorization;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where clicking the \"Back\" button had no secondary confirmation when uploading a document to the knowledge base;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where the query results were incorrect when searching by segment content in the knowledge base segment details;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where the same segment could be associated with the same question multiple times;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Fixed an issue where the \"Number of Related Segments\" count in the question list was incorrect;</li>\n<li>Model: fixed the issue where models in the \"All Models\" list were not displayed in descending order of creation time;</li>\n<li>Resource Authorization: Fixed an issue where users with only knowledge base view permission could add segments to chat logs.</li>\n<li>Folders: Fixed the issue where clicking the Back button in the resource details of applications and knowledge bases always returned to the root directory;</li>\n<li>Chat User (X-Pack): Fixed the issue where user passwords were not synced when synchronizing system users.</li>\n<li>Chat User (X-Pack): Fixed the issue where a new chat user could be created successfully even without setting a user group.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v202\">v2.0.2<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v202\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>August 7, 2025</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">New Features <img alt=\"🌟\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f31f.png\" title=\":star2:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Added the session variable feature to Advanced Orchestration apps.</li>\n<li>Chat User (X-Pack): Support QR code login for chat users.</li>\n<li>Chat User (X-Pack): Support syncing LDAP and WeCom users.</li>\n<li>Resource Management (X-Pack): Supports unified management of workspace-related resources.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Feature Optimizations <img alt=\"🌻\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f33b.png\" title=\":sunflower:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Chat User (X-Pack): Support querying by user source and status.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Improved Knowledge Base retrieval performance for complex scenarios with large amounts of data;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: Chat users now support filtering by user source;</li>\n<li>Application: Adjusted the file upload limits for Advanced Orchestration apps: up to 100 files can be uploaded per conversation, and a single file can be up to 1000 MB.</li>\n<li>Application: Added support for querying by application publish status.</li>\n<li>Application: Chat Users now supports querying by user source.</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Automatically fills in the question field after uploading a file;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Optimized the login interaction experience in floating-window mode and mobile mode;</li>\n<li>User Management: supports querying by user source and status;</li>\n<li>System: Optimized the system UI styles.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where hit testing reported an error in full-text search mode;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where some content on the offline document upload page was displayed incorrectly in internationalization;</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base: fixed the issue where the scroll range of the scrollbar on the segmentation rules page for uploading offline documents was incorrect;</li>\n<li>Application (X-Pack): Fixed the issue where AI replies were not displayed in Markdown style during conversations on the DingTalk platform where the app was integrated;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed an error when executing the MCP Call node in some cases.</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed an issue where connecting two identical nodes multiple times caused duplicate execution.</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where parameters were displayed incorrectly after modifying model parameters;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed an issue where applications in the unpublished state were not filtered when adding an application sub-node.</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where the URL was not displayed when the uploaded file name contained the \"&amp;nbsp\" character;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where images in AI replies could not be clicked to enlarge during user conversations;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where AI replies were misaligned when displayed as table data;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page (X-Pack): Fixed an issue where an error occurred when opening the Q&amp;A page when the License was not authorized;</li>\n<li>Shared Models (X-Pack): Fixed the error that occurred when deleting a shared model.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v201\">v2.0.1<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v201\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>July 18, 2025</p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Question Fix <img alt=\"🌴\" class=\"emojione\" src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/emojione/2.2.7/assets/png/1f334.png\" title=\":palm_tree:\"/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where, when only Show Knowledge Sources was enabled without execution details in Display Settings, the cited segments of knowledge sources were displayed incorrectly during a chat;</li>\n<li>Application: Fixed the issue where the Multi-path Recall node reported an error during a chat when the reranked content was empty;</li>\n<li>Tool: Fixed the issue where the Create Tool interface lacked the Debug feature for users with the Regular User role after logging in;</li>\n<li>Q&amp;A Page: Fixed an issue where audio files in AI replies could not be played by dragging;</li>\n<li>User Management: fixed the issue where an error was reported when editing a user;</li>\n<li>Shared Tools: Fixed the issue where adding tools from the Tool Store failed. (X-Pack)</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"v200\">v2.0.0<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#v200\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p>July 17, 2025</p>\n<table>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"middle\" bgcolor=\"#4B60FC\" style=\"font-weight:bold;color: white;width: 150px\">Module</td>\n<td align=\"middle\" bgcolor=\"#4B60FC\" style=\"font-weight:bold;color: white;width: 150px\">Feature Item</td>\n<td align=\"middle\" bgcolor=\"#4B60FC\" style=\"font-weight:bold;color: white;width: 750px\">Feature Description</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"21\">Application</td>\n<td rowspan=\"4\">Application Management</td>\n<td>Supports creating simple applications and advanced orchestration applications</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports classifying and managing applications with multi-level directories</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports controlling application access behavior, such as allowing public access or disabling public access</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports importing and exporting applications</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"10\">Advanced Orchestration</td>\n<td>Supports creating simple applications and advanced orchestration applications</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Workflow orchestration applications support nodes such as AI chat, knowledge base retrieval, question optimization, judgment, specified reply, document content summarization, text-to-speech, speech-to-text, image understanding, image generation, form collection, and MCP.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports uploading files such as text, images, and audio when asking questions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports referencing tools within a workflow</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports nesting other applications within a workflow</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports multiple outputs, multiple inputs, and parallel execution</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports global variables</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports auto-save and restoring historical versions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports auto-send and auto-play for voice input</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports customizing the label of the thinking process and configuring whether to output the thinking process</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"1\">Q&amp;A Embedding</td>\n<td>Supports embedding Q&amp;A in third-party applications</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Access Restrictions</td>\n<td>Supports limiting the number of daily questions by client</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports embedding a third-party access whitelist setting</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Display Settings</td>\n<td>Supports displaying knowledge sources when asking questions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports the language setting of the Q&amp;A page in Settings</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Statistics Dashboard</td>\n<td>Supports statistics by time of user count, question count, total Tokens, and user satisfaction</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports trend statistics for user count, question count, total Tokens, and user satisfaction metrics</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"12\">Knowledge Base</td>\n<td rowspan=\"1\">Knowledge Base Management</td>\n<td>Supports general-purpose file knowledge bases and Web site document knowledge bases</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"6\">Document Management</td>\n<td>Supports uploading text file documents, including Markdown, TXT, DOCX, PDF, HTML, XLSX, XLS, and CSV formats</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports uploading QA pairs and provides QA pair templates</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports uploading and exporting text files and offline image ZIP archives</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports adjusting the enabled status of knowledge base documents, enabling or disabling documents</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports the command processing modes for knowledge base documents, such as model optimization and direct answering</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports exporting documents from a knowledge base</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"3\">Document Segmentation</td>\n<td>Supports intelligent document segmentation and advanced segmentation methods</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports custom regex segmentation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports migrating knowledge base document segments</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Question Management</td>\n<td>Supports associating questions with document segments</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports automatically generating associated questions for a knowledge base</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"4\">Tool</td>\n<td rowspan=\"4\">Tool Management</td>\n<td>Supports customizing tools through Python functions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports importing and creating from the Tool Store</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports multi-level directory classification management for tools</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports exporting and importing tools</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"4\">Model</td>\n<td rowspan=\"4\">Model Provider Integration</td>\n<td>Supports integration with mainstream large models, including local private large models (Llama 3 / Qwen 2, etc.), domestic public large models (Tongyi Qianwen / Zhipu AI / Baidu Qianfan / Kimi / DeepSeek, etc.), and foreign public large models (OpenAI / Azure OpenAI / Gemini, etc.)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports large language models, embedding models, rerank models, speech recognition, speech synthesis, image understanding, and image generation models</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports custom model parameter settings</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports model permissions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"20\">System Management</td>\n<td rowspan=\"1\">System Language</td>\n<td>Supports three languages: Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese, and English</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"3\">User Management</td>\n<td>Supports user creation/deletion, enable/disable, and password modification</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports LDAP, CAS, OIDC, and OAuth2 integration (X-Pack)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports QR-code login via WeCom, DingTalk, and Feishu (X-Pack)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"1\">Workspace</td>\n<td>Supports independent management of users and resources by workspace (X-Pack)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"2\">Role Management</td>\n<td>Supports the built-in roles of system administrator, workspace administrator, and regular user</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports customizing roles and associating permission controls and user members (X-Pack)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"1\">Resource Management</td>\n<td>Supports viewing all system resources such as applications, knowledge bases, tools, and models (X-Pack)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"1\">Resource Authorization</td>\n<td>Supports authorization of all system resources such as applications, knowledge bases, tools, and models by role or custom authorization</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"1\">Shared Resources</td>\n<td>Supports creating and managing shared resources such as knowledge bases, tools, and models (X-Pack)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"3\">Chat User</td>\n<td>Supports creating and syncing chat users (X-Pack)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports creating chat user groups and managing members (X-Pack)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports login authentication for chat users via LDAP, CAS, OIDC, OAuth2, and other methods (X-Pack)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"3\">System Settings</td>\n<td>Supports email integration</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports customizing the system Logo, login Logo, theme colors, login background image, system name, welcome message, and system help link (X-Pack)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Supports login authentication via LDAP, CAS, OIDC, OAuth2, QR-code login, and other methods (X-Pack)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td rowspan=\"1\">Operation Log</td>\n<td>Supports viewing the operation details of all users (X-Pack)</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n</article>"}, {"location": "changelog.html#1", "title": "1 Release Notes ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#2", "title": "2 Update Content ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v2105-lts", "title": "v2.10.5-lts ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v2104-lts", "title": "v2.10.4-lts ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v2103-lts", "title": "v2.10.3-lts ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v2102-lts", "title": "v2.10.2-lts ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v2101-lts", "title": "v2.10.1-lts ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v2100-lts", "title": "v2.10.0-lts ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v292", "title": "v2.9.2 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v291", "title": "v2.9.1 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v290", "title": "v2.9.0 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v281", "title": "v2.8.1 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v280", "title": "v2.8.0 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v271", "title": "v2.7.1 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v270", "title": "v2.7.0 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v261", "title": "v2.6.1 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v260", "title": "v2.6.0 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v250", "title": "v2.5.0 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v242", "title": "v2.4.2 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v241", "title": "v2.4.1 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v240", "title": "v2.4.0 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v231", "title": "v2.3.1 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v230", "title": "v2.3.0 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v221", "title": "v2.2.1 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v220", "title": "v2.2.0 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v212", "title": "v2.1.2 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v211", "title": "v2.1.1 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v210", "title": "v2.1.0 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v202", "title": "v2.0.2 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v201", "title": "v2.0.1 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "changelog.html#v200", "title": "v2.0.0 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "contact.html", "title": "Contact Us", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Contact Us</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Project Address<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/1Panel-dev/MaxKB/issues\">MaxKB</a> <img alt=\"MaxKB stars\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/github/stars/1Panel-dev/MaxKB\"/></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Community Forum<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>You can search for, ask about, and discuss issues related to the MaxKB agent platform in <a href=\"https://bbs.fit2cloud.com/c/mk/11\">FIT2CLOUD Open-Source Community Forum MaxKB Section</a>, and share your opinions and ideas.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Contact Information<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>Official Website: <a href=\"https://maxkb.cn\">https://maxkb.cn</a></li>\n<li>Email: <a href=\"mailto:support@fit2cloud.com\">support@fit2cloud.com</a></li>\n<li>Phone: 400-052-0755</li>\n<li>WeChat discussion group:   <br/>\n<img alt=\"WeCom\" src=\"img/index/wechat.jpg\" width=\"135px\"/></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "contact.html#1", "title": "1 Project Address ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "contact.html#2", "title": "2 Community Forum ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "contact.html#3", "title": "3 Contact Information ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "instructional_video.html", "title": "Tutorial Video", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Tutorial Video <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Course Introduction<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1xGmHYwE6m?spm_id_from=333.788.videopod.sections&amp;vd_source=2be54e435e136941c6aab6077b8fc303\"><img alt=\"Course Introduction\" src=\"./img/video/课程简介.png\" width=\"300\"/></a></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Installation &amp; Deployment<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV11gmHYaE9Y?spm_id_from=333.788.videopod.sections&amp;vd_source=2be54e435e136941c6aab6077b8fc303\"><img alt=\"Feature Demo - Installation &amp; Deployment\" src=\"./img/video/安装部署.png\" width=\"300\"/></a>\n</p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Feature Demo<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV18JypYeEkj?spm_id_from=333.788.videopod.sections\"><img alt=\"Feature Demo - Model Management\" src=\"./img/video/模型管理.png\" width=\"300\"/></a>\n<a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1SAmHYTEnM?spm_id_from=333.788.videopod.sections&amp;vd_source=2be54e435e136941c6aab6077b8fc303\"><img alt=\"Feature Demo - Knowledge Base\" src=\"./img/video/知识库.png\" width=\"300\"/></a>\n<a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1MKmHYKEbk?spm_id_from=333.788.videopod.sections&amp;vd_source=2be54e435e136941c6aab6077b8fc303\"><img alt=\"Feature Demo - Function Library\" src=\"img/video/函数库.png\" width=\"300\"/></a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Enterprise Edition<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1KziRYaEfS?spm_id_from=333.788.videopod.sections&amp;vd_source=2be54e435e136941c6aab6077b8fc303\"><img alt=\"Feature Demo - Enterprise Edition\" src=\"./img/video/企业版功能.png\" width=\"300\"/></a> </p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "instructional_video.html#1", "title": "1 Course Introduction ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "instructional_video.html#2", "title": "2 Installation & Deployment ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "instructional_video.html#3", "title": "3 Feature Demo ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "instructional_video.html#4", "title": "4 Enterprise Edition ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "quick_start.html", "title": "Quick Start", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Quick Start</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Quick Deployment<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>Supports mainstream Linux distributions (based on Debian / RedHat, including domestic operating systems)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://community.fit2cloud.com/#/products/maxkb/downloads\">Offline Installation Package</a> is recommended for production deployment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Upload the downloaded installation package to the server and unzip it, then run the following script in the installation package directory for a quick installation:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>bash install.sh\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n<p>After installation, access <code>http://目标服务器 IP 地址:8080</code> via your browser and log in to MaxKB with the default administrator username and password.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>用户名：admin\n\n\n\n默认密码：MaxKB@123..\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Interface Introduction<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After entering the MaxKB main interface, you can see the navigation bar at the top of the interface, containing five main modules: Home, Agent, Knowledge Base, Tool, and Model.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Home: Administrators can get an overview of all resources in the workspace, operational monitoring trends, and resource usage rankings, providing data support for resource governance and operational decisions.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Model: supports connecting to mainstream local, domestic, and international large models, covering text generation, speech recognition, visual recognition, and other types, to meet the needs of multiple scenarios.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Tool: Provides built-in and custom functions for data retrieval, logical judgment, information extraction, and other operations; created tools can be called in agent orchestration.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Knowledge Base: Create and manage Knowledge Bases, including uploading offline documents, web sites, Feishu documents, etc., to provide a source of knowledge for Q&amp;A chat, manage knowledge in a unified way, and empower intelligent Q&amp;A.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Agent: provides preconfigured templates and components to quickly create basic Q&amp;A agents, or perform advanced agent orchestration for complex business processes and build a dedicated AI assistant.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Navigation Bar\" src=\"img/index/page_introduction.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Quick Start<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>With MaxKB, you can have a dedicated AI assistant in three steps: connect a large language model, build a knowledge base, and create an agent. It also supports quick embedding into various systems and zero-code rapid integration, giving your existing systems AI capabilities in an instant.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Operation Process\" src=\"img/index/flow.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The following uses a general knowledge base as an example to quickly create and publish an intelligent Q&amp;A agent through the public model service Alibaba Cloud Bailian (for local model deployment operations, such as DeepSeek deployment, refer to <a href=\"https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/bF253jBHZIWIHvNnSMv-Rg\">Quickly Deploy DeepSeek-R1 Using the 1Panel Open-Source Panel</a>) and explain the specific operations.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"31\">3.1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#31\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After logging in to the MaxKB system, open the 【Model】 page, select 【Alibaba Cloud Bailian】 in the provider list, then click 【Add Model】 and configure the parameters in the model configuration form as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the LLM model names supported by Alibaba Cloud Bailian. The dropdown options are some commonly used large language model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>API Key: create and view it under API Key management of the Alibaba Cloud DashScope Model Studio service.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Add Model API Key\" src=\"img/index/add_model.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Different platforms have different parameter requirements. For details on adding configurations of models from other providers, see the detailed documentation for each model integration.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"32\">3.2 Creating a Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#32\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Open the [Knowledge Base] page, click [Create Knowledge Base], enter the knowledge base name and description, select an embedding model, set the knowledge base type to General, and then upload the offline documents by dragging and dropping or by selecting files to upload.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Document Upload Requirements:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Text files: Markdown, TXT, PDF, DOCX, HTML, XLS, XLSX, CSV, ZIP;</li>\n<li>Table format: Excel, CSV;</li>\n<li>QA Q&amp;A pairs: Excel, CSV;</li>\n<li>By default, up to 50 files can be uploaded at once, with each file not exceeding 100 MB. This is configurable: the maximum number of uploaded files is 1000, and a single document is up to 1000 MB;</li>\n<li>Supports selecting a folder and uploading the files under it that meet the format requirements.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Documentation Standards Suggestion:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Standardize segment markers: The segment markers of offline documents should follow certain standards; otherwise the resulting segments will be irregular.</li>\n<li>A paragraph should be complete: ideally a single segment should describe one complete piece of content.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create General Knowledge\" src=\"img/index/dataset.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB supports two segmentation methods: intelligent segmentation and advanced segmentation.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Intelligent Segmentation</strong>: Performs drill-down segmentation level by level according to the Markdown format (supports up to 6 heading levels), with a maximum of 4096 characters per segment;</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Advanced Segmentation</strong>: Supports customizing segment identifiers, segment length, and auto-cleaning. Segment identifiers also support using regular expressions to process documents with complex structures.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Add segment titles as associated questions during import. When checked, the titles of all segments will be set as the associated questions of the segments.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Edit Segment\" src=\"img/index/paragraphing.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After clicking 【Create &amp; Import】, the system backend will perform auto segmentation, storage, and vectorization on the documents; when execution completes, each file's status in the knowledge base document list shows as 【Success】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Document List\" src=\"img/index/doc_list.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"List of split segments\" src=\"img/index/document_list.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"33\">3.3 Creating an Agent<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#33\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Create】, select the agent type, enter the agent name, and click 【Create】.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Simple Agent</strong>: Provides basic features and settings options that can meet most basic Q&amp;A needs, suitable for quickly launching agent applications.</li>\n<li><strong>Advanced Agent</strong>: Orchestrate functions and logic through basic components, tools, and nested agents to design workflows that meet the requirements of various complex business scenarios.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create Application\" src=\"img/index/creat_app.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the agent is created, enter the agent configuration settings page, with the agent information on the left and the debug preview interface on the right.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Name: the title and name of the dialog box shown when users ask questions.</li>\n<li>Description: a description of the agent's scenarios and use cases.</li>\n<li>AI Model: a large language model added under [System Settings] - [Model Management].</li>\n<li>System Prompt: the role or identity setting for the large model's responses.</li>\n<li>User Prompt: a detailed description that guides the model to generate specific output. The prompt can reference the parameter output of preceding nodes, such as the retrieval result of a preceding knowledge base retrieval and the question variable of the Start Node.</li>\n<li>Conversation History: the last N messages of the current session are submitted to the LLM. If set to 0, only the current question is submitted to the LLM.</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base:<ul>\n<li>User Prompt: a detailed description that guides the model to generate specific output. The prompt can reference the parameter output of preceding nodes, such as the retrieval result of a preceding knowledge base retrieval and the question variable of the Start Node.</li>\n<li>Associated Knowledge Base: after the user asks a question, segments will be retrieved from the associated knowledge base.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Skills: supports calling MCP, tools, skills, and agents.</li>\n<li>Opening remark: the greeting that pops up when a user opens a conversation. Markdown format is supported; the content after [-] is quick questions, one per line.</li>\n<li>Output reasoning: Configure whether the reasoning process of the large language model is output.</li>\n<li>Voice input: When enabled, questioning by voice is supported, which requires speech recognition model support.</li>\n<li>Voice playback: When enabled, the answer can be played by voice. It can be played through the browser, or you can also select a speech synthesis model.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>After the agent information is set up, you can test and verify it in the debug preview on the right. The questions asked in the debug preview are not counted in the conversation log.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Application Settings\" src=\"img/index/app_setting.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Detailed description of knowledge base parameter settings:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Retrieval Mode</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Vector retrieval: uses an embedding model to find the text segment most similar to the user's question by computing vector distance;</li>\n<li>Full-Text Search: searches by keyword and returns the text segments containing the most keywords;</li>\n<li>Hybrid Retrieval: Performs full-text retrieval and vector retrieval simultaneously, then reranks to select the best result matching the user's question from the two types of query results.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Similarity:</strong> A higher similarity indicates a stronger correlation between the question and the segment.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Cited Segments TOP:</strong> When asking a question, N segments are selected by similarity to generate the prompt for querying the LLM.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Maximum cited characters:</strong> Sets the maximum number of characters for the cited segment content; content exceeding this limit is truncated.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Handling Knowledge Bases Without Citations</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Continue asking the AI model: when no Knowledge Base segment is matched, the large model continues to answer on its own, which may cause hallucinations.</li>\n<li>Specified reply content: when no knowledge base segment is matched, you can specify reply content for further guidance.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Question Optimization:</strong> Once enabled, the user's question is first processed by an LLM optimization, and then the knowledge base is searched based on the optimized question.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Application Knowledge Base Parameter Settings\" src=\"img/index/parameter_setting.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After saving the settings and publishing, click 【Go to Chat】 on the Overview page of the agent list, or paste the public access link in your browser to enter the Q&amp;A page and ask questions.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Demo Preview\" src=\"img/index/app_view.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"34\">3.4 Agent Integration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#34\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB agents support zero-code quick embedding into third-party web systems.</p>\n<p>On the Agent Overview page, click 【Embed in Third-Party】, copy the corresponding embedding code, and embed it into a third-party system in full-screen or floating window mode. Once embedded, you can chat in the third-party system.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Embed in Third-Party\" src=\"img/index/embed.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB agents also support connecting to mobile agents such as WeCom, Official Accounts, DingTalk, and Feishu. For details, see: <a href=\"user_manual/X-Pack/app_integrate.html\">X-Pack Features - Agent Integration</a>.</p>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "quick_start.html#1", "title": "1 Quick Deployment ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "quick_start.html#2", "title": "2 Interface Introduction ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "quick_start.html#3", "title": "3 Quick Start ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "quick_start.html#31", "title": "3.1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "quick_start.html#32", "title": "3.2 Creating a Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "quick_start.html#33", "title": "3.3 Creating an Agent ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "quick_start.html#34", "title": "3.4 Agent Integration ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "system_arch.html", "title": "System Architecture", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">System Architecture<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Overall Architecture<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<p><img alt=\"Architecture Diagram\" src=\"img/index/maxkb_v2_arch.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Technology Stack<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>Front-end: <a href=\"https://cn.vuejs.org/\">Vue.js</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/didi/LogicFlow\">LogicFlow</a></li>\n<li>Backend: <a href=\"https://www.djangoproject.com/\">Python / Django</a>, <a href=\"https://www.langchain.com/\">langchain</a></li>\n<li>Vector Database: <a href=\"https://www.postgresql.org/\">PostgreSQL / pgvector</a>, Redis</li>\n<li>LLMs: DeepSeek, Tongyi Qianwen, Kimi, Baidu Qianfan, iFlytek Spark, Zhipu AI, OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Ollama, etc.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "system_arch.html#1", "title": "1 Overall Architecture ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "system_arch.html#2", "title": "2 Technology Stack ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "Skills/MaxKB_Skills.html", "title": "Come experience it | MaxKB Skills officially released", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"maxkb-skills\">Come experience it | MaxKB Skills officially released<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#maxkb-skills\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In 2026, following the rapid rise of OpenClaw, AI assistants made the leap from 'conversational Q&amp;A' to 'practical productivity.' Enterprise users gradually realized that simply having a static software system is far from enough - Skills that can be invoked by AI assistants at any time will play an important role in the digital and intelligent transformation of enterprises. In March 2026, the MaxKB open-source project team officially released MaxKB Skills.</p>\n<p>MaxKB Skills can give OpenClaw powerful enterprise knowledge base invocation capabilities. Normally, an AI assistant's knowledge querying is limited to general knowledge bases and cannot reach an enterprise's internal private assets. With MaxKB Skills, users can encapsulate internal enterprise documents, technical manuals, business processes, and more into knowledge retrieval skills that AI can directly invoke, allowing OpenClaw to precisely call these business-savvy \"external brains\". Employees can quickly access the enterprise's proprietary knowledge through natural language queries.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"maxkb-skills_1\">1. Features of MaxKB Skills<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#maxkb-skills_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB Skills are strictly designed following the official specifications, focusing on providing large language models with high-quality, semantically rich knowledge invocation interfaces. Its main functions include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Multi-Agent Collaboration and Answer Integration: breaking the limitations of a single agent. The AI assistant can invoke multiple different agents in sequence based on complex instructions (for example, first querying the product manual, then querying the after-sales case library), and autonomously perform correlation and deep integration analysis;</li>\n<li>Comprehensive agent awareness and expert routing: supports real-time retrieval of all published knowledge-base agents in the platform. The AI assistant can accurately determine which agent (or agents) is best suited to answer the current question and automatically distribute the task.</li>\n<li>Enterprise-grade permission and security isolation (X-Pack): supports workspace ID isolation and multiple authentication methods (based on Token or username/password). Permission control is configured based on MaxKB's backend RBAC (Role-Based Access Control), ensuring that AI assistants strictly adhere to the enterprise's permission boundaries when integrating information from multiple knowledge bases.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"maxkb-skills_2\">2. Methods for Installing MaxKB Skills<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#maxkb-skills_2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Deploying MaxKB Skills is very simple, supporting either manual configuration by developers or AI-guided automation. The following is an example of the installation, configuration, and testing process using OpenClaw:</p>\n<p>1. MaxKB Skills Access Address:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>https://github.com/1Panel-dev/MaxKB-skills\n\nhttps://clawhub.ai/liuruibin/maxkb\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>2. Quick Start</p>\n<p>Quickly install MaxKB Skills by chatting with OpenClaw:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>安装技能：git clone https://github.com/1Panel-dev/MaxKB-skills ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/maxkb-agents\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"openclaw\" src=\"../img/Skills/openclaw_chat.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>3. Security Configuration and Integration</p>\n<p>To ensure that OpenClaw can connect to the MaxKB service safely and stably, you need to configure key environment variables. The specific descriptions of the relevant parameters are as follows:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Variable</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n<th>Default Value</th>\n<th>Required</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>MAXKB_DOMAIN</strong></td>\n<td>MaxKB Service Address</td>\n<td><code>&lt;maxkb_domain&gt;</code></td>\n<td>Yes</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>MAXKB_API_PREFIX</strong></td>\n<td>API path prefix, applicable for subpath deployment</td>\n<td><code>/admin</code></td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>MAXKB_TOKEN</strong></td>\n<td>Bearer Token (Administrator API Key)</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>Choose One of the Two</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>MAXKB_USERNAME</strong></td>\n<td>Login Username</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>Choose One of the Two</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>MAXKB_PASSWORD</strong></td>\n<td>Login Password</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>Choose One of the Two</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>MAXKB_WORKSPACE_ID</strong></td>\n<td>workspace_id</td>\n<td><code>default</code></td>\n<td>No</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Note: If both a username/password and a Token are configured, the system will prioritize using the username/password to log in and obtain a new Token to ensure session validity.</p>\n<p>① MaxKB Community Edition Configuration</p>\n<p>For the MaxKB Community Edition, you usually only need to configure the account and password to complete the connection.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>MAXKB_DOMAIN=&lt;你的 MaxKB 服务地址&gt;\n\nMAXKB_USERNAME=&lt;用户名&gt;\n\nMAXKB_PASSWORD=&lt;密码&gt;\n\nMAXKB_WORKSPACE_ID=default\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>② MaxKB Professional Edition, Enterprise Edition</p>\n<p>For MaxKB Professional or Enterprise Edition users with X-Pack enhancements, you can choose to use the more secure Token authentication method.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>MAXKB_DOMAIN=&lt;你的 MaxKB 服务地址&gt;\n\nMAXKB_WORKSPACE_ID=default\n\nMAXKB_TOKEN=&lt;Bearer Token&gt;\n\n# 或使用账号密码\n\nMAXKB_USERNAME=&lt;用户名&gt;\n\nMAXKB_PASSWORD=&lt;密码&gt;\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"get_API_Key\" src=\"../img/Skills/get_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"maxkb-skills_3\">3. Use Cases for MaxKB Skills<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#maxkb-skills_3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the configuration is complete, you can converse with OpenClaw in natural language and have it perform operations such as listing the existing agents in MaxKB and autonomously choosing an agent to chat with.</p>\n<p>1. List Existing Agents</p>\n<p>Question: Please list the existing agents.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"openclaw\" src=\"../img/Skills/openclaw_ask.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>2. Choose an Agent and Chat</p>\n<p>Question: How do I reset the MaxKB administrator password?</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"openclaw\" src=\"../img/Skills/openclaw_ask1.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"openclaw\" src=\"../img/Skills/openclaw_ask2.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"_1\">4. Summary<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The value of MaxKB Skills goes far beyond adding a \"Knowledge Base Query\" button to an AI assistant. Its deeper significance lies in upgrading a static enterprise private knowledge base into a dynamic \"digital warehouse\" that can be collaboratively invoked by AI through standardized, intelligent interface encapsulation, thereby transforming how knowledge is accessed. The long-term advantages of MaxKB Skills are reflected in:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Breaking down cross-database search barriers: through coordinated invocation of multiple agents, the AI assistant can instantly aggregate data scattered across different manuals and specifications, without requiring users to repeatedly switch pages to search, turning private data into more powerful productivity;</li>\n<li>Precise automated distribution: using the Agent's query skills, the AI assistant can autonomously identify the best-matching knowledge source, transforming \"people looking for knowledge\" into \"knowledge proactively supporting business,\" ensuring the accuracy of professional responses;</li>\n<li>Reduce the cost of AI transformation: users do not need to adjust their existing MaxKB platform. Through the Skills interface, AI assistants can be called quickly, making it a better path for enterprises to quickly deploy AI applications.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "Skills/MaxKB_Skills.html#maxkb-skills_1", "title": "1. Features of MaxKB Skills ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "Skills/MaxKB_Skills.html#maxkb-skills_2", "title": "2. Methods for Installing MaxKB Skills ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "Skills/MaxKB_Skills.html#maxkb-skills_3", "title": "3. Use Cases for MaxKB Skills ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "Skills/MaxKB_Skills.html#_1", "title": "4. Summary ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/APIKey_chat.html", "title": "APIKey chat", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>APIKey chat</h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Agents created in MaxKB support access via the OpenAI SDK format and the provided system SDK. The Professional Edition provides platform-level complete SDKs on top of the Community Edition. For details, see: <a href=\"../user_manual/X-Pack/system_API.html\">System API</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"1-openai-api\">1 Standard OpenAI API Format<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1-openai-api\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB agents are compatible with the OpenAI API format. Simply replace the Base URL and API Key with those provided by the MaxKB agent on top of the original OpenAI API calling method.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"API doc\" src=\"../img/dev/openai_baseurl.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 将 url 和 Authorization 替换为 MaxKB 智能体实际真实的 Base URL 和 API Key。\n\n\n\ncurl https://maxkb.fit2cloud.com/api/application/xxxxxxxx-8c56-11ef-a99e-0242ac140003/chat/completions \\\n\n    -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n\n    -H \"Authorization: Bearer application-xxxxxxxxf00e21a7530d1177c20967\"  \\\n\n    -d '{\n\n        \"model\": \"gpt-3.5-turbo\",\n\n        \"messages\": [\n\n            {\n\n              \"role\": \"你是杭州飞致云信息科技有限公司旗下产品 MaxKB 知识库问答系统的智能小助手，你的工作是帮助 MaxKB 用户解答使用中遇到的问题，用户找你回答问题时，你要把主题放在 MaxKB 知识库问答系统身上。\",\n\n              \"content\": \"MaxKB 是什么？\"\n\n            }\n\n        ]\n\n    }'\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2-api\">2 System API<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2-api\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"21-api\">2.1 Open API Documentation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#21-api\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Copy and visit the swagger address in the agent information.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"API doc\" src=\"../img/dev/app_swaagger.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"22-api-key\">2.2 API Key Authentication<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#22-api-key\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p><img alt=\"APIKEY\" src=\"../img/dev/app_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"23\">2.3 Get Agent Information<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#23\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Call the profile API to get the detailed information of the agent (agent id, name, etc.).</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\" profile\" src=\"../img/dev/app_profile.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"24\">2.4 Open Session<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#24\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Call the open-session API, enter the agent id obtained in the previous step, open the session and get the session id.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"appid\" src=\"../img/dev/chat_open.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"25\">2.5 Conducting a Conversation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#25\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Call the chat API and enter the session id to chat.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"chatid\" src=\"../img/dev/app_chat.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "dev_manual/APIKey_chat.html#1-openai-api", "title": "1 Standard OpenAI API Format ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/APIKey_chat.html#2-api", "title": "2 System API ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/APIKey_chat.html#21-api", "title": "2.1 Open API Documentation ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/APIKey_chat.html#22-api-key", "title": "2.2 API Key Authentication ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/APIKey_chat.html#23", "title": "2.3 Get Agent Information ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/APIKey_chat.html#24", "title": "2.4 Open Session ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/APIKey_chat.html#25", "title": "2.5 Conducting a Conversation ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/dev_environment.html", "title": "Development Environment Setup", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Development Environment Setup <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Project Structure<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>.          \n\n├── LICENSE                 # License 申明        \n\n├── README.md           \n\n├── apps                    # 后端项目根目录        \n\n│ ├── application           # 应用\n\n│ ├── common                # 项目公共资源目录\n\n│ ├── dataset               # 知识库\n\n│ ├── embedding             # 向量化\n\n│ ├── function_lib          # 函数库\n\n│ ├── ops                   # \n\n│ ├── setting               # 设置\n\n│ ├── smartdoc              # 项目主目录          \n\n│ ├── users                 # 用户相关          \n\n│ └── manage.py             # django项目入口         \n\n├── installer               # 安装相关  \n\n├── pyproject.toml          # 后端依赖 配置文件         \n\n└── ui                      # 前端项目根目录          \n\n├── config_example.yml      # 项目配置示例             \n\n├── main.py                 # 项目入口文件              \n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Environment Preparation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Front-end Environment Preparation</strong> <br/>\n  Install <a href=\"https://nodejs.org/\">node</a>, v16 or later</li>\n<li><strong>Backend Environment Preparation</strong> <br/>\n  Install <a href=\"https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3115/\">python</a>, version v3.11.x<br/>\n  Install <a href=\"https://www.jetbrains.com/pycharm/download/\">pycharm</a></li>\n<li><strong>Database</strong> <br/>\n  Install <a href=\"https://www.postgresql.org/\">PostgreSql</a>, version v15.x</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Local Configuration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"31\">3.1 Create Database<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#31\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Manually create the MaxKB application database in PostgreSql, named <code>maxkb</code>.<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 创建数据库\n\nCREATE DATABASE \"maxkb\"; \n\n# 切换使用数据库\n\n\\c \"maxkb\"; \n\n# 创建 vector 扩展\n\nCREATE EXTENSION \"vector\";\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"32\">3.2 Configuration File<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#32\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before starting the project, you need to prepare the configuration file and directory.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Preparing the Configuration File</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\"># 将 config_example.yml 配置文件拷贝至 /opt/maxkb/conf 目录下</span>\n\ncp<span class=\"w\"> </span>config_example.yml<span class=\"w\"> </span>/opt/maxkb/conf\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Configure /opt/maxkb/conf/config_example.yml</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 数据库配置（将以下信息替换为实际环境信息）\n\nDB_NAME: maxkb\n\nDB_HOST: localhost\n\nDB_PORT: 5432\n\nDB_USER: root\n\nDB_PASSWORD: xxx\n\nDB_ENGINE: django.db.backends.postgresql_psycopg2\n\n\n\n# 模型相关配置\n\n# 模型路径:如果 EMBEDDING_MODEL_NAME 是绝对路径则无效,反之则会从 https://huggingface.co/ 下载模型到当前目录\n\nEMBEDDING_MODEL_PATH: /opt/maxkb/model/\n\n# 模型名称:如果模型名称是路径,则会加载目录下的模型,如果是模型名称,则会在 https://huggingface.co/ 下载模型 模型的下载位置为 EMBEDDING_MODEL_PATH\n\nEMBEDDING_MODEL_NAME: /opt/maxkb/model/shibing624_text2vec-base-chinese\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Development and Debugging<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"41\">4.1 Starting the Frontend<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#41\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\"># 在 `ui`目录 执行安装前端需要的依赖</span>\n\nnpm<span class=\"w\"> </span>install\n\n\n\n<span class=\"c1\"># 然后启动项目</span>\n\nnpm<span class=\"w\"> </span>run<span class=\"w\"> </span>dev\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>After starting successfully, it will be displayed as shown below.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Start Frontend\" src=\"../img/dev/npm_run.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"42\">4.2 Starting the Backend<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#42\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For the backend system, you need to start the web service, the local model service, and the asynchronous task queue service. <br/>\nNote: run this in the project root directory</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Run the following commands in sequence in the MaxKB project root directory to start the Web service.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 安装 poetry 包管理器\n\npip install poetry\n\n\n\n# 安装后端需要的依赖\n\npoetry install\n\n* 注意：如果在国内安装，需要配置 poetry 的源，否则下载非常慢，经常无法正常安装，配置命令为：`poetry source add --priority=primary mirrors http://mirrors.aliyun.com/pypi/simple`\n\n\n\n# 启动项目\n\npython main.py start\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Start Web Service\" src=\"../img/dev/main_start.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Run the following commands in sequence in the MaxKB project root directory to start the local model service.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 启动项目\n\npython main.py dev local_model\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Start Local Model Service\" src=\"../img/dev/main_localmodel.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Run the following commands in sequence in the MaxKB project root directory to start the asynchronous task service.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 启动项目\n\npython main.py dev celery\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Start Asynchronous Task Service\" src=\"../img/dev/main_celery.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"5\">5 Access Project<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Once both the front-end and back-end have started successfully, you can access the application in your browser via the front-end route (the access address shown when the front-end starts).</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Browser Access\" src=\"../img/dev/maxkb_running.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "dev_manual/dev_environment.html#1", "title": "1 Project Structure ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/dev_environment.html#2", "title": "2 Environment Preparation ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/dev_environment.html#3", "title": "3 Local Configuration ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/dev_environment.html#31", "title": "3.1 Create Database ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/dev_environment.html#32", "title": "3.2 Configuration File ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/dev_environment.html#4", "title": "4 Development and Debugging ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/dev_environment.html#41", "title": "4.1 Starting the Frontend ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/dev_environment.html#42", "title": "4.2 Starting the Backend ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "dev_manual/dev_environment.html#5", "title": "5 Access Project ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/GPU_runOllama.html", "title": "How to Run LLM Models with Ollama on GPU", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"ollama-gpu-llm\">How to Run LLM Models with Ollama on GPU <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#ollama-gpu-llm\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Taking NVIDIA as an example, this section explains the specific operations for running large models with Ollama in GPU mode.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Install the NVIDIA Container Toolkit<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Taking Ubuntu 22.04 as an example (for other systems, refer to: <a href=\"https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/cloud-native/container-toolkit/latest/arch-overview.html\">NVIDIA Official Documentation</a>)</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Configure the apt source<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>curl -fsSL https://nvidia.github.io/libnvidia-container/gpgkey | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /usr/share/keyrings/nvidia-container-toolkit-keyring.gpg \\\n\n&amp;&amp; curl -s -L https://nvidia.github.io/libnvidia-container/stable/deb/nvidia-container-toolkit.list | \\\n\n    sed 's#deb https://#deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/nvidia-container-toolkit-keyring.gpg] https://#g' | \\\n\n    sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/nvidia-container-toolkit.list\n\n</code></pre></div></li>\n<li>Update Source\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>sudo apt-get update\n\n</code></pre></div></li>\n<li>Installing the Toolkit<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>sudo apt-get install -y nvidia-container-toolkit\n\n</code></pre></div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2-gpu-ollama\">2 Running Ollama on GPU<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2-gpu-ollama\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 以后台模式运行 ollama 容器，并允许容器访问主机上所有可用的 NVIDIA GPU\n\ndocker run --gpus all -d -v /opt/ai/ollama:/root/.ollama -p 11434:11434 --name ollama ollama/ollama\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3-ollama\">3 Downloading a Model with Ollama<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3-ollama\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 在线下载并运行模型\n\ndocker exec -it ollama ollama run qwen:7b\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"4-maxkb-ollama\">4 Adding an Ollama Model in MaxKB<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4-maxkb-ollama\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After downloading and running the model service, you can add and use the corresponding model in MaxKB.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Add Model\" src=\"../img/FAQ/addmodel.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "faq/GPU_runOllama.html#1", "title": "1 Install the NVIDIA Container Toolkit ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/GPU_runOllama.html#2-gpu-ollama", "title": "2 Running Ollama on GPU ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/GPU_runOllama.html#3-ollama", "title": "3 Downloading a Model with Ollama ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/GPU_runOllama.html#4-maxkb-ollama", "title": "4 Adding an Ollama Model in MaxKB ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/MaxKB%20VS.Dify.html", "title": "", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/Offline_install_OllamaModel.html", "title": "How to Deploy LLM Models with Ollama Offline", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"ollama-llm\">How to Deploy LLM Models with Ollama Offline <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#ollama-llm\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Taking the qwen:0.5b model as an example, this section details the process and steps for deploying LLM models offline with Ollama.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Download Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Visit Hugging Face and download the qwen1_5-0_5b-chat-q5_k_m.gguf model file.<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen1.5-0.5B-Chat-GGUF/tree/main\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Download Model\" src=\"../img/FAQ/downModel.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Upload Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Upload the downloaded Qwen1.5-0.5B-Chat-GGUF model file to the server where Ollama is installed.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3-ollama-modelfile\">3 Creating an Ollama Modelfile<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3-ollama-modelfile\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Create a file named Modelfile with the following contents:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>FROM ./qwen1_5-0_5b-chat-q5_k_m.gguf\n\n\n\nTEMPLATE \"\"\"{{ if .System }}&lt;|im_start|&gt;system\n\n{{ .System }}&lt;|im_end|&gt;{{ end }}&lt;|im_start|&gt;user\n\n{{ .Prompt }}&lt;|im_end|&gt;\n\n&lt;|im_start|&gt;assistant\n\n\"\"\"\n\n\n\nPARAMETER stop \"&lt;|im_start|&gt;\"\n\nPARAMETER stop \"&lt;|im_end|&gt;\"\n\n</code></pre></div>Note: Different models have different Modelfile contents. For details, refer to the Ollama official website <a href=\"https://ollama.com/library/qwen:0.5b\">Parameter Settings</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Model Parameter Template\" src=\"../img/FAQ/modelSetting.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4-ollama\">4 Creating a Model in Ollama<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4-ollama\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Run the following command to create the model:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>ollama create qwen:0.5b -f Modelfile\n\n</code></pre></div>Run the following command to confirm the model was created successfully:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>ollama list\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Ollama View Model List\" src=\"../img/FAQ/ollamaList.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"5-maxkb\">5 Add the Created Private Model in MaxKB<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5-maxkb\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<p><img alt=\"Adding a Model in MaxKB\" src=\"../img/FAQ/MaxKBaddModel.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "faq/Offline_install_OllamaModel.html#1", "title": "1 Download Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/Offline_install_OllamaModel.html#2", "title": "2 Upload Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/Offline_install_OllamaModel.html#3-ollama-modelfile", "title": "3 Creating an Ollama Modelfile ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/Offline_install_OllamaModel.html#4-ollama", "title": "4 Creating a Model in Ollama ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/Offline_install_OllamaModel.html#5-maxkb", "title": "5 Add the Created Private Model in MaxKB ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/apply_setting.html", "title": "Application FAQ", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Application FAQ<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Canvas Display Issue on the Application Advanced Orchestration Settings Page<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The browser kernel version is too low (e.g., Google Chrome 93.0.4577.63), so the browser must be upgraded.<br/>\n<strong>Note</strong>: Workflow orchestration does not support the Safari browser; we recommend using the latest version of Google Chrome.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Cannot Retrieve the Knowledge Base After Trying a Different Answer<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When the [Get Another Answer] feature is used, the retrieval mechanism excludes all segments retrieved previously and then performs a new retrieval. If the previous retrieval returned only one match, the new retrieval may return empty results.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Displaying Different Language Interfaces in the Same Application<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The language selection in Application Display Settings is not consistent. You need to select the desired language in Application Display Settings and save it.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/%E8%AF%AD%E8%A8%80%E6%98%BE%E7%A4%BA%E8%AE%BE%E7%BD%AE.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4-file-is-not-a-zip-file\">4 Application Document Content Extraction Reports the ‘File is not a zip file’ Error<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4-file-is-not-a-zip-file\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The uploaded file is actually a doc-type file rather than a zip file. Make sure the uploaded file format is correct.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"5-mcp-unhandled-errors-in-a-taskgroup1-sub-exception\">5 Application Reports Error \"unhandled errors in a TaskGroup(1 sub-exception)\" When Adding an MCP Component<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5-mcp-unhandled-errors-in-a-taskgroup1-sub-exception\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The MCP service failed to start. The database connection password contains the special character <code>@</code>, which conflicts with the dbhub startup command.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"6-mcp-transport\">6 Application Reports Error \"transport\" When Adding an MCP Component<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#6-mcp-transport\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The MCP Server Config format is incorrect; it is missing \"transport\": \"sse\". Add \"transport\": \"sse\" to the configuration.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"7-swagger-api-url-scheme-must-be-http-or-https-for-cors-request\">7 Requesting the Swagger API Reports Error \"URL scheme must be 'http' or 'https' for CORS request.\"<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#7-swagger-api-url-scheme-must-be-http-or-https-for-cors-request\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The schemes format of the Swagger documentation was not selected correctly. The IP address uses http while the domain uses https. Ensure the protocols of the IP and domain match.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"8\">8 How Are Files Uploaded During Application Conversations Stored? Are They Deleted on a Schedule?<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#8\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Files uploaded by MaxKB applications during a conversation are first temporarily stored in the database, and then cleared daily at a scheduled time (00:05:00) by clearing the chat history, to ensure data security.</p>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "faq/apply_setting.html#1", "title": "1 Canvas Display Issue on the Application Advanced Orchestration Settings Page ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/apply_setting.html#2", "title": "2 Cannot Retrieve the Knowledge Base After Trying a Different Answer ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/apply_setting.html#3", "title": "3 Displaying Different Language Interfaces in the Same Application ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/apply_setting.html#4-file-is-not-a-zip-file", "title": "4 Application Document Content Extraction Reports the ‘File is not a zip file’ Error ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/apply_setting.html#5-mcp-unhandled-errors-in-a-taskgroup1-sub-exception", "title": "5 Application Reports Error \"unhandled errors in a TaskGroup(1 sub-exception)\" When Adding an MCP Component ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/apply_setting.html#6-mcp-transport", "title": "6 Application Reports Error \"transport\" When Adding an MCP Component ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/apply_setting.html#7-swagger-api-url-scheme-must-be-http-or-https-for-cors-request", "title": "7 Requesting the Swagger API Reports Error \"URL scheme must be 'http' or 'https' for CORS request.\" ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/apply_setting.html#8", "title": "8 How Are Files Uploaded During Application Conversations Stored? Are They Deleted on a Schedule? ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/doc_segment.html", "title": "How to Segment Knowledge Base Documents Sensibly", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>How to Segment Knowledge Base Documents Sensibly</h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Based on the document structure, how to reasonably segment the content is very important for the subsequent knowledge base retrieval and matching; splitting by headings is the most common method.\nBy default, MaxKB splits uploaded documents using the two rules of Intelligent Segmentation and Advanced Segmentation. Both rules essentially extract content based on segment identifiers and character counts, and for documents with well-structured styles (referring to styles that use multi-level headings), the desired effect can be achieved.</p>\n<p>So how should documents that look regular but do not use standard heading styles, like the document shown in the figure below, be segmented sensibly?</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/doc_split.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The default segmentation rules of MaxKB essentially split text according to specific regular expressions. In addition, the advanced segmentation rules support manually entering regular expressions for splitting, so text can be segmented reasonably according to the regular expression patterns in the document.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Common Segmentation Markers and Their Regular Expressions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Scenarios</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Example</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Expression</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Chapter Title</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>第一章 RAG与大模型应用</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>[第][一二三四五六七八九十]+[章]</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Section Title</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>第一节 大模型应用的方向：RAG</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>[第][一二三四五六七八九十]+[节]</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Numbered Heading</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>一、 RAG与大模型应用</code> <code>1.1 大模型应用的方向：RAG</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>[一二三四五六七八九十|1-9]+[、|.][1-9]*[.]*[1-9]*</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Item</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>第一条：本公司员工均应遵守以下规定。</code></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>[第][一二三四五六七八九十]+[条]</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Operations and Results<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After uploading the document, if the segmentation preview is not satisfactory when the default segmentation rule is selected, you can use advanced segmentation.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/doc_default_split.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/doc_advance_split.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>To segment effectively, you need to manually enter the regular expression <code>[第][一二三四五六七八九十]+[条]</code> for the segment identifier in the Segment Identifier field (Note: press Enter after entering it for it to take effect), set the length to the maximum length of a single segment, and then click Generate Preview.\nFrom the preview results, you can see that each item is completely split into one segment, ensuring semantic integrity.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/doc_re_split.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "faq/doc_segment.html#1", "title": "1 Common Segmentation Markers and Their Regular Expressions ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/doc_segment.html#2", "title": "2 Operations and Results ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/function_library.html", "title": "Function Library", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Function Library <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Missing Dependencies Prompted After the Function Library Runs<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/%E5%87%BD%E6%95%B0%E5%BA%93%E7%BC%BA%E5%B0%91%E4%BE%9D%E8%B5%96.png\" width=\"900px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The \"missing dependencies\" prompt in the Function Library at runtime occurs because some function libraries need to call other third-party libraries to complete specific functions at runtime. If these third-party libraries are not installed, the function library cannot run properly, and a missing dependency prompt is shown. <br/>\nEnter the MaxKB container:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>docker exec -it maxkb bash \n\n</code></pre></div>Use pip to install third-party dependencies, such as pymysql:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>pip install pymysql\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2-sql-server\">2 Error Connecting the Function Library to a SQL Server Database<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2-sql-server\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/%E5%87%BD%E6%95%B0%E5%BA%93%E8%BF%9E%E6%8E%A5%E6%95%B0%E6%8D%AE%E5%BA%93%E5%A4%B1%E8%B4%A5.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When connecting to the SQL Server database, an error is reported: pymssql connection failed 20002, b'DB-Lib error message 20002, severity 9: Adaptive Server connection failed.<br/>\nPossible causes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Network issue: the container cannot access the target server IP (e.g., 192.168.0.23).</li>\n<li>Dependency Issue: the pymssql version is incompatible, or its installation failed.</li>\n<li>Connection configuration issue: The correct TDS version is not specified.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Solution:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ensure network connectivity: Check whether the network connection between the container and the target server is normal, verify SQL Server is configured to allow remote connections, and check that the firewall settings permit access to the target port.</li>\n<li>Reinstall a compatible version of pymssql. After installing the dependency libraries in the container, ensure that these dependency libraries are used correctly to connect to the database in the function library.</li>\n<li>Specify the TDS version: explicitly specify the TDS version in the connection statement (e.g., 7.0).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3-exceptionkeyword-eval-is-banned-in-the-tool\">3 Execution Prompt \"Exception: keyword 'eval(' is banned in the tool.\"<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3-exceptionkeyword-eval-is-banned-in-the-tool\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>此限制在 v2.4.0 及之后版本已修改，不再限制 Python 代码内容，改成限制运行进程的边界。\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>To strengthen security and prevent malicious script execution, MaxKB V2 prohibits statements such as subprocess, system, and eval in tool scripts.</p>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "faq/function_library.html#1", "title": "1 Missing Dependencies Prompted After the Function Library Runs ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/function_library.html#2-sql-server", "title": "2 Error Connecting the Function Library to a SQL Server Database ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/function_library.html#3-exceptionkeyword-eval-is-banned-in-the-tool", "title": "3 Execution Prompt \"Exception: keyword 'eval(' is banned in the tool.\" ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/install_configuration.html", "title": "Installation, Deployment, and Startup Issues", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Installation, Deployment, and Startup Issues <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-maxkb-docker-compose-xxxx\">1 Error During MaxKB Installation: docker-compose--X.XX.X Cannot Start or Access the Service<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1-maxkb-docker-compose-xxxx\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>An outdated Docker version may cause installation to fail; it is recommended to use the Docker bundled in the installation package. The Docker version used in the installation package is 27.2.0, and the Compose version is v2.29.2.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2-pgsql\">2 How Do I Expose the Built-in pgsql to External Access Through a Specified Host Port?<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2-pgsql\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When installing with the default configuration, for security, the pgsql container only exposes port 5432 to the host machine, and no other address can access it.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"PostgreSQL Default Access Rules\" src=\"../img/FAQ/lcoal_pgsql.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>If you need to expose pgsql to other servers, configure it in /opt/maxkb/.env, then run <code>mkctl reload</code> to reload the configuration.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"PostgreSQL Default Access Rules\" src=\"../img/FAQ/expose_pgsql_config.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"PostgreSQL Default Access Rules\" src=\"../img/FAQ/expose_pgsql.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3-modulenotfounderror-no-module-named-xxx\">3 Error During Upgrade: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'XXX'<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3-modulenotfounderror-no-module-named-xxx\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Some dependency packages of older versions are incompatible with the new version, preventing the system from running properly. Enter the storage directory of the dependency packages:\nRun the following command to create the model:\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>cd /opt/maxkb/python-packages\n\n</code></pre></div>Find the packages causing the dependency conflict, usually by checking the error logs to determine the conflicting package names. After cleaning up the dependency packages, restart the service with <code>mkctl restart</code> to ensure the changes take effect.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"4-postgresql-too-many-clients-already\">4 PostgreSQL Exceeds the Maximum Number of Client Connections, Reporting the ‘too many clients already’ Error<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4-postgresql-too-many-clients-already\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>This indicates that the number of client connections configured has reached its limit, and the configuration needs to be adjusted to allow more connections. Navigate to the directory where the PostgreSQL configuration file is located:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>cd /opt/maxkb/data/postgresql/pgdata/\n\n</code></pre></div>In the postgresql.conf file, find the max_connections parameter and set its value to the required number of connections. For example, set the maximum number of connections to 200<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>max_connections = 200\n\n</code></pre></div>Stop the currently running MaxKB service and delete the PostgreSQL container:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>docker stop maxkb\n\n\n\ndocker rm maxkb\n\n</code></pre></div>Run <code>mkctl reload</code> to reload the service configuration and start the service.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"5\">5 Migration FAQ<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"51-powershell\">5.1 Cannot Execute PowerShell Script<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#51-powershell\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p><img alt=\"Unable to run the PowerShell script\" src=\"../img/FAQ/error1.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>If you cannot run the PowerShell script, you may need to change the execution policy:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Temporary Modification (Recommended)<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>Set-ExecutionPolicy -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Scope Process       \n\n</code></pre></div></li>\n<li>Permanent Modification (requires administrator permission)<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>Set-ExecutionPolicy -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope LocalMachine     \n\n</code></pre></div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"52\">5.2 Garbled Error Reported After Executing the Script<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#52\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p><img alt=\"Garbled text when running PowerShell scripts\" src=\"../img/FAQ/error2.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Open the file with Notepad and save the file as text in ANSI format.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Solution\" src=\"../img/FAQ/solution1.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Execute PowerShell again to run the migration command normally.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Solution\" src=\"../img/FAQ/solution2.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"53-docker-desktop-maxkb-maxkb\">5.3 After Migration, the Directory Path Content of MaxKB Installed via Docker Desktop Is Empty, but MaxKB Runs Normally<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#53-docker-desktop-maxkb-maxkb\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After migrating MaxKB installed via Docker Desktop, the mount path content is empty, but MaxKB runs normally.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Solution\" src=\"../img/FAQ/Path%20missing.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When installing MaxKB V2, the container data mount directory is /opt/maxkb; simply change the mount directory.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>V1:/var/lib/postgresql/data\n\nV2:/opt/maxkb\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Solution\" src=\"../img/FAQ/solution3.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "faq/install_configuration.html#1-maxkb-docker-compose-xxxx", "title": "1 Error During MaxKB Installation: docker-compose--X.XX.X Cannot Start or Access the Service ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/install_configuration.html#2-pgsql", "title": "2 How Do I Expose the Built-in pgsql to External Access Through a Specified Host Port? ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/install_configuration.html#3-modulenotfounderror-no-module-named-xxx", "title": "3 Error During Upgrade: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'XXX' ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/install_configuration.html#4-postgresql-too-many-clients-already", "title": "4 PostgreSQL Exceeds the Maximum Number of Client Connections, Reporting the ‘too many clients already’ Error ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/install_configuration.html#5", "title": "5 Migration FAQ ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/install_configuration.html#51-powershell", "title": "5.1 Cannot Execute PowerShell Script ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/install_configuration.html#52", "title": "5.2 Garbled Error Reported After Executing the Script ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/install_configuration.html#53-docker-desktop-maxkb-maxkb", "title": "5.3 After Migration, the Directory Path Content of MaxKB Installed via Docker Desktop Is Empty, but MaxKB Runs Normally ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/knowledge_base.html", "title": "Knowledge Base", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Unsatisfactory Intelligent Segmentation Results<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The default segmentation logic may not fully fit the content structure of a particular document. After importing the document, you can try selecting “Advanced Segmentation” and entering a regular expression directly in the segment identifier input box to achieve precise segmentation.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/%E4%BD%BF%E7%94%A8%E9%AB%98%E7%BA%A7%E5%88%86%E6%AE%B5.png\" width=\"900px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Example Use Cases</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Multi-level Numeric Numbering</strong><br/><br/>\n    Regular expression: \\d+.\\d*.\\d*.[a-zA-Z\\s]*[\\u4e00-\\u9fa5，]+</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Chinese ordinal numbering</strong>: <br/>\n    Regular expression: [一二三四五六七八九十]*、[\\u4e00-\\u9fa5a-zA-Z]+<br/>\n    Example: 一、Title</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Novel chapter table of contents</strong>: <br/>\n    Regular expression: [第][一二三四五六七八九十]+[章][\\u4e00-\\u4e00a-zA-Z]+<br/>\n    Example: Chapter 1 Title</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Multi-level Chinese + Numeric Numbering</strong>: <br/>\n    Regular expression: [一二三四五六七八九十|1-9]+[、|.]1-9*.[1-9]*[\\u4e00-\\u9fa5a-zA-Z]+<br/>\n    Example: 一、Level 1 heading 1.1 Level 2 heading</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For detailed operations and preview effects, refer to <a href=\"https://kb.fit2cloud.com/?p=bfe242a4-9a77-459c-ac75-4ef078e170c9\"><strong>MaxKB Segmentation Using Regular Expressions</strong></a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2-0\">2 The Character Count Is 0 After Vectorizing the Uploaded Document<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2-0\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The uploaded document is actually in <code>.doc</code> format rather than another supported format, resulting in 0 characters after vectorization.\nDocument upload requirements:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Text files: Markdown, TXT, PDF, DOCX, HTML, XLS, XLSX, CSV, ZIP;</li>\n<li>Tables: XLS, XLSX, CSV, ZIP;</li>\n<li>QA Q&amp;A pairs: XLS, XLSX, CSV, ZIP;</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Document Submitted Successfully But the Uploaded Document Is Not Displayed<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Press F12 to view the error code. If it shows \"413 Request Entity Too Large\", the request size configured in a reverse proxy such as nginx is too small. If it is nginx, modify the client_max_body_size value and then reload the nginx configuration.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"4-zip\">4 Segment Count Mismatch After Exporting and Re-importing a Knowledge Base in ZIP Format<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4-zip\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After exporting the knowledge base, when re-uploading the ZIP file, select <strong>“QA Q&amp;A Pairs”</strong> to import it.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"5\">5 Document Title Is Garbled After Uploading a Document to the Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Compression software can cause issues. WinRAR and 52 Compression are known to have compatibility problems; we recommend using other compression software to compress and decompress files.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"6\">6 Vectorization Succeeded, but Question Generation Failed<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#6\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The large language model currently used for question generation may have issues. You can try switching to another large language model for question generation to resolve the problem. Additionally, you can check the backend log files for more error information. The log files are located in the <code>/opt/maxkb/logs</code> directory; reviewing the logs will help you understand the specific cause of the error.</p>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "faq/knowledge_base.html#1", "title": "1 Unsatisfactory Intelligent Segmentation Results ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/knowledge_base.html#2-0", "title": "2 The Character Count Is 0 After Vectorizing the Uploaded Document ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/knowledge_base.html#3", "title": "3 Document Submitted Successfully But the Uploaded Document Is Not Displayed ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/knowledge_base.html#4-zip", "title": "4 Segment Count Mismatch After Exporting and Re-importing a Knowledge Base in ZIP Format ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/knowledge_base.html#5", "title": "5 Document Title Is Garbled After Uploading a Document to the Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/knowledge_base.html#6", "title": "6 Vectorization Succeeded, but Question Generation Failed ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/maxkb_In_halo.html", "title": "Integrating the MaxKB Assistant into Halo", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"maxkb-halo\">Integrating the MaxKB Assistant into Halo <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#maxkb-halo\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/halo-dev/halo\">Halo</a> [ˈheɪloʊ], a powerful and easy-to-use open-source website-building tool. Through the MaxKB Assistant plugin, article content can be synced to the MaxKB knowledge base, and intelligent Q&amp;A can be provided for the website via floating-window mode.     <br/>\nFor instructions on using the MaxKB Assistant plugin, please see <a href=\"https://www.halo.run/store/apps/app-aWHcE\">Official Documentation</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"halo\" src=\"../img/FAQ/halo.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "faq/maxkb_multimodal_workflow.html", "title": "Building MaxKB Multimodal Knowledge Base (Image, Audio, Video) with a Workflow Knowledge Base", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"maxkb\">Building MaxKB Multimodal Knowledge Base (Image, Audio, Video) with a Workflow Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#maxkb\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Leveraging the workflow knowledge base feature of the MaxKB open-source enterprise-grade agent platform, enterprises can build end-to-end multimodal knowledge processing pipelines, enabling business systems to automatically recognize file types and invoke the corresponding processing workflows.</p>\n<p>The system extracts structured information from multimodal files, automatically splits knowledge segments based on content logic, and stores the text along with the corresponding image, audio, and video source files in a unified way, ultimately enabling cross-modal semantic similarity retrieval so unstructured knowledge can be efficiently integrated and reused.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Solution Design<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The core of the image, audio, and video multimodal workflow knowledge base is to loop through the multiple types of files uploaded by users (image/audio/video), extract their content, and import the results into the knowledge base.</p>\n<p>The overall flow is described below:</p>\n<p>(1) File upload and initial processing: Through MaxKB’s file upload node, receive multiple types of files uploaded by users, such as images, audio, and video, and feed them into a loop node (suited to batch processing of multiple files).</p>\n<p>(2) File information extraction and type recognition: Use the parameter extraction component to extract the file’s metadata, including file_id and file_name.</p>\n<p>(3) File type routing: According to the results of the intent recognition node, apply the corresponding dedicated processing logic to different types of files, preparing for subsequent content extraction and knowledge base import.</p>\n<p>(4) File content parsing: Perform the following operations in sequence based on the file type:</p>\n<p>① If it is an image file: call the image understanding component node to return the image's visual content and text description. Then call the custom tool node to obtain the original image resource;</p>\n<p>② If it is an audio file: call the speech-to-text component node to convert the audio content into text. Then call the custom tool node to obtain the original audio resource;</p>\n<p>③ If it is a video file: call the video understanding component node to extract the combined visual and audio text information of the video. Then call the custom tool node to obtain the original video resource;</p>\n<p>④ Write a Python function, pass the above content extraction results and original resource information into the function, and aggregate them into segmented text/data structures that conform to the knowledge base import specification.</p>\n<p>(5) Knowledge base import: Invoke MaxKB’s knowledge base import node to import the data into the knowledge base, completing the file’s final processing.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"multimodal\" src=\"../img/FAQ/MaxKB%E7%9F%A5%E8%AF%86%E5%BA%93%E5%B7%A5%E4%BD%9C%E6%B5%81%E6%9E%84%E5%BB%BA%E5%A4%9A%E6%A8%A1%E6%80%81%E7%9F%A5%E8%AF%86%E5%BA%93.jpeg\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Implementation Logic<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The complete logic of MaxKB's image, audio, and video multimodal workflow knowledge base is shown in the figure below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"workflow\" src=\"../img/FAQ/workflow.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"21\">2.1 Internal Logic of the Image Workflow<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#21\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the loop body, use a function to obtain the data parameter of the extracted image file, use the image understanding node to understand the image content, and use a function to generate a directly renderable image path label for the file. Use the designated reply node to concatenate the two, use a function to integrate the extraction results with file_id and name into a standardized structure, and after segmenting them in the segment node as needed, write them into the knowledge base.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"picture\" src=\"../img/FAQ/picture_workflow.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Original Image Path Generation and Rendering Function:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>def image(data):\n\n    try:\n\n        # 1. 使用f-string将data变量嵌入到图片路径中，生成完整的Markdown图片语法字符串\n\n        markdown_img = f'![](./oss/file/{data})'\n\n        # 2. 返回包含图片字符串的列表\n\n        return markdown_img\n\n    except Exception as e:\n\n        # 3. 异常处理，返回错误信息\n\n        return [f\"【错误】处理图片URL失败：{str(e)}\"]\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Image understanding component prompt:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>请严格遵循以下步骤，分析并描述提供的图片：\n\n\n\n**第一步：全面解析图片视觉信息**\n\n*   **图片内容**：仔细识别并完整、一字不差地提取图片中的所有可见文字。不得进行任何概括、总结或删减，内容格式易读。\n\n\n\n**第二步：基于解析生成总结**\n\n*   **归纳核心主题**：根据提取的文字和视觉元素，用一句话精准概括图片的核心主题。此句话将作为你最终回复的标题。\n\n*   **说明图片目的**：结合文字与视觉内容，综合分析这张图片旨在传达的主要信息、目的或功能。\n\n\n\n**第三步：格式化输出**\n\n请将你的全部回答内容置于**一个Markdown分段**中，格式要求如下：\n\n*   将第二步中生成的“核心主题”句子，作为该分段的**一级标题**（使用一个 `#`）。\n\n*   在标题下方，依次呈现“图片内容”和“图片目的说明”作为正文内容。\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Generate the format that the \"Document Segmentation\" component can receive:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>import re\n\ndef all_content(content: str,content_name: str,content_id: str) -&gt; str:\n\n    result = [\n\n        {\n\n            'id': content_id, 'name': content_name, 'content': content\n\n        }\n\n    ]\n\n    # 添加返回语句，将构造的列表返回\n\n    return result\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"22\">2.2 Internal Logic of the Audio Workflow<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#22\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the loop body, use a function to obtain the data parameter of the audio file, use the speech-to-text node to convert the speech into text, and use a function to generate a Markdown-syntax path string for the file. Use the designated reply node to concatenate the two, use a function to integrate the extraction results with the metadata file_id and name into a standardized structure, and after segmenting them in the segment node as needed, write them into the knowledge base.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"voice\" src=\"../img/FAQ/voice_workflow.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Voice source file generation and rendering function:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>def voice(data):\n\n    try:\n\n        # 1. 使用f-string将data变量嵌入到语音路径中，生成HTML的audio标签字符串\n\n        # controls属性显示播放控件，可根据需要添加autoplay（自动播放，部分浏览器限制）等属性\n\n        audio_html = f'&lt;audio src=\"./oss/file/{data}\" controls&gt;&lt;/audio&gt;'\n\n        return audio_html\n\n    except Exception as e:\n\n        # 2. 异常处理，返回错误信息\n\n        return [f\"【错误】处理语音URL失败：{str(e)}\"]\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"23\">2.3 Internal Logic of the Video Workflow<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#23\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the loop body, use a function to obtain the data parameter of the video file, use the video understanding node to understand the video content, and use a function to generate a Markdown-syntax path string for the file. Use the designated reply node to concatenate the two, use a function to integrate the extraction results with the metadata file_id and name into a standardized structure, and after segmenting them in the segment node as needed, write them into the knowledge base.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"video\" src=\"../img/FAQ/video_workflow.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Video source file generation and rendering function:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>def video(data):\n\n    try:\n\n        # 1. 使用f-string将data变量嵌入到视频路径中，生成HTML的video标签字符串（支持本地/oss视频文件）\n\n        # controls属性表示显示播放控件，width可以根据需要调整（如100%、600px等）\n\n        video_html = f'&lt;video src=\"./oss/file/{data}\" controls width=500 height=300&gt;&lt;/video&gt;'\n\n\n\n        return video_html\n\n    except Exception as e:\n\n        # 2. 异常处理，返回错误信息\n\n        return [f\"【错误】处理视频URL失败：{str(e)}\"]\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Effect Display<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"31\">3.1 Knowledge Base Import Effect Display<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#31\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the MaxKB image, audio, and video multimodal knowledge base workflow is set up, use uploading files in the three formats of image, audio, and video as examples to verify the final implementation result.</p>\n<p>After the task is completed, go to the MaxKB knowledge base backend to check; you can observe that all three types of files achieve the complete import effect of “content extraction + source file association”.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Image file: the interpretation of the image content generated by image understanding is clearly presented in the knowledge base, with an image preview below.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"picture\" src=\"../img/FAQ/picture_result.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Audio file: Presents the complete speech-to-text result in the knowledge base, with a playable audio control displayed below.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"voice\" src=\"../img/FAQ/voice_result.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Video file: The knowledge base contains a video description and displays a fixed-size video player window, supporting basic operations such as play, pause, and progress adjustment.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"video\" src=\"../img/FAQ/video_result.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"32\">3.2 Demonstrating Application Q&amp;A Effects<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#32\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>To further verify the practical value of the multimodal knowledge base, we build a simple intelligent Q&amp;A application, link it to this multimodal knowledge base, and test the answering effect by asking questions in natural language.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"video\" src=\"../img/FAQ/qa_result.jpeg\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "faq/maxkb_multimodal_workflow.html#1", "title": "1 Solution Design ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/maxkb_multimodal_workflow.html#2", "title": "2 Implementation Logic ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/maxkb_multimodal_workflow.html#21", "title": "2.1 Internal Logic of the Image Workflow ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/maxkb_multimodal_workflow.html#22", "title": "2.2 Internal Logic of the Audio Workflow ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/maxkb_multimodal_workflow.html#23", "title": "2.3 Internal Logic of the Video Workflow ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/maxkb_multimodal_workflow.html#3", "title": "3 Effect Display ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/maxkb_multimodal_workflow.html#31", "title": "3.1 Knowledge Base Import Effect Display ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/maxkb_multimodal_workflow.html#32", "title": "3.2 Demonstrating Application Q&A Effects ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/system_management.html", "title": "System Management", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">System Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 User Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"11\">1.1 What to Do If You Forget Your Login Password<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#11\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Forgot Password for Non-admin Users</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Email binding is set: if a user has set and bound an email, they can change or recover their password through the Change Password feature on the personal information page.</li>\n<li>No email binding: If a user has not bound an email, an admin administrator can log in to the system, find the corresponding user on the User Management page, and directly change their password to help the user recover it.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>admin user forgot password</strong>: <br/>\nIf email settings have been configured, you can click 【Forgot Password】on the login page to recover your password. If email is not configured, you need to restore the password to the default password by modifying the database. The steps are as follows: <br/>\nFor online installation, enter the MaxKB container (if using the offline installation package, enter the pgsql container).</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>docker exec -it maxkb bash\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Log in to PgSQL<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>psql -Uroot\n\n</code></pre></div>Enter the MaxKB database<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>\\c maxkb;\n\n</code></pre></div>After connecting to the database, run the following SQL statement to reset the password of the admin user to MaxKB@123..<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>update  \"public\".\"user\" set password='d880e722c47a34d8e9fce789fc62389d' where username='admin';\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n<p><strong>Note: After recovering the admin password, configure an email first so that next time you forget your password you can directly use the 【Forgot Password】 feature to recover it.</strong></p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"12\">1.2 No Access Permission When Editing a User<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#12\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The gateway configuration did not allow the PUT method, resulting in a permission verification failure.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/%E6%8A%A5%E9%94%99%E6%B2%A1%E6%9C%89%E6%9D%83%E9%99%90.png\" width=\"900px\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Model Integration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"21-ollama-api\">2.1 API Base URL Invalid When Connecting Ollama<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#21-ollama-api\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/API%E5%9F%9F%E5%90%8D%E6%97%A0%E6%95%88.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>API Base URL Description</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>API Base URL format: the IP address of the service where <a href=\"http://ollama\">http://ollama</a> resides:the Ollama port number / .</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note: The API Base URL cannot use 127.0.0.1 or localhost.</strong></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Obtain the IP address of the Ollama service</strong>: <br/>\nRun ip addr on the server where Ollama is installed to obtain the server's IP address. If the Ollama server IP address is 172.26.186.35, the API Base URL is: <a href=\"http://172.26.186.53:11434\">http://172.26.186.53:11434</a></p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/%E8%8E%B7%E5%8F%96ipaddr.png\" width=\"900px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Ensure the service is accessible:</strong> <br/>\nThe MaxKB container must be able to access the Ollama service normally. Access the Ollama API Base URL in the MaxKB container and make sure it returns the 【Ollama is running】status.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/ollama%E5%8F%AF%E8%AE%BF%E9%97%AE.png\" width=\"900px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Ollama Configuration File Modification:</strong><br/></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>After confirming the above, add the Ollama model in MaxKB. <br/>\nFor installing Ollama on Windows, you can further refer to: <a href=\"https://kb.fit2cloud.com/?p=349d848b-7a0a-421b-8029-38e0440f35d4\">Tutorial for Local Deployment of Ollama + MaxKB on Windows</a>.</strong></p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"22\">2.2 Verification Failure When Connecting an Image Generation Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#22\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/%E5%9B%BE%E7%89%87%E7%94%9F%E6%88%90%E6%A8%A1%E5%9E%8B%E9%AA%8C%E8%AF%81%E5%A4%B1%E8%B4%A5.png\" width=\"900px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The cause is an incorrect parameter component type. Specifically, the \"guidance_scale\" component type is set incorrectly. The solution is to change the \"guidance_scale\" component type to a slider and set the step size to 1.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/%E8%AE%BE%E7%BD%AE%E6%AD%A5%E9%95%BF%E4%B8%BA1.png\" width=\"900px\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"23-xinference\">2.3 Verification Failure When Connecting XInference Speech Synthesis Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#23-xinference\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p><img alt=\"doc\" src=\"../img/FAQ/%E5%AF%B9%E6%8E%A5XInferenc%E8%AF%AD%E9%9F%B3%E6%A8%A1%E5%9E%8B%E5%A4%B1%E8%B4%A5.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The error message is as follows: Error code: 400 - {'detail': '[address=0.0.0.0:4215, pid=41292] Model not found, uid: XXX'}. <br/>\nThe cause may be an incorrect model name or version. Resolution steps:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check the model name: use a curl request in the container to see whether the corresponding model name is returned.</li>\n<li>Check the XInference version. If the version being used is v1.3.0.post2, this version is a test version and may be unstable. We recommend switching to a more stable version, such as the latest stable release of XInference.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"24-connection-error\">2.4 Adding a Model Fails with a Connection Error<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#24-connection-error\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>This is usually caused by network connection issues. Troubleshooting ideas:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Check the firewall settings: confirm whether the firewall restricts the relevant ports. If it does, open the port so that the container can access the network normally.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Check the container network configuration: confirm whether there is network connectivity inside the container. You can try running a network test command inside the container (such as ping or curl) to check network connectivity.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"25-balance\">2.5 Adding a Model Fails with a Balance-Related Message<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#25-balance\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Check model availability on the corresponding platform to ensure the model has balance available for calls.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"26-str-object-has-no-attribute-model_dump-invalid-api-key-provided\">2.6 Error When Adding a Model: 'str' object has no attribute 'model_dump' or Invalid API-key provided<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#26-str-object-has-no-attribute-model_dump-invalid-api-key-provided\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Verify the API Base URL and key: ensure the API Base URL is available and correctly configured, and the corresponding API Key is valid and has sufficient permissions. If it is a third-party proxy service, you may need to contact its provider to confirm service status and configuration requirements.</p>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "faq/system_management.html#1", "title": "1 User Management ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/system_management.html#11", "title": "1.1 What to Do If You Forget Your Login Password ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/system_management.html#12", "title": "1.2 No Access Permission When Editing a User ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/system_management.html#2", "title": "2 Model Integration ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/system_management.html#21-ollama-api", "title": "2.1 API Base URL Invalid When Connecting Ollama ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/system_management.html#22", "title": "2.2 Verification Failure When Connecting an Image Generation Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/system_management.html#23-xinference", "title": "2.3 Verification Failure When Connecting XInference Speech Synthesis Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/system_management.html#24-connection-error", "title": "2.4 Adding a Model Fails with a Connection Error ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/system_management.html#25-balance", "title": "2.5 Adding a Model Fails with a Balance-Related Message ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/system_management.html#26-str-object-has-no-attribute-model_dump-invalid-api-key-provided", "title": "2.6 Error When Adding a Model: 'str' object has no attribute 'model_dump' or Invalid API-key provided ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/wps_contract_review.html", "title": "Design and Implementation of the WPS Contract Review Assistant", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Design and Implementation of the WPS Contract Review Assistant</h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The specific method of connecting WPS Office through the MaxKB open-source agent platform to build an 'Intelligent Contract Review Assistant'.</p>\n<p>By integrating enterprise contract knowledge base capabilities directly into the daily office environment, contract review is transformed from a manual process that once took days into an intelligent operation completed in minutes, greatly improving the efficiency and accuracy of contract review while keeping review standards consistent.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Solution Design<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The core of the MaxKB WPS Contract Review workflow is to implement categorized knowledge base selection, document preprocessing, and real-time pushing of the review results using SSE (Server-Sent Events) technology.</p>\n<p>Users configure and publish a contract review workflow in MaxKB in advance, then install the MaxKB WPS plugin in WPS and connect to the contract review workflow to achieve efficient contract review within WPS.</p>\n<p>The overall flow is described below:</p>\n<p>(1) Configuration Management: On first use, the user configures the MaxKB service address, APP Key, and salesperson name;</p>\n<p>(2) Category Selection: Select the corresponding knowledge base based on the contract's product line (e.g., DataEase, JumpServer, etc.) and type (subscription, authorization, maintenance, etc.);</p>\n<p>(3) Document Preprocessing: Automatically accept all tracked changes and remove comments to ensure the document is clean;</p>\n<p>(4) Export PDF: Add a timestamp suffix to the filename and convert the Word document to PDF format;</p>\n<p>(5) Upload File: Upload the PDF file to the MaxKB file service;</p>\n<p>(6) Intelligent Review: The MaxKB agent uses the selected category to call the corresponding enterprise knowledge base for contract analysis;</p>\n<p>(7) Streaming Response: Use SSE technology to push review results in real time so users can watch the analysis process;</p>\n<p>(8) Real-Time Rendering: Render the returned Markdown content in real time and display it in the task pane;</p>\n<p>(9) Export Report: Generate a professional PDF report from the review results and save it in the same directory as the original contract;</p>\n<p>(10) Restore Document: Delete temporary files and reopen the original contract document.</p>\n<p>The MaxKB WPS Contract Review Assistant is implemented with a front-end/back-end separated architecture, where the front-end handles document processing and interface display and the back-end provides the AI review service.\nAfter the user uploads a file on the front-end, the document undergoes document merging, PDF conversion, parsing, classifier categorization, and more in MaxKB. It is then reviewed by AI combined with the knowledge base retrieval results. Finally the review result is returned to the front-end and the rendered result is presented to the user.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"wps_contract\" src=\"../img/FAQ/MaxKB%20WPS%E5%90%88%E5%90%8C%E5%AE%A1%E6%A0%B8%E5%8A%A9%E6%89%8B%E6%9E%B6%E6%9E%84%E5%9B%BE.jpeg\"/>\n<img alt=\"wps_contract\" src=\"../img/FAQ/MaxKB%E5%90%88%E5%90%8C%E5%AE%A1%E6%A0%B8%E5%91%A8%E6%89%8B%E5%B7%A5%E4%BD%9C%E6%B5%81.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Plugin Installation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"21-macos\">2.1 macOS Operating System<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#21-macos\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Open a terminal and run the following command:\n'''\ncurl -sSL <a href=\"https://east.dataease.cn/maxkb_wps_quick_start.sh\">https://east.dataease.cn/maxkb_wps_quick_start.sh</a> | bash\n'''</p>\n<p>This script will automatically download and install the plugin to the WPS plugin directory: ~/Library/Containers/com.kingsoft.wpsoffice.mac/Data/.kingsoft/wps/jsaddons.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"wps_contract\" src=\"../img/FAQ/macOS_MaxKB%20WPS%E6%8F%92%E4%BB%B6%E5%AE%89%E8%A3%85.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"22-windows\">2.2 Windows Operating System<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#22-windows\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Download the plugin from the web page: <a href=\"https://maxkb-tools-1323865188.cos.ap-guangzhou.myqcloud.com/maxkb-wps.exe\">https://maxkb-tools-1323865188.cos.ap-guangzhou.myqcloud.com/maxkb-wps.exe</a>.</p>\n<p>After running, the plugin will be automatically installed to: C:\\Users${Your_Name}\\AppData\\Roaming\\kingsoft\\wps\\jsaddons.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"wps_contract\" src=\"../img/FAQ/Windows_MaxKB%20WPS%E6%8F%92%E4%BB%B6%E5%AE%89%E8%A3%85.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Implementation Steps and Effect Display<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>With the MaxKB WPS Contract Review Assistant, users can complete contract review work that previously took hours in just a few minutes. The following are the detailed operation steps and effect description:</p>\n<p>(1) Configuration System</p>\n<p>On first use, find the “MaxKB WPS Plugin” option in the toolbar at the top of WPS, then click the “Contract Review” button. In the toolbar on the right side of the page, click the gear icon in the top-right corner to configure initialization, and fill in the review information such as the MaxKB service’s Base URL, APP Key, and salesperson name.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Base URL: the MaxKB service address</li>\n<li>APP Key: the application-level authentication key</li>\n<li>Salesperson name: Reviewer information</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"wps_contract\" src=\"../img/FAQ/MaxKB%20WPS%E6%8F%92%E4%BB%B6%E8%8F%9C%E5%8D%95.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"wps_contract\" src=\"../img/FAQ/MaxKB%20WPS%E5%88%9D%E5%A7%8B%E5%8C%96_01.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"wps_contract\" src=\"../img/FAQ/MaxKB%20WPS%E5%88%9D%E5%A7%8B%E5%8C%96_02.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>(2) Select Contract Category</p>\n<p>Select the corresponding knowledge base based on the contract content: first select the product line (such as DataEase, MaxKB, etc.), then select the contract type (such as subscription, authorization, maintenance, etc.).</p>\n<p>The system automatically matches the corresponding Knowledge Base based on the selected category, ensuring the review logic is consistent with enterprise standards.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"wps_contract\" src=\"../img/FAQ/WPS%E5%90%88%E5%90%8C%E5%AE%A1%E6%A0%B8%E5%8A%A9%E6%89%8B%E7%9F%A5%E8%AF%86%E5%BA%93%E9%80%89%E6%8B%A9.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>(3) One-Click Review</p>\n<p>Upload a contract file, and the system automatically completes document preprocessing (such as accepting revisions and deleting comments), exports the PDF file, calls the agent to analyze the contract, and displays the review results in real time.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"wps_contract\" src=\"../img/FAQ/MaxKB%20WPS%E5%90%88%E5%90%8C%E5%AE%A1%E6%A0%B8%E5%8A%A9%E6%89%8B%E5%AE%A1%E6%A0%B8%E7%BB%93%E6%9E%9C%E5%B1%95%E7%A4%BA.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>(4) View Review Report</p>\n<p>After the review is completed, the system displays the complete review report in the task pane, including:</p>\n<p>■ Review overview: the basic contract information, reviewers, and review time;</p>\n<p>■ Risk assessment: high-risk, medium-risk, and low-risk clauses;</p>\n<p>■ Clause analysis: review the contract clauses one by one and flag potential issues;</p>\n<p>■ Compliance check: compare against enterprise standards and point out non-compliant items;</p>\n<p>■ Revision suggestions: specific revision opinions and reference text.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"wps_contract\" src=\"../img/FAQ/MaxKB%20WPS%E5%90%88%E5%90%8C%E5%AE%A1%E6%A0%B8%E5%8A%A9%E6%89%8B%E5%AE%A1%E6%A0%B8%E6%8A%A5%E5%91%8A.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>(5) Export PDF Report</p>\n<p>The system automatically exports the review report as a PDF file and saves it in the same directory as the original contract. The specifications followed by the PDF report include:</p>\n<p>■ File name format: OriginalContractName_ContractReviewResult_20241210_153045.pdf</p>\n<p>■ Full format preservation: Markdown format, tables, lists, etc.;</p>\n<p>■ Intelligent pagination: prevent headings, tables, and code blocks from being truncated.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"wps_contract\" src=\"../img/FAQ/MaxKB%20WPS%E5%90%88%E5%90%8C%E5%AE%A1%E6%A0%B8%E5%8A%A9%E6%89%8B%E5%AE%A1%E6%A0%B8%E6%8A%A5%E5%91%8A%E5%AF%BC%E5%87%BA.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "faq/wps_contract_review.html#1", "title": "1 Solution Design ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/wps_contract_review.html#2", "title": "2 Plugin Installation ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/wps_contract_review.html#21-macos", "title": "2.1 macOS Operating System ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/wps_contract_review.html#22-windows", "title": "2.2 Windows Operating System ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "faq/wps_contract_review.html#3", "title": "3 Implementation Steps and Effect Display ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/1panel_installtion.html", "title": "1Panel Installation", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>1Panel Installation</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-1panel\">1 Install 1Panel<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1-1panel\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For the installation, deployment, and basic feature introduction of 1Panel, please refer to <a href=\"https://1panel.cn/docs/\">1Panel Official Documentation</a>. After completing the 1Panel installation and deployment, open a browser and visit the prompted URL to enter 1Panel; the interface is shown below.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"1panel\" src=\"../img/index/1panel.jpg\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2-maxkb\">2 Install MaxKB<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2-maxkb\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Go to the app store application list and find the MaxKB application under the [AI/Large Model] category to install it.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"1panel-maxkb\" src=\"../img/index/1panel_maxkb.jpg\"/> </p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Configure the MaxKB application parameters on the installation page:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Name: the name of the MaxKB application you want to create.</li>\n<li>Version: select the MaxKB version.</li>\n<li>Port: the service port of the MaxKB application.</li>\n<li>Container Name: the name of the MaxKB application container.</li>\n<li>CPU Limit: the number of CPU cores that the MaxKB application can use.</li>\n<li>Memory Limit: the amount of memory available to the MaxKB application.</li>\n<li>External port access: The MaxKB application can be accessed using IP:PORT (the MaxKB application must check the external port access option).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"maxkb-setting\" src=\"../img/index/maxkb_setting.jpg\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click Confirm to start the installation. The page will automatically jump to the installed application list and wait for the MaxKB application status to become Started.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"MaxKB Startup\" src=\"../img/index/maxkb-start.jpg\"/> </p>\n<h2 id=\"3-maxkb\">3 Access MaxKB<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3-maxkb\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After installation is complete, log in to MaxKB by visiting the following page in your browser:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>地址: http://目标服务器IP地址:服务运行端口（默认 8080）     \n\n用户名: admin    \n\n密码: MaxKB@123..\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>For security, admin is required to change the default password on first login. After changing the password, you can log in to the system again to use MaxKB.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Logged in\" src=\"../img/index/login.jpg\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "installation/1panel_installtion.html#1-1panel", "title": "1 Install 1Panel ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/1panel_installtion.html#2-maxkb", "title": "2 Install MaxKB ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/1panel_installtion.html#3-maxkb", "title": "3 Access MaxKB ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/aliyun.html", "title": "Cloud Marketplace Deployment Guide", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Cloud Marketplace Deployment Guide<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>This guide covers how to purchase, deploy, and use the <strong>MaxKB</strong> image through the Alibaba Cloud Marketplace, and provides a discounted link for purchasing a server.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Purchase Image<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>MaxKB is now available on the Alibaba Cloud Marketplace. You can purchase the image directly via the following link:\n<a href=\"https://market.aliyun.com/products/53690006/cmjj00067609.html?userCode=kmemb8jp\">MaxKB Cloud Marketplace Purchase Link</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>You can also purchase an Alibaba Cloud server yourself and search for <strong>MaxKB</strong> when selecting an image, so you can quickly select an image for deployment.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> When purchasing, choose an appropriate instance specification; 4C/8G or higher is recommended.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Server Discounts</p>\n<p>If you do not have a server yet, you can purchase an Alibaba Cloud server through the following promotional link:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://market.aliyun.com/common/dashi/maxkb?userCode=kmemb8jp\">Exclusive Alibaba Cloud deal link: 45% off</a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Start Service<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the image is started, you can access the following address in your browser to log in to MaxKB:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>服务访问地址: http://服务器IP:8080\n\n默认用户名: admin\n\n默认密码: MaxKB@123..\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>After your first login, it is recommended to change your password promptly and perform other security settings.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Opening Ports<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>To ensure that the MaxKB service can be accessed from outside, you need to open port <code>8080</code> in the security group rules of the Alibaba Cloud server.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>For the specific setup steps, please refer to Alibaba Cloud's <a href=\"https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/25471.html\">Port Allowlist Tutorial</a>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "installation/aliyun.html#1", "title": "1 Purchase Image ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/aliyun.html#2", "title": "2 Start Service ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/aliyun.html#3", "title": "3 Opening Ports ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/backup.html", "title": "Backup & Restore", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Backup &amp; Restore <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After installing MaxKB, the distribution paths of the related files are as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>/opt/maxkb: The default runtime path, which can be set during installation. It mainly stores the configuration files required by MaxKB at runtime and the data generated at runtime, including log files and more.</li>\n<li>/usr/bin: The docker and docker-compose executables are placed in this directory by default.</li>\n<li>/usr/local/bin/mkctl: MaxKB's command line tool</li>\n<li>/var/lib/docker: Docker images are loaded here by default</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In summary, backing up MaxKB mainly requires backing up the running path, such as the /opt/maxkb directory. The restore steps are as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>This method is applicable to the migration of the same version of MaxKB. In the new environment, please install the same version of MaxKB and select the same configuration parameters during installation.</li>\n<li>Stop the MaxKB service by running the command: mkctl stop</li>\n<li>Overwrite the /opt/maxkb directory in the new environment with the entire /opt/maxkb directory from the original environment.</li>\n<li>Start the MaxKB service in the new environment: mkctl restart</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "installation/cli.html", "title": "Command Line Tool", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Command Line Tool</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-mkctl\">1 mkctl Command<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1-mkctl\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The MaxKB offline installation package comes with the command-line operations tool mkctl by default. By executing <code>mkctl help</code>, you can view the related command descriptions.</p>\n<p><strong>Description</strong>: When installing via Online Installation or the 1Panel method, the mkctl command is not built in.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>Usage:\n\nmkctl [COMMAND] [ARGS...]\n\nmkctl --help\n\n\n\nCommands: \n\nstatus              查看 MaxKB 服务运行状态\n\nstart               启动 MaxKB 服务\n\nstop                停止 MaxKB 服务\n\nrestart             重启 MaxKB 服务\n\nreload              重新加载 MaxKB 服务\n\nuninstall           卸载 MaxKB 服务（不会删除数据）\n\nversion             查看 MaxKB 版本信息\n\nclear-images        清理 MaxKB 旧版本的相关镜像\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "installation/cli.html#1-mkctl", "title": "1 mkctl Command ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html", "title": "Migration Tool", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Migration Tool<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Migration Notes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"11\">1.1 Migration Path<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#11\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: For v1, you must first upgrade to <strong>v1.10.10-lts</strong> or a later version, and then use the Migration Tool to migrate to <strong>v2.1.0</strong>. The migrated v2 version is <strong>v2.1.0</strong>, after which you can upgrade to a higher v2 version.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"migrate\" src=\"../img/index/migrate_route.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"12\">1.2 Notes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#12\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>This tool is a migration tool used to migrate data from v1 1.10.10-lts and later versions to v2.1.0, not a direct upgrade tool;</li>\n<li>This tool only supports data migration from v1 1.10.10-lts and later versions to v2.1.0;</li>\n<li>The target environment for data migration must be v2.1.0 and must not contain any data (except the license);</li>\n<li>Before migration, please stop any operations in the v1 environment to avoid incomplete data migration.</li>\n<li>Before migration, be sure to check the disk space and ensure there is enough storage space before and after data export and import.</li>\n<li>During migration, ensure that both the v1 and v2 containers are running normally (no need to stop services).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Migration Tool Download<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Open the <a href=\"https://github.com/1Panel-dev/MaxKB-v1-to-v2-migrator\">MaxKB Migration Tool Download</a> page, download the latest version of the tool, and upload it to the deployment server.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"migrate\" src=\"../img/index/migrate_step.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Migration Operation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"31-linuxmacos\">3.1 Linux/macOS Systems<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#31-linuxmacos\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<h4 id=\"311\">3.1.1 Exporting Data<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#311\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>On a machine running v1.10.10-lts or a later version, download MaxKB-v1-to-v2-migrator-&lt;version&gt;.zip, unzip it, enter the directory, and run the following command to export the v1 data.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If v1 contains a large amount of data, the export process will take some time; please be patient.</li>\n<li>After the export is complete, a migrate.zip will be generated in MaxKB-v1-to-v2-migrator-&lt;version&gt;.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>unzip MaxKB-v1-to-v2-migrator-&lt;version&gt;.zip \n\n\n\ncd  MaxKB-v1-to-v2-migrator-&lt;version&gt;\n\n\n\nbash export_v1_data.sh &lt;v1_container_name&gt;\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"v1 Data Export\" src=\"../img/index/migrate_linux_export.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Copy MaxKB-v1-to-v2-migrator-&lt;version&gt; to the machine where v2.1.0 is installed.</p>\n</div>\n<h4 id=\"312\">3.1.2 Importing Data<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#312\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>On the v2.1.0 machine, ensure that the v2.1.0 container has been started and contains no other data, <strong>The Professional Edition requires importing a license in advance.</strong>.</p>\n<p>Enter the migration tool directory and run the following command to import the data into v2.1.0.<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>cd MaxKB-v1-to-v2-migrator-&lt;version&gt;\n\n\n\nbash import_v2_data.sh &lt;v2_container_name&gt;\n\n</code></pre></div><strong>Note</strong>: The v1 Community Edition can only be migrated to the v2 Community Edition, and the v1 Professional Edition can only be migrated to the v2 Professional Edition; in addition, both the v1 and v2 Professional Editions must have a valid license.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Import on Linux\" src=\"../img/index/migrate_linux_import.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After a successful import, restart the MaxKB service.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Import on Linux\" src=\"../img/index/migrate_linux_import1.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"32-windows\">3.2 Windows System<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#32-windows\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<h4 id=\"321\">3.2.1 Operational Requirements<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#321\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supported Operating Systems:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows 10</li>\n<li>Windows 11</li>\n<li>Windows Server 2016 and above</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Prerequisites:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Docker Desktop for Windows is installed;</li>\n<li>The MaxKB v1 and v2 containers are running;</li>\n<li>For PowerShell scripts, PowerShell 5.0 or later is required.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h4 id=\"322\">3.2.2 Exporting Data<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#322\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>On Windows systems, MaxKB provides PowerShell scripts (.ps1) to export data from v1 1.10.10-lts and later versions. Download and unzip the migration tool, open the migration directory as an administrator in the terminal, and run the command to export v1 data.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If v1 contains a large amount of data, the export process will take some time; please be patient.</li>\n<li>After the export is complete, a migrate.zip will be generated in MaxKB-v1-to-v2-migrator-&lt;version&gt;.<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># PowerShell 脚本\n\n.\\export_v1_data.ps1 -ContainerName &lt;v1_container_name&gt;\n\n</code></pre></div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Export on Windows\" src=\"../img/index/migrate_windows_export.png\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"323\">3.2.3 Importing Data<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#323\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>On the v2.1.0 machine, ensure that the v2.1.0 container has been started and contains no other data, <strong>The Professional Edition requires importing a license in advance.</strong>.<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>#PowerShell 脚本\n\n.\\import_v2_data.ps1 -ContainerName &lt;v2_container_name&gt;\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: The v1 Community Edition can only be migrated to the v2 Community Edition, and the v1 Professional Edition can only be migrated to the v2 Professional Edition; in addition, both the v1 and v2 Professional Editions must have a valid license.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Export on Windows\" src=\"../img/index/migrate_windows_import.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Migration Change Notes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"41\">4.1 Users<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#41\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>If the user's 【Name】 is empty in v1, after migration the 【Username】 will automatically be used as the 【Name】;</li>\n<li>Resources in a workspace are queried by Name;</li>\n<li>The admin account is granted by default the System Administrator, Workspace Administrator, and Regular User permissions (X-Pack);</li>\n<li>Except for admin, system users or other user types will have the default role of Regular User after migration (X-Pack).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"42\">4.2 Resources<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#42\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>Applications/knowledge bases that v1 authorized to other members are granted the corresponding permissions after migration;</li>\n<li>The creator of a resource has the permission to manage that resource.</li>\n<li>After migrating the v1 function library, the creator has management permission in Tools, while other users are in an unauthorized state by default;</li>\n<li>After public models are migrated, by default all regular users are granted view permission via resource authorization, while the creator is granted management permission.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"43\">4.3 Interfaces<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#43\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>The interface documentation of v1 and v2 are inconsistent; if there are API calls, they need to be reconfigured;</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"44\">4.4 Application Integration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#44\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>The callback URLs of applications integrated with WeCom and so on will change, and the app integration and login authentication (QR code login) need to be reconfigured (X-Pack);</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"45\">4.5 Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#45\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>Since documents uploaded to the knowledge base in v1 did not save the original document, after migrating to v2, the corresponding knowledge base documents do not support the 【Download Original Document】 feature.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#1", "title": "1 Migration Notes ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#11", "title": "1.1 Migration Path ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#12", "title": "1.2 Notes ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#2", "title": "2 Migration Tool Download ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#3", "title": "3 Migration Operation ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#31-linuxmacos", "title": "3.1 Linux/macOS Systems ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#311", "title": "3.1.1 Exporting Data ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#312", "title": "3.1.2 Importing Data ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#32-windows", "title": "3.2 Windows System ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#321", "title": "3.2.1 Operational Requirements ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#322", "title": "3.2.2 Exporting Data ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#323", "title": "3.2.3 Importing Data ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#4", "title": "4 Migration Change Notes ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#41", "title": "4.1 Users ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#42", "title": "4.2 Resources ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#43", "title": "4.3 Interfaces ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#44", "title": "4.4 Application Integration ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/migrate.html#45", "title": "4.5 Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/offline_installtion.html", "title": "Offline Installation (Recommended for Production)", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Offline Installation (Recommended for Production)</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Deployment Requirements<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For production environments, offline installation is the officially recommended installation method.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"11\">1.1 Server Configuration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#11\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Deployment server requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Operating System: Ubuntu 22.04 / CentOS 7 (kernel version requirement ≥ 3.10)</li>\n<li>CPU/Memory: 4C/8GB or above</li>\n<li>Disk Space: 100GB</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tip: An outdated Docker version may cause the installation to fail. It is recommended to use the Docker bundled with the installer, or Docker v26.0.0 or later.</strong></p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"12\">1.2 Port Requirements<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#12\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The access ports that need to be opened for offline deployment of MaxKB are described below:</p>\n</div>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Port</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Purpose</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>22</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">SSH</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">Installation, Upgrade, and Management</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8080</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">Web Service Port</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">The default Web service access port, which can be changed as needed.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Installer Download<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Open the <a href=\"https://community.fit2cloud.com/#/products/maxkb/downloads\">FIT2CLOUD Open-Source Community MaxKB Community Edition Download</a> page, download the latest version of the installation package, and upload it to the deployment server (using v2.0.0 as an example to illustrate the installation and deployment process).</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Installation &amp; Deployment<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"31\">3.1 Unpacking the Installation Package<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#31\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Log in to the deployment server as the root user via the SSH protocol and decompress the installation package:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>tar -zxvf maxkb-v2.0.0-x86_64-offline-installer.tar.gz\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"32\">3.2 Installing and Configuring (Optional)<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#32\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Information such as the MaxKB installation directory, service port, and database configuration can be configured in the install.conf file after extracting the installation package.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 基础配置\n\n## 安装目录\n\nMAXKB_BASE=/opt\n\n## 服务端口\n\nMAXKB_PORT=8080\n\n## docker 网段设置\n\nMAXKB_DOCKER_SUBNET=172.31.250.192/26\n\n\n\n# 数据库配置\n\n## 是否使用外部数据库\n\nMAXKB_EXTERNAL_PGSQL=false\n\n## 数据库地址\n\nMAXKB_PGSQL_HOST=pgsql\n\n## 数据库端口\n\nMAXKB_PGSQL_PORT=5432\n\n## 数据库库名\n\nMAXKB_PGSQL_DB=maxkb\n\n## 数据库用户名\n\nMAXKB_PGSQL_USER=root\n\n## 数据库密码\n\nMAXKB_PGSQL_PASSWORD=Password123@postgres\n\n\n\n# Redis配置\n\n## 是否使用外部Redis\n\nMAXKB_EXTERNAL_REDIS=false\n\n## Redis地址\n\nREDIS_HOST=redis\n\n## Redis端口\n\nREDIS_PORT=6379\n\n## Redis数据库\n\nREDIS_DB=0\n\n## Redis密码\n\nREDIS_PASSWORD=Password123@redis\n\n\n\n# 镜像配置\n\n## 镜像仓库\n\nMAXKB_IMAGE_REPOSITORY=registry.fit2cloud.com/maxkb\n\n## 镜像名称\n\nMAXKB_IMAGE=maxkb\n\n## 版本号\n\nMAXKB_VERSION=v2.0.0\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Before the first installation, you can modify the parameters in the install.conf file; during installation, the installation is performed according to the modified parameters. If you need to modify the configuration parameters again after installation, you must modify them in the ${MAXKB_BASE}/maxkb/.env (default is /opt/maxkb/.env) file, and after modification you must run the <code>mkctl reload</code> command to reload the configuration file.</li>\n<li>MAXKB_PGSQL_PORT and REDIS_PORT only apply when using an external database; if you use the built-in database, do not modify them.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"33\">3.3 Running the Installation Script<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#33\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 进入安装包解压缩后目录  \n\ncd maxkb-v2.0.0-x86_64-offline-installer\n\n\n\n# 执行安装命令\n\nbash install.sh\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Install\" src=\"../img/index/install.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Logging In and Accessing<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After all container statuses display <code>healthy</code>, you can access address <code>http://目标服务器 IP 地址:8080</code> via a browser and log in to MaxKB with the default administrator username and password.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>用户名：admin\n\n默认密码：MaxKB@123..\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Log In\" src=\"../img/index/login.jpg\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"5\">5 Offline Upgrade<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Note: Please <a href=\"backup\">Perform a backup.</a> the data before upgrading.</strong></p>\n<p>Offline upgrade is basically the same process as installation: download the new version's installation package, upload and extract it, then run the installation command again to upgrade.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 进入新版本目录\n\ncd maxkb-v2.x.y-offline\n\n\n\n# 运行安装脚本\n\nbash install.sh\n\n\n\n# 查看 MaxKB 运行状态\n\nmkctl status\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "installation/offline_installtion.html#1", "title": "1 Deployment Requirements ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/offline_installtion.html#11", "title": "1.1 Server Configuration ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/offline_installtion.html#12", "title": "1.2 Port Requirements ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/offline_installtion.html#2", "title": "2 Installer Download ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/offline_installtion.html#3", "title": "3 Installation & Deployment ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/offline_installtion.html#31", "title": "3.1 Unpacking the Installation Package ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/offline_installtion.html#32", "title": "3.2 Installing and Configuring (Optional) ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/offline_installtion.html#33", "title": "3.3 Running the Installation Script ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/offline_installtion.html#4", "title": "4 Logging In and Accessing ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/offline_installtion.html#5", "title": "5 Offline Upgrade ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/online_installtion.html", "title": "Online Installation", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Online Installation</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Deployment Requirements<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For production environments, offline installation is the officially recommended installation method.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"11\">1.1 Server Configuration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#11\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Deployment server requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Operating System: Ubuntu 22.04 / CentOS 7 (kernel version requirement ≥ 3.10)</li>\n<li>CPU/Memory: 4C/8GB or above</li>\n<li>Disk Space: 100GB</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tip: An outdated Docker version may cause the installation to fail. It is recommended to use the Docker bundled with the installer, or Docker v26.0.0 or later.</strong></p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"12\">1.2 Port Requirements<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#12\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The access ports that need to be opened for the online deployment of MaxKB are described as follows:</p>\n</div>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Port</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Purpose</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>22</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">SSH</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">Installation, Upgrade, and Management</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8080</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">Web Service Port</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">The default Web service access port, which can be changed as needed.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Online Quick Deployment<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>On an operating system with a Docker environment configured, you only need to run the following command to install MaxKB with one click:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># Linux 操作系统\n\ndocker run -d --name=maxkb --restart=always -p 8080:8080 -v ~/.maxkb:/opt/maxkb registry.fit2cloud.com/maxkb/maxkb\n\n\n\n# Windows 操作系统\n\ndocker run -d --name=maxkb --restart=always -p 8080:8080 -v C:/maxkb:/opt/maxkb registry.fit2cloud.com/maxkb/maxkb\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n<p>After all container statuses display <code>healthy</code>, you can access MaxKB via a browser:<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>http://目标服务器 IP 地址:8080\n\n\n\n默认登录信息\n\n用户名：admin\n\n默认密码：MaxKB@123..\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Online Upgrade<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Note: Please <a href=\"backup\">Perform a backup.</a> the data before upgrading.</strong></p>\n<p>Perform the upgrade by following the steps below in order:</p>\n<p>(1) Download the latest image<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>docker pull registry.fit2cloud.com/maxkb/maxkb\n\n</code></pre></div>(2) View and confirm the previous data persistence directory, then copy and save it.<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>docker inspect maxkb\n\n</code></pre></div></p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Obtain the pgsql directory\" src=\"../img/index/mount_pgsqldir2.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>(3) Delete the running old-version MaxKB container.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>docker rm -f maxkb \n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(4) Start and run the new-version MaxKB container.</p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Make sure the data persistence directory (i.e., the directory after -v in the command line) is consistent with the directory you viewed in step (2); otherwise, all system data will be empty after startup.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code> docker run -d --name=maxkb --restart=always -p 8080:8080 -v ~/.maxkb:/opt/maxkb registry.fit2cloud.com/maxkb/maxkb\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "installation/online_installtion.html#1", "title": "1 Deployment Requirements ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/online_installtion.html#11", "title": "1.1 Server Configuration ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/online_installtion.html#12", "title": "1.2 Port Requirements ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/online_installtion.html#2", "title": "2 Online Quick Deployment ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/online_installtion.html#3", "title": "3 Online Upgrade ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "installation/tencent.html", "title": "Cloud Application Deployment Guide", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Cloud Application Deployment Guide<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>This guide covers how to quickly install the <strong>MaxKB</strong> cloud application in Tencent Cloud.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Install Application<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The MaxKB Community Edition is now available as a Tencent Cloud cloud application and can be quickly deployed directly on Tencent Cloud servers.</p>\n<p>Step 1: Associate our Tencent Cloud partner account to enjoy more benefits: <a href=\"https://partner.cloud.tencent.com/invitation/10002820907763620ace838b1?inviteType=2\">Click the link to associate</a></p>\n<p>Step 2: Open <a href=\"https://app.cloud.tencent.com/detail/SPU_BHDJDDBHBE5864\">MaxKB Cloud Application</a> directly.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Tencent Cloud App\" src=\"../img/index/maxkb_app_cloud.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Step 3: Select appropriate cloud resource configuration. After clicking [Install App], configure the cloud resource settings; a specification of at least 4C8G or higher is recommended.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Application Resources\" src=\"../img/index/app_resource.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Application Resources\" src=\"../img/index/app_resource2.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Step 4: Install and start. Click [Install App], wait for the backend installation and service startup. Once startup is complete, click [Open App], and you can log in to MaxKB using the default administrator user and password.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>用户名：admin\n\n默认密码：MaxKB@123..\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Install\" src=\"../img/index/open_maxkb_app.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "installation/tencent.html#1", "title": "1 Install Application ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/Customlanguage.html", "title": "Custom Language Pack", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Custom Language Pack<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"_2\">1. Language Pack Format Specifications<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB v2.10.0-lts supports custom international language packs. Language packs are uniformly in ZIP archive format and have strict naming and file structure specifications. All file names must remain consistent, otherwise the language pack will not take effect.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"11\">1.1 Naming Rules<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#11\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>1. Overall language pack archive name: international-language-code.zip</p>\n<p>2. The archive must contain two files: 国际语言代码.json, 国际语言代码.po</p>\n<p>3. Core requirement: the ZIP archive name, the JSON file name, and the PO file name must be identical.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"12\">1.2 Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#12\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Taking German as an example, the international language code for German is de:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>- 语言包压缩包：de.zip\n\n\n\n- 包内文件：de.json、de.po\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"13\">1.3 How to Look Up Language Codes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#13\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The standard international language code for the target language (ISO 639 language code) can be obtained from the official query website: <a href=\"https://www.udtool.com/toolbox/langcodes.html\">https://www.udtool.com/toolbox/langcodes.html</a></p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"_3\">2. Steps for Creating a Custom Language Pack<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB provides a Chinese language pack by default. The language pack is <a href=\"https://maxkb-apps-1323865188.cos.ap-shanghai.myqcloud.com/zh.zip\">Custom Language Pack</a>. You can quickly create any international language pack based on the Chinese language pack. The specific steps are as follows:</p>\n<p>Step 1: Look up the target language code</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>打开上方语言代码查询网址，查找需要适配的目标语言对应的纯字母国际语言代码（如英语：en、日语：ja、韩语：ko）。\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Step 2: Extract and translate the source language pack</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>解压 MaxKB 原始中文语言包，复制包内的 zh.json 和 zh.po 源文件，将文件内所有中文文本逐条翻译为目标语言文本，保证语义准确、适配系统界面场景。\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Step 3: Rename the language pack file</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>将翻译完成的两个文件，重命名为目标语言国际代码格式，严格遵循命名规范：\n\n\n\n原文件：zh.json、zh.po\n\n\n\n修改后：xx.json、xx.po（xx 为目标语言代码）\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Step 4: Package to generate the custom language pack</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>将重命名后的 xx.json、xx.po 两个文件，压缩为同名 ZIP 压缩包，最终生成 xx.zip 格式的自定义语言包。\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"_4\">3. Methods for Deploying and Installing Language Packs<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the custom language pack is created, it must be placed in the language pack directory specified by MaxKB. There are two scenarios: native deployment and Docker container deployment.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"31\">3.1 Native Deployment (Direct Server Installation)<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#31\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>1. Enter the language pack folder in the MaxKB installation directory; the default path is /opt/maxkb/local/locales</p>\n<p>2. If the directory does not exist, you can create it manually: mkdir -p /opt/maxkb/local/locales</p>\n<p>3. Place the prepared xx.zip custom language pack into this directory.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"32-docker\">3.2 Docker Image Deployment<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#32-docker\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Docker deployment requires directory mapping to sync the host machine language pack to a specified directory inside the container, as follows:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"mf\">1</span><span class=\"err\">、</span><span class=\"n\">在宿主机创建语言包目录</span><span class=\"err\">（</span><span class=\"n\">可自定义路径</span><span class=\"err\">），</span><span class=\"n\">放入自定义语言包</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ZIP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">文件</span>\n\n\n\n<span class=\"mf\">2</span><span class=\"err\">、</span><span class=\"n\">启动</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">重启容器时</span><span class=\"err\">，</span><span class=\"n\">添加目录挂载参数</span><span class=\"err\">，</span><span class=\"n\">将宿主机目录映射至容器内</span><span class=\"err\">：</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">容器固定语言包路径</span><span class=\"err\">：</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">opt</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">maxkb</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">local</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">locales</span>\n\n\n\n<span class=\"mf\">3</span><span class=\"err\">、</span><span class=\"n\">若容器内无</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">opt</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">maxkb</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">local</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">locales</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">目录</span><span class=\"err\">，</span><span class=\"n\">可进入容器手动创建</span>\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"_5\">4. How It Takes Effect<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the language pack is placed, you must restart the MaxKB service. After the restart, you can select and use the custom international language in the language switching option in the MaxKB system backend.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Custom Language Pack\" src=\"../../img/language/change.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Custom Language Pack\" src=\"../../img/language/qiehuan.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"_6\">5. Precautions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_6\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Make sure the archive, JSON file, and PO file have exactly the same name, including a consistent case; otherwise, the language pack cannot be recognized.</p>\n<p>Only standard ISO 639 international language codes are supported; non-standard codes cannot be customized.</p>\n<p>The translated content must adapt to scenarios such as the system interface, buttons, and prompt text to avoid semantic confusion</p>\n<p>When deploying with Docker, make sure the directory mount takes effect, otherwise the container cannot read the custom language pack.</p>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/Customlanguage.html#_2", "title": "1. Language Pack Format Specifications ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/Customlanguage.html#11", "title": "1.1 Naming Rules ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/Customlanguage.html#12", "title": "1.2 Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/Customlanguage.html#13", "title": "1.3 How to Look Up Language Codes ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/Customlanguage.html#_3", "title": "2. Steps for Creating a Custom Language Pack ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/Customlanguage.html#_4", "title": "3. Methods for Deploying and Installing Language Packs ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/Customlanguage.html#31", "title": "3.1 Native Deployment (Direct Server Installation) ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/Customlanguage.html#32-docker", "title": "3.2 Docker Image Deployment ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/Customlanguage.html#_5", "title": "4. How It Takes Effect ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/Customlanguage.html#_6", "title": "5. Precautions ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/chat_to_API.html", "title": "Chatting via API Key", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"api-key\">Chatting via API Key<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#api-key\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Applications created in MaxKB support access via the OpenAI SDK format and the provided system SDK. The Professional Edition provides platform-level complete SDKs on top of the Community Edition. For details, see: <a href=\"X-Pack/system_API\">System API</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"1-openai-api\">1 Standard OpenAI API Format<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1-openai-api\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB applications are compatible with the OpenAI API format. Simply replace the Base URL and API Key with those provided by the MaxKB application on top of the original OpenAI API calling method.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"API Example\" src=\"../img/system/api_example.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Note:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>The format of the OpenAI URL is: Base URL/chat/completions</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The format of OpenAI Authorization is: Bearer API Key</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 将 url 和 Authorization 替换为 MaxKB 应用实际真实的 Base URL 和 API Key。\n\n\n\ncurl https://maxkb.fit2cloud.com/chat/api/xxxxxxxx-3fdf-7941-a6f4-0572478f57f6/chat/completions \\\n\n    -H \"Content-Type: application/json\"  \\\n\n    -H \"Authorization: Bearer agent-xxxxxxxxxx987f1bc06ab16e0ef\"   \\\n\n    -d '{\n\n        \"model\": \"gpt-3.5-turbo\",\n\n        \"messages\": [\n\n            {\n\n              \"role\": \"你是杭州飞致云信息科技有限公司旗下产品 MaxKB 知识库问答系统的智能小助手，你的工作是帮助 MaxKB 用户解答使用中遇到的问题，用户找你回答问题时，你要把主题放在 MaxKB 知识库问答系统身上。\",\n\n              \"content\": \"MaxKB 是什么？\"\n\n            }\n\n        ]\n\n    }'\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2-api\">2 System API<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2-api\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"21-api\">2.1 Open API Documentation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#21-api\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the application 【Overview】, click to visit the MaxKB API address, and create an API Key under API Key.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Open Document\" src=\"../img/system/open_api_doc.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Open Document\" src=\"../img/system/open_api_doc1.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"22-api-key\">2.2 API Key Authentication<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#22-api-key\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Authorize】 and enter the API Key you have created.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"API Authentication\" src=\"../img/system/api_auth.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"23\">2.3 Get Session Information<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#23\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>By calling the open API, you can generate a session id.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Session ID\" src=\"../img/system/api_chatid.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"24\">2.4 Conducting a Session<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#24\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Call the chat API, fill in the obtained session id, and enter parameters such as the question to start chatting.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Chat\" src=\"../img/system/api_chat.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Chat\" src=\"../img/system/api_chat1.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/chat_to_API.html#1-openai-api", "title": "1 Standard OpenAI API Format ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/chat_to_API.html#2-api", "title": "2 System API ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/chat_to_API.html#21-api", "title": "2.1 Open API Documentation ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/chat_to_API.html#22-api-key", "title": "2.2 API Key Authentication ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/chat_to_API.html#23", "title": "2.3 Get Session Information ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/chat_to_API.html#24", "title": "2.4 Conducting a Session ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/choose_model_dataset.html", "title": "Choosing a Model or Knowledge Base in the Q&A Page", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Choosing a Model or Knowledge Base in the Q&amp;A Page<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In MaxKB v2.8.0 and later versions, the Model and Knowledge Base components have been added to the User Input feature of the Advanced Agent. When chatting on the Q&amp;A page, users can choose the configured model and the knowledge base to be retrieved on their own, effectively improving the accuracy and flexibility of the chat.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"_2\">Model Switch Configuration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the Advanced Agent workflow, add a user input parameter in Basic Information, select Model as the component type, set the model type, and then configure the selectable models and the default model.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Add User Input\" src=\"../img/system/add_parameter.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In AI Chat or other components that require adding a model, you can switch the AI model to a referenced variable and select a user input parameter already created in the global variables.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Set Model Parameters\" src=\"../img/system/set_model.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After saving the workflow, users can switch between different models at any time to chat on the Q&amp;A page.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Switch Model\" src=\"../img/system/switch_model.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"_3\">Knowledge Base Switch Configuration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the Advanced Agent workflow, add a user input parameter in Basic Information, select Knowledge Base as the component type, and set the selectable knowledge bases and the default knowledge base (multiple selections allowed).</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Add User Input\" src=\"../img/system/add_parameter_dataset.png\" width=\"600px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the Document Tag Retrieval or Knowledge Base Retrieval components, you can switch the knowledge base to a referenced variable and select a user input parameter already created in the user's global variables.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Set Knowledge Base Parameters\" src=\"../img/system/set_dataset.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After saving the workflow, users can switch between different knowledge bases at any time to chat on the Q&amp;A page.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Switch Knowledge Base\" src=\"../img/system/switch_dataset.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/choose_model_dataset.html#_2", "title": "Model Switch Configuration ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/choose_model_dataset.html#_3", "title": "Knowledge Base Switch Configuration ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/email.html", "title": "Email Settings", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Email Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports the system administrator configuring mail server related information, so that the system can send notifications via email or perform other email-related operations.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../img/system/email.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/user_community.html", "title": "User Management", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">User Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 User List<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>System Administrators can create and manage users.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/userlist.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Create User<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports the system administrator creating users:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Username: the user account information, cannot be modified;</li>\n<li>Name: the user's name;</li>\n<li>Email: The user's email.</li>\n<li>Phone number: the user's phone number;</li>\n<li>Default password: defaults to <code>MaxKB@123..</code>.</li>\n<li>Role Settings: a workspace must be set when selecting the Regular User and workspace roles.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Role management is an Enterprise Edition X-Pack feature.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/create_user.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Edit User<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The username cannot be edited; other attributes can be edited.<br/>\n<strong>Note</strong>: Role management is an enterprise edition X-Pack feature.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/edit_userinfo.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>If the user status is disabled, the user cannot log in to MaxKB.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/forbid_user.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Resetting the Password<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>System Administrators can change the password for every user. In the user list, click [Change Password]; the change password dialog pops up, and the change succeeds after saving.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/edit_usermessges.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"5\">5 Delete User<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the user list, click 【Delete】, and a prompt box will appear. After confirmation, only the current user is deleted. <br/>\n<strong>Note</strong>: the built-in admin user cannot be deleted.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/delete_user.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"6\">6 Query User<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#6\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports searching users by username, name, and email.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/search_user.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/user_community.html#1", "title": "1 User List ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/user_community.html#2", "title": "2 Create User ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/user_community.html#3", "title": "3 Edit User ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/user_community.html#4", "title": "4 Resetting the Password ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/user_community.html#5", "title": "5 Delete User ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/user_community.html#6", "title": "6 Query User ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/workbuddy_maxkb_skills.html", "title": "WorkBuddy + MaxKB Skills Usage Guide", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"workbuddy-maxkb\">WorkBuddy + MaxKB Skills Usage Guide<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#workbuddy-maxkb\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"_1\">1. Introduction<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>WorkBuddy is an AI agent development platform. Through the \"MaxKB Skill\" (maxkb-platform-pro), it consolidates common MaxKB platform operations into natural language instructions. In the WorkBuddy dialog, the user describes a need in one sentence, and the skill automatically recognizes the intent and calls the MaxKB API to complete the operation, without needing to remember commands or API details.</p>\n<p>This skill consolidates the common MaxKB operations and maintenance tasks into four capabilities:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Capability</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>① Knowledge Base Import</td>\n<td>Write documents into the MaxKB knowledge base (supports DOCX intelligent segmentation)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>② Create an Agent</td>\n<td>Create a Simple (SIMPLE) or Workflow (WORK_FLOW) agent</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>③ Intelligent Query / Execution</td>\n<td>Invoke the agent to chat and execute tasks (such as group message notifications)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>④ Intelligent Report Generation</td>\n<td>Collect statistical data and generate Excel / HTML visual dashboards</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition warning\">\n<p class=\"admonition-title\">Applicable Scope Tip</p>\n<p>This skill depends on the MaxKB platform API, <strong>Only applicable to MaxKB Commercial Edition deployment, not to MaxKB Community Edition.</strong>.</p>\n<p>The MaxKB Community Edition does not expose Knowledge Base APIs; it only exposes three types of agent-related APIs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>① Obtain the agent session ID;</li>\n<li>② Query the agent details;</li>\n<li>③ Chat with the agent (send a message and get the answer).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Community Edition does not support creating Agents, Knowledge Base import, background statistics, and other capabilities, so most instructions cannot be used normally on the Community Edition.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"skill\">2. Installing Skills<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#skill\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"21\">2.1 Prerequisites<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#21\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before installing and performing any operation in this guide, make sure the following conditions are all satisfied:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The WorkBuddy client has been installed and successfully logged in;</li>\n<li>This machine can access the MaxKB address on the internal network normally;</li>\n<li>The operator holds a MaxKB platform account (used to verify the results in the backend).</li>\n<li>MaxKB connection information (the address and API Key) is usually preconfigured by the administrator into the skill. If it is not configured, WorkBuddy will prompt you to provide it on first use.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"22\">2.2 Download and Install<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#22\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>This skill is provided as a ZIP installation package: <a href=\"https://maxkb-apps-1323865188.cos.ap-shanghai.myqcloud.com/maxkb-platform-pro.zip\">maxkb-platform-pro-skills</a></p>\n<p>After the download is complete, install it in WorkBuddy by following these steps:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Open WorkBuddy and click the \"Experts · Skills · Connectors\" entry on the left;</li>\n<li>Switch to the 「Skills」 tab at the top;</li>\n<li>Click the 「Import Skill」 button in the upper-right corner;</li>\n<li>In the dialog box that appears, drag the Skills ZIP file into it (or click the 「Select ZIP File」 button to select a file);</li>\n<li>Wait for the installation to complete, and confirm the skill has appeared in the \"My Installed\" list.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Expected Result</strong>: In the「My Installed」skill list, maxkb-platform-pro is visible, and the skill description reads「The unified operation entry for connecting WorkBuddy with MaxKB v2」.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Import Skills\" src=\"../img/Skills/workbuddy_import_skill.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"skill_1\">3. Using Skills<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#skill_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"31\">3.1 Invocation Method<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#31\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After installation, you can invoke it in the chat window via + Skill.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Invoke Skill\" src=\"../img/Skills/workbuddy_invoke_skill.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"_2\">4. Typical Scenarios<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The following lists four typical scenarios as a reference for writing prompts. In practice, adjust the prompts as needed; the following are examples rather than fixed templates.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"41\">4.1 Uploading Files to the Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#41\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<p><strong>Example command:</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Upload a file to the knowledge base, using the newly created knowledge base named workbuddy 测试 @MaxKB文档研发工作流参考.docx</p>\n</blockquote>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>执行效果：自动新建知识库 → 上传文档 → 智能分段 → 写入知识库。\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><img alt=\"WorkBuddy side: upload complete, showing the new knowledge base information\" src=\"../img/Skills/workbuddy_kb_upload.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"MaxKB Backend: confirming the document has been added to the knowledge base\" src=\"../img/Skills/workbuddy_kb_doc.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"42\">4.2 Generating Usage Reports<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#42\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>执行效果：从 MaxKB 后台采集统计 → 生成 HTML 看板 + Excel 明细 → 在 WorkBuddy 中呈现。\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><img alt=\"MaxKB Report Display\" src=\"../img/Skills/workbuddy_show.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"43\">4.3 Creating an Agent<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#43\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>执行效果：创建 WORK_FLOW 工作流智能体 → 绑定知识库 → 发布上线。\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create an Advanced (Workflow) agent (on the WorkBuddy side)\" src=\"../img/Skills/workbuddy_create_agent.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"MaxKB Backend: the workflow canvas for a new agent\" src=\"../img/Skills/workbuddy_workflow_editor.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"44\">4.4 Asking the Agent<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#44\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>执行效果：智能体检索知识库 → AI 生成回答 → 回答标注引用来源。\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><img alt=\"MaxKB Backend: asking the agent a question and viewing the answer\" src=\"../img/Skills/workbuddy_maxkb_chat1.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"_3\">5. Summary<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>This skill consolidates the common operations and maintenance tasks of the MaxKB platform into natural language instructions, so users do not need to memorize commands or API details; they only need to describe their needs in the WorkBuddy dialog box. The following is a quick reference table of common instructions:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Requirement</th>\n<th>Recommended instructions (example)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Upload Documents to the Knowledge Base</td>\n<td><code>@maxkb-platform-pro 上传 XX.docx 到 XX 知识库</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>New Knowledge Base</td>\n<td><code>@maxkb-platform-pro 新建一个名称为 XX 的知识库</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Executing an Agent Task</td>\n<td><code>@maxkb-platform-pro 执行 XX 智能体</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Generate Usage Report</td>\n<td><code>@maxkb-platform-pro 展示 XX 类智能体的使用报表</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Create an agent that can search documents</td>\n<td><code>@maxkb-platform-pro 创建一个高级智能体，用于查询 XX 文档</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Asking the Agent a Question</td>\n<td><code>@maxkb-platform-pro XX 要求是什么</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>In the instruction, you should use natural and clear language to describe 「what to do」 (including the target object and the expected result). WorkBuddy will convert it into specific operations on MaxKB. The clearer the instruction, the more accurate the execution result.</p>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/workbuddy_maxkb_skills.html#_1", "title": "1. Introduction ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/workbuddy_maxkb_skills.html#skill", "title": "2. Installing Skills ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/workbuddy_maxkb_skills.html#21", "title": "2.1 Prerequisites ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/workbuddy_maxkb_skills.html#22", "title": "2.2 Download and Install ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/workbuddy_maxkb_skills.html#skill_1", "title": "3. Using Skills ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/workbuddy_maxkb_skills.html#31", "title": "3.1 Invocation Method ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/workbuddy_maxkb_skills.html#_2", "title": "4. Typical Scenarios ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/workbuddy_maxkb_skills.html#41", "title": "4.1 Uploading Files to the Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/workbuddy_maxkb_skills.html#42", "title": "4.2 Generating Usage Reports ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/workbuddy_maxkb_skills.html#43", "title": "4.3 Creating an Agent ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/workbuddy_maxkb_skills.html#44", "title": "4.4 Asking the Agent ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/workbuddy_maxkb_skills.html#_3", "title": "5. Summary ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/app_auth.html", "title": "Access Restrictions", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Access Restrictions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports restricting agent access through authentication, further ensuring information security. You can set [Password Verification] or [Login Authentication].</p>\n<p>After selecting [Login Authentication], you need to enable at least one login method.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>【Chat Users】requires the administrator to add, delete, and modify user groups and users under 【Chat Users】 and 【User Groups】 in 【System Management】.</li>\n<li>【Login Methods】will only be displayed after the administrator configures 【Login Authentication】 in 【System Management】 and enables single sign-on and QR code login in 【Chat Users】.</li>\n<li>【Account Login Captcha Settings】Agent managers can enable the captcha verification feature after chat users fail to log in a specified number of times. When consecutive login failures reach the preset threshold, the system automatically triggers the captcha verification mechanism, effectively preventing security risks such as brute-force attacks.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Login Authentication\" src=\"../../img/system/chat_authentication2.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After agent authentication is enabled, accessing through a public link (including the floating widget) requires entering a verification password to enter the Q&amp;A page.</p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> After authentication is enabled, accessing the agent via the public access link requires entering a verification password, including demo and full-screen/floating-window embedding; agents connected to WeCom, Official Accounts, DingTalk, and Feishu are not affected.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Authentication\" src=\"../../img/app/app_password1.png\"/><br/> </p>\n<p><img alt=\"Authentication\" src=\"../../img/app/app_password3.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>If QR code login is selected (such as DingTalk, Feishu, or WeCom), when a user accesses the assistant to chat, the system will automatically pop up the QR code scan interface of the selected platform. After the user scans the code, they can quickly log in and start chatting</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Login Authentication\" src=\"../../img/system/QR_code.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/app_chatueser.html", "title": "Chat User", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Chat User <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports setting which user groups and users are allowed to enter the current application's Q&amp;A page to ask questions.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>If a chat user belongs to multiple user groups, authorization of any user group allows the user to enter the application and ask questions. After a user is removed from a user group, the corresponding authorization will be revoked.<br/>\nAutomatic Authorization Rules:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When enabled: the current user group and subsequently added members are automatically authorized to enter the application and ask questions.</li>\n<li>Disabled: group members must be manually authorized, and newly added members are not authorized by default.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>In an application, only viewing and authorizing user groups are supported. User group and member management must be performed by a workspace administrator or system administrator in 【System Management】.</li>\n<li>If login authentication is not enabled in Authentication, all knowledge bases associated with the application can be retrieved by any user.</li>\n<li><strong>After login authentication is enabled for an application, if the knowledge bases in the application are not configured with chat users, the knowledge base content cannot be retrieved. You need to authorize the specified chat user in the knowledge base.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Chat User\" src=\"../../img/app/userteam_auth.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/app_integrate.html", "title": "Third-Party Access", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Third-Party Access <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports connecting the created agents to the WeCom smart bot, WeCom agent, WeCom customer service, Official Accounts (service accounts and subscription accounts), DingTalk agent, and Feishu agent, enabling conversations between an enterprise's internal employees and the external public.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"1\">1 WeCom Intelligent Bot<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The WeCom bot supports @the AI bot in <strong>WeCom Internal Group Chat</strong> for Q&amp;A conversations.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Chat Demo\" src=\"../../img/app/wechat_ai_asker.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In Agent Integration, click the Configure button of 【WeCom Intelligent Robot】. A callback URL is automatically generated in the configuration information and needs to be copied into the URL field in the API reception settings of the WeCom intelligent robot.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Bot Configuration\" src=\"../../img/app/wechat_ai_add.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Creating a bot: in <a href=\"https://work.weixin.qq.com/wework_admin/frame#apps\">WeCom Admin Console</a>, click 【Security &amp; Management】-【Management Tools】-【Intelligent Robot】-【Create Robot】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Creating a WeCom Bot\" src=\"../../img/app/wechat_ai_create.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Creating a WeCom Bot\" src=\"../../img/app/wechat_ai_create1.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select [Create via API Mode].</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"API Mode Creation\" src=\"../../img/app/wechat_ai_API.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After filling in the basic information, enter the callback URL from the MaxKB agent configuration into the URL field. At the same time, fill in the randomly generated Token and Encoding-AESKey in the MaxKB agent configuration and save the agent configuration. After saving, return to the WeCom admin console to create the bot.</p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Before saving the WeCom agent's API message-receiving configuration, be sure to complete and save the WeCom agent configuration in MaxKB; otherwise, saving will report the error <code>openapi回调地址请求不通过</code>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Callback Address\" src=\"../../img/app/wechat_ai_recall.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After creation, you can @ the intelligent robot in <strong>WeCom Internal Group Chat</strong> to ask questions.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Chat Demo\" src=\"../../img/app/wechat_ai_asker.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"2\">2 WeCom Agent<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After connecting the WeCom agent, you can find the corresponding agent in 【WeCom】-【Workbench】 and start a conversation.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Chat\" src=\"../../img/app/enter_wechat_dialog.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In Agent Integration, click the 【Configure】 button of 【WeCom Agent】. A callback URL is automatically generated in the configuration information and needs to be copied to the API reception settings of the WeCom agent. All other information will be generated and obtained in the WeCom admin console.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Display Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/ent_wechat_setting.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Obtain the enterprise ID: In <a href=\"https://work.weixin.qq.com/wework_admin/frame#apps\">WeCom Admin Console</a>, click the [My Enterprise] menu, and you can see the enterprise ID information at the bottom.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Enterprise ID\" src=\"../../img/system/obtain_wxid.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Creating a WeCom agent: in 【Agent Management】, click 【Create Agent】, choose the agent logo, and set the agent name, agent introduction, and visibility range.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Agent Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/robot_info.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Obtain the Agentid and Secret: Enter the created Agent and obtain the AgentId and Secret. Click [View]; the Secret will be viewed through WeCom.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Agent Information\" src=\"../../img/system/qiwei_appinfo.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Obtain the Token and EncodingAESKey: In the WeCom Agent settings, go to [Receive Messages] - [Set Up API Reception], and obtain the Token and EncodingAESKey.</p>\n<p>Enter the corresponding parameters in the MaxKB WeCom agent configuration and save them. Then go back to the WeCom agent settings and copy the callback URL automatically generated in the agent access configuration under 【Receive Messages】-【Set API Reception】, and finally click 【Save】.</p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Before saving the WeCom agent's API message-receiving configuration, be sure to complete and save the WeCom agent configuration in MaxKB; otherwise, saving will report the error <code>openapi回调地址请求不通过</code>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Set Up API Reception\" src=\"../../img/app/recmsg_api.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Before saving the WeCom agent's API message-receiving configuration, be sure to complete and save the WeCom agent configuration in MaxKB; otherwise, saving will report the error <code>openapi回调地址请求不通过</code>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Set Up API Reception\" src=\"../../img/app/recmsg_api_setting.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Configure enterprise trusted IP: Go to [Enterprise Trusted IP] in the WeCom agent settings and set the IP address of the MaxKB service as a trusted IP.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Configure Trusted IP\" src=\"../../img/system/qiwei_ip.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the above steps are configured and the WeCom agent information is entered and saved in the WeCom agent access configuration, you can find the bot in WeCom agents to start a conversation.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Chat\" src=\"../../img/app/enter_wechat_dialog.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"3\">3 WeCom Customer Service<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After connecting WeCom customer service, you can @WeCom Customer Service in group chats and use the jump link to achieve one-on-one customer service Q&amp;A.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Customer Service Account\" src=\"../../img/app/dialog_cs.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After connecting the MaxKB agent to a WeCom agent, you can also connect this agent to WeChat Customer Service to provide services to external users. <br/>\nCreate a customer service account: under [Agent Management] in the WeCom management console, click [WeChat Customer Service] and create an account. For the account's reception mode, select: Robot + Human Reception</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Customer Service Account\" src=\"../../img/app/weichat_customservice.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Customer Service Account\" src=\"../../img/app/create_cs_account.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Linking Customer Service Accounts to Agents: in WeChat Customer Service, configure the 【Agents That Can Call APIs】, and set up the customer service account.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Customer Service Account\" src=\"../../img/app/cs_app.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Customer Service Account\" src=\"../../img/app/config_cs_account.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Enable Customer Service Assistant: After enabling [Customer Service Assistant] in the enterprise's external group settings, WeChat Customer Service joins the group. Any user in the group only needs to @ the Customer Service Assistant to start a consultation and have a one-on-one conversation with WeChat Customer Service.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Customer Service Account\" src=\"../../img/app/enable_cs.png\" width=\"500px\"/>\n<img alt=\"WeCom Customer Service Account\" src=\"../../img/app/dialog_cs.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"4\">4 WeChat Official Account<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After connecting, you can directly use the WeChat Official Account to conduct Q&amp;A conversations.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Official Account Chat\" src=\"../../img/app/public_account_dialog.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In Agent Integration, click the 【Configure】 button of 【Official Account】. A callback URL is automatically generated in the configuration information and needs to be copied into the server address URL under 【WeChat Official Accounts Platform - Settings &amp; Development - Basic Configuration - Server Configuration】. All other information will be generated and obtained in the WeChat Official Accounts Platform.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Official Account Configuration\" src=\"../../img/app/public_account_setting_empty.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Obtain the APP ID, APP Secret, Token, and message encryption/decryption key: In the WeChat Official Account Platform - Settings &amp; Development - Basic Configuration, obtain the APP ID and APP Secret, and then enable the server configuration to generate the Token and message encryption/decryption key.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Official Account Information\" src=\"../../img/app/public_account_basicinfo.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Official Account Information\" src=\"../../img/app/public_account_setting1.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Enter the generated APP ID, APP Secret, Token, and message encryption/decryption key information into the MaxKB Official Account configuration window, then save.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Official Account Information\" src=\"../../img/app/public_account_setting2.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Set the URL in 【Official Account - Basic Configuration - Server Configuration】 to the callback URL shown in the MaxKB Official Account configuration window, then submit and enable the server configuration.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Official Account Information\" src=\"../../img/app/public_account_setting_url.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Enable the customer service API permission.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Customer Service API Permissions\" src=\"../../img/app/public_account_enable_api.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Set the IP whitelist: In the [IP Whitelist] of the Official Account Basic Configuration, add the IP address of the MaxKB server.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Official Account IP Allowlist\" src=\"../../img/app/public_account_ip.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After completing the configuration following the above steps, you can send messages in the official account to start a chat.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Official Account Chat\" src=\"../../img/app/public_account_dialog.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"5\">5 DingTalk Agent<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After connecting DingTalk, you can @ the bot in a group chat for Q&amp;A conversations.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Robot Chat\" src=\"../../img/app/ding_dialog1.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In Agent Integration, click the 【Configure】 button of 【DingTalk Agent】. A callback URL is automatically generated in the configuration information and needs to be copied into the message reception address under DingTalk - Robot Settings. Other information will be generated and obtained in the DingTalk Open Platform.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Robot Creation\" src=\"../../img/app/dingding_setting.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Creating a bot: in <a href=\"https://open-dev.dingtalk.com/\">DingTalk Open Platform</a>'s 【Agent Development】-【DingTalk Agent】, click 【Create Agent】, fill in the agent information, then click 【Save】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Robot Creation\" src=\"../../img/app/dingding_robot_create.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Obtain the Client ID and Client Secret: Enter the created DingTalk Agent, open the [Credentials &amp; Basic Information] page, and obtain the Client ID and Client Secret.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Agent Information\" src=\"../../img/app/dingding_info.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the MaxKB DingTalk agent configuration window, enter the Client ID and Client Secret agent credentials obtained in the previous steps, and save.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Agent Information\" src=\"../../img/app/dingding_setting2.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Add Agent Capability】, select the 【Robot】 capability, and click 【Add】. After entering the robot's basic configuration information, set 【Message Receiving Mode】 to HTTP mode, fill the callback URL from the MaxKB DingTalk agent configuration into the message receiving address, and then click 【Publish】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Robot Add\" src=\"../../img/app/dingding_robot_add.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"DingTalk Robot Message Reception Mode\" src=\"../../img/app/dingding_msg_recvmode.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After completing the configuration following the above steps, you can chat by @-mentioning the bot in a group, or have a one-on-one chat with the bot agent.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Chat\" src=\"../../img/app/dingding_dialog.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"6\">6 Feishu Agent<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#6\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After connecting Feishu, you can find the corresponding agent in the agent list for Q&amp;A conversations.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Chat\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_dialog1.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In Agent Integration, click the 【Configure】 button of 【Feishu Agent】. A callback URL is automatically generated in the configuration information and needs to be copied into the request address under 【Feishu Open Platform - Events &amp; Callbacks - Event Configuration - Configure Subscription Method】. All other information will be generated and obtained in the Feishu Open Platform.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Agent Configuration\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_setting.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Creating a Feishu bot: first, in <a href=\"https://open.feishu.cn/app/\">Feishu Open Platform</a>'s 【Enterprise Self-built Agent】, click 【Create Enterprise Self-built Agent】, and fill in the agent information.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Add Robot\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_create_app.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Add Agent Capability】, select 【Add by Capability - Robot】, and click 【Add】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Add Robot\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_add_robot.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Add Permission: Open 【Permission Management】, copy the following permission configuration and paste it into the 【API Permission - Permission Configuration】 input box, select all the filtered permission items, click 【Batch Enable】, and finally click 【Confirm】.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code> contact:contact.base:readonly,contact:user.base:readonly,im:message.group_at_msg:readonly, im:message.p2p_msg:readonly,im:message:send_as_bot,im:resource\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Permissions\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_app_auth.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Obtain the APP ID, APP Secret, and Verification Token: Enter the created Feishu Agent, open the [Credentials &amp; Basic Information] page, and obtain the APP ID and APP Secret.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Agent Information\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_app_info.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Open [Events &amp; Callbacks - Encryption Policy] to obtain the Verification Token.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu token\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_verify_token.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Enter the above information in the MaxKB Feishu agent configuration window, and save.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Events and Callbacks\" src=\"../../img/app/maxkb_feishu_config.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Configure the callback URL: In the Feishu open platform, in [Events and Callbacks] - [Callback Configuration] &gt; Subscription, fill the callback URL of the MaxKB Feishu agent into the [Request Address].</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Events and Callbacks\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_event_config1.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Events and Callbacks\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_event_config2.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Publishing the agent: click 【Create Version】, fill in the version information, then click 【Save】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Agent Publishing\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_app_create1.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Agent Publishing\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_app_create2.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After confirmation of publishing, the Agent status will be updated to <code>已启用</code>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Agent Publishing\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_app_enabled.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After completing the configuration following the above steps, open the Feishu client and search for <code>MaxKB小助手</code>, then click Add to start a one-on-one chat.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Chat\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_app_search.png\" width=\"500px\"/> <img alt=\"Feishu Chat\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_dialog.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/app_integrate.html#1", "title": "1 WeCom Intelligent Bot ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/app_integrate.html#2", "title": "2 WeCom Agent ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/app_integrate.html#3", "title": "3 WeCom Customer Service ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/app_integrate.html#4", "title": "4 WeChat Official Account ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/app_integrate.html#5", "title": "5 DingTalk Agent ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/app_integrate.html#6", "title": "6 Feishu Agent ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/app_logo_settting.html", "title": "Application Display Settings", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Application Display Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In addition to supporting language, showing the source of knowledge, and showing execution details, X-Pack also supports richer configurations, including the application dialog theme color, font color, display and replacement of the AI reply avatar, display and replacement of the asking user's avatar, the floating-window intake entry icon and its position, conversation history, guide images, and disclaimers, etc.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Display Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/view_setting.png\" width=\"800px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Example of the application display configuration effect:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Chat Dialog\" src=\"../../img/app/app_fuchuang.jpg\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/authorization_resources.html", "title": "Resource Authorization", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Resource Authorization<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Resource Authorization feature is used to manage users' access permissions to resources within a workspace.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>System Administrators can authorize all resources in [System Management];</li>\n<li>Workspace administrators can grant access to all resources in the workspace;</li>\n<li>Regular users can authorize the resources they create.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 System Resource Authorization<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>System Administrators (all workspaces) and Workspace Administrators (who can only select workspaces where they have the Workspace Administrator role) can perform resource authorization operations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Member: lists the members under the selected workspace who are Regular Users or inherit the Regular User role.</li>\n<li>Resources: Agents, knowledge bases, tools, and models list the resources under the selected workspace by the folder management directory of the workspace.</li>\n<li>Operation:<ul>\n<li>No authorization: no authorization is granted to resources by default.</li>\n<li>View: You can only view and use the resource, and cannot add, delete, or modify it.</li>\n<li>Manage: allows all operations on the resource.</li>\n<li>By user role: for the selected resources, grant users the permissions owned by the role.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Features such as Workspace and Role Management are X-Pack features.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resources\" src=\"../../img/system/authorization_resources.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 User Resource Authorization<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Users can authorize resources to specified users in agents, knowledge bases, tools, and models. The authorized users are all members of the current workspace. Resource authorization supports filtering by name, username, permission, and role; after filtering, permissions can be configured in batch.</p>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: User roles are an X-Pack feature.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resource Authorization\" src=\"../../img/system/authorization_resources_app.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Resource Authorization Rules<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>By default, authorization to the system administrator is granted by user role; changing the workspace administrator and the system administrator does not affect either’s role permissions over resources (high priority);</li>\n<li>When a Regular User is granted the [Manage] permission, they can also perform resource authorization operations on agents, but must follow the rule that role permissions take precedence;</li>\n<li>If a member has multiple roles, the authorization is based on the maximum permissions (the union) of all roles.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/authorization_resources.html#1", "title": "1 System Resource Authorization ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/authorization_resources.html#2", "title": "2 User Resource Authorization ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/authorization_resources.html#3", "title": "3 Resource Authorization Rules ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/chat_authentication.html", "title": "Login Authentication", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Login Authentication<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports restricting application access through authentication, further ensuring information security. You can set [Password Verification] or [Login Authentication].</p>\n<p>After selecting [Login Authentication], you need to enable at least one login method.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>【Chat Users】requires the administrator to add, delete, and modify user groups and users under 【Chat Users】 and 【User Groups】 in 【System Management】.</li>\n<li>【Login Methods】will only be displayed after the administrator configures 【Login Authentication】 in 【System Management】 and enables single sign-on and QR code login in 【Chat Users】.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Authentication Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/app_auth.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After app authentication is enabled, a verification password is required to enter the Q&amp;A page when accessing via a public access link (including the floating box).<br/> <br/>\n<strong>Note:</strong> After app authentication is enabled, a verification password is required to access the application via public access links, including demos and full-screen/floating mode embeds, while applications integrated into WeCom, WeChat Official Accounts, DingTalk, and Feishu are not affected.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Authentication\" src=\"../../img/app/app_password1.png\"/><br/> <br/>\n<img alt=\"Authentication\" src=\"../../img/app/app_password2.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/chat_user.html", "title": "Chat User", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Chat User <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Chat users are users who, after authentication, can ask questions on the Q&amp;A page. Administrators can use the user group management feature to flexibly control which users can access the Q&amp;A page and use knowledge bases in 【Agents】 and 【Knowledge Bases】, and assign different permissions to different user groups. <br/>\nPermission Description:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>System Administrator</strong>: Manages chat users, user groups, and login authentication.</li>\n<li><strong>Workspace Administrator</strong>: Manages chat users and user groups.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 User Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"11\">1.1 Create User<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#11\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Administrators can create and delete Chat Users. User information includes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Username: 4-20 characters, required and unique.</li>\n<li>Name: 1-20 characters, required and unique.</li>\n<li>Status: Normal/Disabled. Once disabled, the user cannot access any feature of the system.</li>\n<li>Email, phone number: not required.</li>\n<li>Password: required, with the same rules as system users. The default password for third-party users is the password in the Profile configuration (for example: MaxKB@123).</li>\n<li>User group: a user can belong to multiple user groups, or not select any user group.</li>\n<li>User Source: created locally.</li>\n<li>Creation Time: automatically records the time the user was created.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create chat user\" src=\"../../img/system/create_chatuser.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Except for the username, all other attributes can be edited and modified.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Edit Chat User\" src=\"../../img/system/edit_chatuser.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Administrators can change the login password of a Chat User account; the password rules are the same as those for system users.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Changing the Password of Chat Users\" src=\"../../img/system/edit_usermessage.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"12\">1.2 Set User Group<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#12\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Set user groups. Supports batch-setting user groups for multiple chat users.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Select the chat users you want to configure.</li>\n<li>Click the 【Set User Group】 button to open the settings dialog.</li>\n<li>Select the configuration method:<ul>\n<li>Append: Add new user groups to the selected users.</li>\n<li>Replace: Delete the selected user's existing user group and set a new user group.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Set User Group\" src=\"../../img/system/set_usergaroup.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"13\">1.3 Import User<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#13\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Only the System Administrator can perform this operation; Workspace Administrators do not have this feature.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>User Source: supports syncing system users and third-party user information such as WeCom.</li>\n<li>Synchronized fields: username, name, email, mobile phone number, status, password, and user type.</li>\n<li>User group: synchronized users will be assigned to the default user group.</li>\n<li>User Type: consistent with system users.</li>\n<li>Synchronization logic: existing users will be skipped and will not be added or updated again.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Sync chat users\" src=\"../../img/system/synchronize_users.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 User Group Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>User groups are for chat user management, used to classify and centrally manage users. Through user groups, administrators can assign different permissions to different types of users.<br/>\nSystem administrators and workspace administrators can perform the following operations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add User Group: Create a new user group.</li>\n<li>Deleting/Renaming User Groups: the system has a built-in default user group that cannot be deleted but can be renamed.</li>\n<li>Add/Remove Members: Add or remove members from a user group, supporting batch operations.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Delete user group\" src=\"../../img/system/chatgroup_set.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The user group name is unique, up to 128 characters.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create User Group\" src=\"../../img/system/create_group.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When deleting a user group, the system prompts for confirmation and reminds the administrator that all members under the user group will be removed.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Delete user group\" src=\"../../img/system/delete_group.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports adding members to a user group.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Add Chat User\" src=\"../../img/system/add_groupuser.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Login Authentication<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The system supports flexible configuration of the login authentication method for Chat Users, including integrating QR-code login from mainstream third-party platforms, suitable for building a secure, efficient, and unified Chat User management system.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Login Authentication\" src=\"../../img/system/chat_authentication.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the login authentication configuration is complete, this login method can be displayed in 【Agent】 - 【Overview】 - 【Access Restrictions】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Login Authentication\" src=\"../../img/system/chat_authentication2.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>If QR code login is selected (such as DingTalk, Feishu, or WeCom), when a user accesses the assistant to chat, the system will automatically pop up the QR code scan interface of the selected platform. Once the user scans the code, they can quickly log in and start chatting.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Login Authentication\" src=\"../../img/system/QR_code.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"31\">3.1 WeCom Agent Passwordless Login<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#31\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>To enable password-free login for agents, the system administrator must configure the WeCom information in advance in [System Management] - [Chat Users] - [Login Authentication] - [QR Code Login].</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Login Authentication\" src=\"../../img/system/chat_authentication.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the agent, enable [Access Restriction] - [Authentication] - [Login Authentication] and check WeCom, then save the login authentication settings. At the same time, authorize the corresponding chat user in [Chat User].</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Password-Free Login\" src=\"../../img/system/wechat_login_auth.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The construction of the agent's homepage URL can refer to the WeCom development guide <a href=\"https://developer.work.weixin.qq.com/document/path/91120#%E6%9E%84%E9%80%A0%E4%BC%81%E4%B8%9Aoauth2%E9%93%BE%E6%8E%A5\">Create a web authorization link — construct an enterprise OAuth2 link</a>.</p>\n<p>The link format and parameter description are as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Link format: <a href=\"https://open.weixin.qq.com/connect/oauth2/authorize?appid=CORPID&amp;redirect_uri=REDIRECT_URI/chat/api/auth/wecom/oauth2?accessToken=ACCESSTOKEN&amp;response_type=code&amp;scope=snsapi_privateinfo&amp;agentid=AGENTID&amp;state=STATE#wechat_redirect\">https://open.weixin.qq.com/connect/oauth2/authorize?appid=CORPID&amp;redirect_uri=REDIRECT_URI/chat/api/auth/wecom/oauth2?accessToken=ACCESSTOKEN&amp;response_type=code&amp;scope=snsapi_privateinfo&amp;agentid=AGENTID&amp;state=STATE#wechat_redirect</a></li>\n<li>CORPID: the CorpID of WeCom</li>\n<li>REDIRECT_URI: the callback link address redirected to after authorization. The link needs to be processed with urlencode, for example: https%3A%2F%2Fmaxkbk.fit2cloud.cn. Just adjust the domain part.</li>\n<li>ACCESSTOKEN: the Agent ID. For example, if the public access link is <a href=\"https://maxkb.fit2cloud.cn/chat/e113a4980984be3fe\">https://maxkb.fit2cloud.cn/chat/e113a4980984be3fe</a>, e113a4980984be3fe is the corresponding Agent ID.</li>\n<li>AGENTID: the WeCom application ID, e.g., 1000001</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Example home page address: <a href=\"https://open.weixin.qq.com/connect/oauth2/authorize?appid=ww8ef82888c6f6e33&amp;redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fmaxkb.fit2cloud.cn/chat/api/auth/wecom/oauth2?accessToken=e113a4980984be3fe&amp;response_type=code&amp;scope=snsapi_privateinfo&amp;agentid=1000002&amp;state=STATE#wechat_redirect\">https://open.weixin.qq.com/connect/oauth2/authorize?appid=ww8ef82888c6f6e33&amp;redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fmaxkb.fit2cloud.cn/chat/api/auth/wecom/oauth2?accessToken=e113a4980984be3fe&amp;response_type=code&amp;scope=snsapi_privateinfo&amp;agentid=1000002&amp;state=STATE#wechat_redirect</a></p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/weichat_oauth2.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Set the trusted domain: In [Application Management], click [Set Trusted Domain], add a trusted domain, and verify it. You can refer to <a href=\"https://kb.fit2cloud.com/?p=915e0151-5581-406f-ac2e-22afb9b3b4bf\">Trusted Domain Configuration</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/trusted_domain.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Configure the enterprise trusted IP. Configure the trusted IP in [Enterprise Trusted IP].</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Configure Trusted IP\" src=\"../../img/system/qiwei_ip.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the configuration is complete, find the MaxKB agent in the WeCom workbench and chat without login.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/qiwei_oauth2_login.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"32\">3.2 DingTalk Agent Passwordless Login<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#32\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>To enable password-free login for agents, the system administrator must configure the DingTalk information in advance in [System Management] - [Chat Users] - [Login Authentication] - [QR Code Login].</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Login Authentication\" src=\"../../img/system/chat_authentication.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the agent, enable [Access Restriction] - [Authentication] - [Login Authentication] and check DingTalk, then save the login authentication settings. At the same time, authorize the corresponding chat user in [Chat User].</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Passwordless Login\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_login_auth.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Add the web application capability. In the 【Application Capability】 of the DingTalk open platform, add 【Web Application】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Create Application\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_add_webapp.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Set [App Home Page] and [PC Home Page URL].</p>\n<p>The link format and parameter description are as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Link format: http(s)://xxx.xxx.xxx/chat/login/ACCESSTOKEN?client=dingtalk&amp;corpId=CORPID.</li>\n<li>ACCESSTOKEN: the Agent ID. For example, if the public access link is <a href=\"https://maxkb.fit2cloud.cn/chat/e113a4980984be3fe\">https://maxkb.fit2cloud.cn/chat/e113a4980984be3fe</a>, e113a4980984be3fe is the corresponding Agent ID.</li>\n<li>CORPID: the CorpId of the DingTalk enterprise, for example dinge20bxxxxxxxxxxxxx53d9884</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_url_set.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Security Settings. Set the redirect URL in 【Security Settings】.</p>\n<p>Note: This address is the DingTalk callback URL in 【System Management】 - 【Chat User】 - 【Login Authentication】 - 【QR Code Login】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Security Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_save_setting.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Share Settings: in 【Access Login】, set the 【Callback Domain】.</p>\n<p>Note: This address is the DingTalk callback URL in 【System Management】 - 【Chat User】 - 【Login Authentication】 - 【QR Code Login】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Security Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_share_setting.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Permission Management: go to Permission Management and add the permission as shown below.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Application Information\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_permissions.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the app is published, you can access MaxKB from the DingTalk workbench without logging in.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Security Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_display.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"33\">3.3 Feishu Agent Passwordless Login<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#33\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>To enable password-free login for agents, the system administrator must configure the Feishu information in advance in [System Management] - [Chat Users] - [Login Authentication] - [QR Code Login].</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Login Authentication\" src=\"../../img/system/chat_authentication.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the agent, enable [Access Restriction] - [Authentication] - [Login Authentication] and check Feishu, then save the login authentication settings. At the same time, authorize the corresponding chat user in [Chat User].</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Passwordless Login\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_login_auth.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Add the 【Page Application】 capability.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Add Page Application\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_add_webapp.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Configure the web application.</p>\n<p>The link format and parameter description are as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Link format: http(s)://xxx.xxx.xxx/chat/login/ACCESSTOKEN?client=lark&amp;appId=AppID.</li>\n<li>ACCESSTOKEN: the Agent ID. For example, if the public access link is <a href=\"https://maxkb.fit2cloud.cn/chat/e113a4980984be3fe\">https://maxkb.fit2cloud.cn/chat/e113a4980984be3fe</a>, e113a4980984be3fe is the corresponding Agent ID.</li>\n<li>AppID: the App ID of the Feishu application</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Page Application Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_web_set.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Add the redirect URL in 【Security Settings】.</p>\n<p>The link format and parameter description are as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>In 【System Management】-【Chat Users】-【Login Authentication】-【QR Code Login】, the Feishu callback address is: http(s)://xxx.xxx.xxx/chat/api/auth/lark</li>\n<li>http(s)://xxx.xxx.xxx/chat/login/ACCESSTOKEN. Here ACCESSTOKEN is the agent ID. For example, the public access link is <a href=\"https://maxkb.fit2cloud.cn/chat/e113a4980984be3fe\">https://maxkb.fit2cloud.cn/chat/e113a4980984be3fe</a>, and e113a4980984be3fe is the corresponding ACCESSTOKEN.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Security Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_security_set.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the app is published, you can access MaxKB from the Feishu workbench without logging in.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Security Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_display.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Usage Scenarios<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the System Administrator has set up Chat Users, when users create Agents and Knowledge Bases, they can set a Chat User group to control the related usage permissions.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Login Authentication\" src=\"../../img/system/chat_user_dataset.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Login Authentication\" src=\"../../img/system/chat_user_app.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/chat_user.html#1", "title": "1 User Management ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/chat_user.html#11", "title": "1.1 Create User ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/chat_user.html#12", "title": "1.2 Set User Group ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/chat_user.html#13", "title": "1.3 Import User ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/chat_user.html#2", "title": "2 User Group Management ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/chat_user.html#3", "title": "3 Login Authentication ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/chat_user.html#31", "title": "3.1 WeCom Agent Passwordless Login ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/chat_user.html#32", "title": "3.2 DingTalk Agent Passwordless Login ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/chat_user.html#33", "title": "3.3 Feishu Agent Passwordless Login ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/chat_user.html#4", "title": "4 Usage Scenarios ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/dataset_chatuser.html", "title": "Chat User", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Chat User <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The knowledge base supports setting the user groups and users allowed to access the current knowledge base.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>If a chat user belongs to multiple user groups, authorization of any user group allows the user to ask questions to the knowledge base. After a user is removed from a user group, the corresponding authorization will be revoked.</p>\n<p>Automatic Authorization Rules:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When enabled: if you enable auto-authorization after authorizing a user group, the current user group and subsequently added members are automatically authorized to access the knowledge base content.</li>\n<li>Disabled: group members must be manually authorized, and newly added members are not authorized by default.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Note:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>In a knowledge base, only viewing and authorizing user groups are supported. User group and member management must be performed by a workspace administrator or system administrator in 【System Management】.</li>\n<li>This configuration takes effect only after the associated Agent enables login authentication for chat users.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Chat User\" src=\"../../img/app/dataset_chatuser.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After enabling Knowledge Base Chat Users, in the agent you need to set the login authentication method to account login in <a href=\"app_auth\">Agent Access Restriction</a>, and set the user groups and users allowed to enter the current agent's Q&amp;A page to ask questions.</p>\n<p>After configuring the chat users for the knowledge base and the agent respectively, when asking the agent, users authorized for the knowledge base can retrieve relevant segments in the knowledge base, while users not authorized for the knowledge base cannot obtain knowledge base information.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Chat User\" src=\"../../img/app/dataset_chatuser1.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Chat User\" src=\"../../img/app/dataset_chatuser2.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/feishu_doc.html", "title": "Feishu Document Knowledge Base", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Feishu Document Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Feishu Bot Configuration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports building a knowledge base from Feishu documents, currently supporting Feishu cloud documents and spreadsheet documents. <br/>\nNote: Support for Feishu documents is implemented through a Feishu bot with the corresponding document permissions configured, and in groups by setting the bot as a collaborator.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"11\">1.1 Create a Feishu Bot<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#11\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>First, in the [Enterprise Self-Built Application] area of <a href=\"https://open.feishu.cn/app/\">Feishu Open Platform</a>, click [Create Enterprise Self-Built Application] and fill in the application information.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Create\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_create_app.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Add Application Capability】, select 【Add by Capability - Robot】, and click 【Add】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Add Robot\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_add_robot.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"12\">1.2 Add Permission<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#12\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Open [Permission Management], copy the permission configuration below and paste it into the [API Permission - Permission Configuration] input box, select all the filtered permission items, click [Batch Enable], and finally click [Confirm].</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>docs:document:export,docx:document:readonly,drive:drive,space:document:retrieve\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Document Permissions\" src=\"../../img/dataset/feishu_doc_access.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"13\">1.3 Obtain Required Information<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#13\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Obtain the APP ID, APP Secret, and Folder Token.\nEnter the created Feishu application, open the [Credentials &amp; Basic Information] page, and obtain the APP ID and APP Secret.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Application Information\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_app_info.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"14\">1.4 Application Publishing<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#14\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Create Version】, fill in the version information, and click 【Save】; after the administrator reviews it, proceed with the group settings.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Application Publishing\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_robot_release.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"15\">1.5 Group Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#15\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Add the corresponding group bot to the internal group.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Group Robot\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_group_robot1.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the folder of the Feishu document, add the group that contains the app bot as a collaborator.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Group Robot\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_doc_collaborator.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Create a Feishu Document Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When creating a knowledge base, select 【Feishu】 as the knowledge base type and configure the corresponding parameters:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>App ID: the unique ID of the Feishu application.</li>\n<li>App Secret: the Feishu application credential.</li>\n<li>Folder Token: the unique ID of each folder in the Feishu cloud space, used to distinguish and operate on specific folders. Select the folder and you can obtain it from the link information.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Folder\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_folder_token.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Feishu Knowledge Base Creation\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_kb_create.png\"/> </p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the Feishu knowledge base, click 【Import Documents】, select the documents to upload from the Feishu folder, and click Start Import to import the Feishu documents into MaxKB.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Document Filtering\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_doc_select.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Feishu Document Filtering\" src=\"../../img/app/feishu_doc_select2.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/feishu_doc.html#1", "title": "1 Feishu Bot Configuration ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/feishu_doc.html#11", "title": "1.1 Create a Feishu Bot ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/feishu_doc.html#12", "title": "1.2 Add Permission ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/feishu_doc.html#13", "title": "1.3 Obtain Required Information ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/feishu_doc.html#14", "title": "1.4 Application Publishing ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/feishu_doc.html#15", "title": "1.5 Group Settings ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/feishu_doc.html#2", "title": "2 Create a Feishu Document Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html", "title": "Login Authentication", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Login Authentication<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"_2\">Login Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB supports configuring the default login method and the account login verification code.</p>\n<p>Login Method: administrators can freely choose and enable the most suitable login method based on the identity authentication strategy and security management requirements of the enterprise.</p>\n<p>Default login method: Administrators can pre-set the system’s default login method according to the enterprise’s unified login policy, such as account-password login or third-party login.</p>\n<p>Account login verification code settings: When a user's consecutive login failures reach the preset threshold, the system automatically triggers the verification code mechanism and the account-lock function after failed logins, effectively preventing security risks such as brute-force attacks.</p>\n<p>Default role assignment for third-party users: the default workspace and role assigned by default to users who log in via third-party accounts, for unified management of third-party users.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Login Setting\" src=\"../../img/system/login_setting.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Login Setting\" src=\"../../img/system/login_setting1.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"_3\">Login Authentication<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports LDAP, CAS, OIDC, OAUTH2, and SAML2 single sign-on authentication protocols, as well as QR-code login and passwordless login on the mobile end for WeCom, DingTalk, and Feishu, meeting enterprises' needs for strong authentication and access control.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Scan the QR code\" src=\"../../img/system/login_auth_view.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"1-ldap\">1 LDAP<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1-ldap\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For the LDAP configuration process, refer to the figure below. Note that this feature is enabled by checking 'Enable LDAP Authentication' below. <br/>\nTip: After the configuration is complete, you can click [Test Connection] above to immediately test whether the configuration information is correct and whether the network is connected.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"LDAP\" src=\"../../img/system/LDAP.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"2-cas\">2 CAS<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2-cas\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For the CAS configuration process, refer to the figure below. Note that this feature is enabled by checking 'Enable CAS Authentication' below. <br/>\n<strong>Note:</strong> The CAS callback address is the MaxKB access address plus /api/cas, for example: <a href=\"http://40.100.86.240:8080/admin/api/cas\">http://40.100.86.240:8080/admin/api/cas</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"CAS\" src=\"../../img/system/CAS.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"3-oidc\">3 OIDC<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3-oidc\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For the OIDC configuration process, refer to the figure below. Note that this feature is enabled by checking 'Enable OIDC Authentication' below. <br/>\n<strong>Note:</strong> The OIDC callback address is the MaxKB access address plus /api/oidc, for example: <a href=\"http://40.100.86.240:8080/admin/api/oidc\">http://40.100.86.240:8080/admin/api/oidc</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"OIDC\" src=\"../../img/system/OIDC.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"4-oauth2\">4 OAUTH2<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4-oauth2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For the OAUTH2 configuration process, refer to the figure below (using Github as the authorization endpoint example). Note that this feature is enabled by checking 'Enable OAHTU2 Authentication' below. <br/>\n<strong>Note:</strong> The OAUTH2 callback address is the MaxKB access address plus /api/oauth2, for example: <a href=\"http://40.100.86.240:8080/admin/api/oauth2\">http://40.100.86.240:8080/admin/api/oauth2</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"OAHTU2\" src=\"../../img/system/oauth2.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"5-saml2\">5 SAML2<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5-saml2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For the SAML2 configuration process, refer to the figure below (using Github as the authorization endpoint example). Note that this feature is enabled by checking 'Enable SAML2 Authentication' below.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"SAML2\" src=\"../../img/system/saml2.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"6\">6 Scan to Log In<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#6\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports WeCom, DingTalk, and Feishu integration, as well as QR-code login and passwordless login.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Scan the QR code\" src=\"../../img/system/scan_code%20_login.png\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"61\">6.1 Connecting WeCom<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#61\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<h5 id=\"611\">6.1.1 WeCom Connection Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#611\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h5>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>To connect MaxKB to WeCom, fill in the following information:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Corp ID: the enterprise ID. Obtained by the WeCom administrator under [Enterprise Information] in the management console.</li>\n<li>Agent ID: the unique ID of the WeCom self-built application, obtained when the WeCom administrator creates or views the application in the management console.</li>\n<li>App Secret: the secret of the WeCom self-built application.</li>\n<li>Callback address: the URL used to access MaxKB.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When configuring WeCom QR-code login for MaxKB, the WeCom administrator needs to log in to <a href=\"https://work.weixin.qq.com/wework_admin/frame\">WeCom Management</a> and create an enterprise self-built application, then publish the application after completing the configuration.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom App Creation\" src=\"../../img/system/qiwei_create_app1.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom App Creation\" src=\"../../img/system/obtain_wxid.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Step 1: Create an application. In [App Management - Apps - Self-Built], click [Create App], enter the application name and other information. Once the app is created, you can view the application's Agent ID and Secret.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom App Creation\" src=\"../../img/system/qiwei_create_app.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom App Information\" src=\"../../img/system/qiwei_appinfo.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Step 2: Set the trusted domain. In [Developer Interface], click [Set Trusted Domain], add a trusted domain, and verify it. See <a href=\"https://kb.fit2cloud.com/?p=915e0151-5581-406f-ac2e-22afb9b3b4bf\"><strong>Trusted Domain Configuration</strong></a>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Set Trusted Domain\" src=\"../../img/system/qiwei_yuming.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Step 3: Authorize the callback domain. In [WeCom Authorization], set the authorization callback domain.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Set Callback Domain\" src=\"../../img/system/qiwei_callback.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Step 3: Configure the enterprise trusted IP. In [Enterprise Trusted IP], configure the trusted IP.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Configure Trusted IP\" src=\"../../img/system/qiwei_ip.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After configuring and publishing the WeCom application, configure the corresponding information on the MaxKB WeCom login QR code configuration page and pass the verification.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/qiwei_setting.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Afterwards, you can click WeCom on the MaxKB login page to log in by scanning the QR code.</p>\n</div>\n<h5 id=\"612\">6.1.2 WeCom Password-Free Login Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#612\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h5>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For constructing the app homepage URL, refer to the WeCom development guide<a href=\"https://developer.work.weixin.qq.com/document/path/91120#%E6%9E%84%E9%80%A0%E4%BC%81%E4%B8%9Aoauth2%E9%93%BE%E6%8E%A5\">Create a web authorization link — construct an enterprise OAuth2 link</a>.<br/>\nThe link format and parameter descriptions are as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Link format: <a href=\"https://open.weixin.qq.com/connect/oauth2/authorize?redirect_uri=REDIRECT_URI/admin/api/wecom/oauth2&amp;response_type=code&amp;scope=snsapi_privateinfo&amp;appid=CorpID&amp;agentid=AgentID&amp;state=maxkb#wechat_redirect\">https://open.weixin.qq.com/connect/oauth2/authorize?redirect_uri=REDIRECT_URI/admin/api/wecom/oauth2&amp;response_type=code&amp;scope=snsapi_privateinfo&amp;appid=CorpID&amp;agentid=AgentID&amp;state=maxkb#wechat_redirect</a></li>\n<li>CORPID: the CorpID of the enterprise</li>\n<li>REDIRECT_URI: the callback link address redirected to after authorization. The link needs to be processed with urlencode, for example: https%3A%2F%2Fmaxkbk.fit2cloud.cn. Just adjust the domain part.</li>\n<li>SCOPE: just fill in snsapi_privateinfo</li>\n<li>AGENTID: the application ID</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Example home page address: <a href=\"https://open.weixin.qq.com/connect/oauth2/authorize?redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fmaxkbk.fit2cloud.cn/admin/api/wecom/oauth2&amp;response_type=code&amp;scope=snsapi_privateinfo&amp;appid=ww5fad05aaa36d118c&amp;agentid=1000002&amp;state=maxkb#wechat_redirect\">https://open.weixin.qq.com/connect/oauth2/authorize?redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fmaxkbk.fit2cloud.cn/admin/api/wecom/oauth2&amp;response_type=code&amp;scope=snsapi_privateinfo&amp;appid=ww5fad05aaa36d118c&amp;agentid=1000002&amp;state=maxkb#wechat_redirect</a></p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/weichat_oauth2.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the configuration is complete, find the MaxKB application in the WeCom workbench and access MaxKB without login.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"WeCom Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/weichat_oauth3.png\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"62\">6.2 Connecting DingTalk<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#62\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<h5 id=\"621\">6.2.1 DingTalk Connection Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#621\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h5>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>To connect MaxKB to DingTalk, fill in the following information:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Corp ID: the DingTalk organization ID; view it in the organization information at the top right of the DingTalk open platform.</li>\n<li>APP Key: the DingTalk application ID; view it under the application's [Credentials and Basic Information] in the DingTalk open platform.</li>\n<li>App Secret: the DingTalk application secret; view it under the application's [Credentials and Basic Information] in the DingTalk open platform.</li>\n<li>Callback address: the URL used to access MaxKB.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When configuring DingTalk QR-code login for MaxKB, you need to create and configure an application in <a href=\"https://open-dev.dingtalk.com/\"><strong>DingTalk Open Platform</strong></a>.</p>\n<p>Step 1: Create an application. In [App Development - DingTalk App], click [Create App]. After the app is created, you can view the APPKey and APPSecret information in [Credentials &amp; Basic Information].</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Create Application\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_app_create.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"DingTalk Application Information\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_app_info.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Step 2: Permission settings.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Go to [Permission Management] and add the permissions shown in the figure below.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Application Information\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_permissions.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>Also add the authorized callback domain in the 【Callback Domain】 under 【Share Settings】, noting that the domain must match the 【Callback Domain】 filled in on the MaxKB platform.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Callback Information\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_url.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>Also add the authorized callback domain in the 【Redirect URL】 under 【Security Settings】, and ensure the domain name is consistent.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Security Information\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_safe.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Step 3: In [Version Management &amp; Publishing], fill in the application version number and version description, then click [Save] to publish the application.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Application Information\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_app_release.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After completing the configuration, publish it, then configure and save it on the MaxKB DingTalk QR code login configuration page.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Create Application\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_setting.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Afterwards, you can click DingTalk on the MaxKB login page to log in by scanning the QR code.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Application Display\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_deplay.jpg\"/></p>\n<h5 id=\"622\">6.2.2 DingTalk Password-Free Login Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#622\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h5>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Add the web application capability. In the 【Application Capability】 of the DingTalk open platform, add 【Web Application】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Create Application\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_add_webapp.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Set [App Home Page] and [PC Home Page URL].</p>\n<p>The address format is: http(s)://xxx.xxx.xxx/admin/login?client=dingtalk=CORPID. Note that corpId=CORPID must be replaced with the actual CORPID.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_webapp_config.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Security Settings. In 【Security Settings】, set the redirect URL and the in-app login-free address.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Security Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_security_config.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Share Settings: in 【Access Login】, set the 【Callback Domain】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Security Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/dingding_share_config.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the app is published, you can access MaxKB from the DingTalk workbench without logging in.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DingTalk Security Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/dingdingview.png\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"63\">6.3 Connecting Feishu<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#63\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<h5 id=\"631\">6.3.1 Feishu Connection Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#631\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h5>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>To connect MaxKB to Feishu, fill in the following information:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>APP Key；</li>\n<li>Corp ID；</li>\n<li>App Secret: the callback address provided by MaxKB, which also serves as the redirect address for Feishu login-free authorization;</li>\n<li>Callback address: the MaxKB URL address plus '/api/feishu', for example: <a href=\"http://xx.xxx.xx.xxx/api/feishu\">http://xx.xxx.xx.xxx/api/feishu</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When configuring Feishu QR-code login for MaxKB, you need to create an enterprise self-built application in <a href=\"https://open.feishu.cn/\"><strong>Lark Open Platform</strong></a>, publish it after completing the configuration, and then configure and save it on the MaxKB Feishu QR-code login configuration page.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Step 1: Create an enterprise self-built application. Click [Create Enterprise Self-Built Application], enter the application name and description, upload an application icon, then click [Create].</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Create\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_create_app.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Feishu Create\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_create_app1.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Step 2: Permission configuration</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Configure the redirect URL. In [Development Configuration - Security Settings], enter the callback address in the MaxKB Feishu QR-code configuration dialog, and click [Add].</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Configure Callback URL\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_url.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>Application authorization: authorize the application in the Permission Management of the application. Refer to the following figure for the specific permissions:</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Application Authorization\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_permissions.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Step 3: Publish the application. In [Version Management &amp; Publishing], enter the application version number and update notes, then click [Save] to complete the application publishing.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Publish Application\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_app_release.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_setting.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After publishing the app, you can click Feishu on the MaxKB login page to log in by scanning the QR code.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Display\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_deplay.jpg\"/></p>\n<h5 id=\"632\">6.3.2 Feishu Password-Free Login Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#632\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h5>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Add the 【Page Application】 capability.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Add Page Application\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_add_webapp.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Configure the desktop home page. For example, enter the desktop home page address in the configuration, such as: http(s)://xxx.xxx.xxx/admin/login?client=lark&amp;appId=cli_a7e1c1ddexxxxx.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Page Application Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_webapp_config.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Add the redirect URL in 【Security Settings】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Security Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_security_config.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the app is published, you can access MaxKB from the Feishu workbench without logging in.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Feishu Security Configuration\" src=\"../../img/system/feishu_view.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#_2", "title": "Login Settings ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#_3", "title": "Login Authentication ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#1-ldap", "title": "1 LDAP ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#2-cas", "title": "2 CAS ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#3-oidc", "title": "3 OIDC ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#4-oauth2", "title": "4 OAUTH2 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#5-saml2", "title": "5 SAML2 ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#6", "title": "6 Scan to Log In ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#61", "title": "6.1 Connecting WeCom ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#611", "title": "6.1.1 WeCom Connection Settings ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#612", "title": "6.1.2 WeCom Password-Free Login Settings ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#62", "title": "6.2 Connecting DingTalk ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#621", "title": "6.2.1 DingTalk Connection Settings ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#622", "title": "6.2.2 DingTalk Password-Free Login Settings ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#63", "title": "6.3 Connecting Feishu ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#631", "title": "6.3.1 Feishu Connection Settings ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/login_auth.html#632", "title": "6.3.2 Feishu Password-Free Login Settings ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/operation_log.html", "title": "System Logs", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">System Logs<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB system administrators can view and export all users' operations on knowledge bases, models, applications, and more under [System Settings - Operation Log] for easy auditing and review.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Supports filtering operation logs by different time periods or a custom time range.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Supports searching by user, status, IP address, and other criteria.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Supports setting a clearing policy, which defaults to 180 days and is customizable.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"operation_log\" src=\"../../img/system/opeartion_log.png\"/><br/>\n<img alt=\"operation_log\" src=\"../../img/system/opeartion_log1.png\"/> </p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/resource_management.html", "title": "Resource Management", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Resource Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Resource Management feature provides system administrators with a unified and efficient way to manage resources visually. System administrators can centrally view, manage, and maintain core resources across all workspaces, including agents, knowledge bases, tools, models, and more.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 View Resources<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports viewing the knowledge base, agent, model, and tool resources of different workspaces:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Resource display: Displays information such as the resource name, type, status, workspace, creator, last published time, and creation time.</li>\n<li>Search filter: Supports querying by creator, name, type, status, and workspace.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Supports keyword search and field filtering for quickly locating resources.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resources\" src=\"../../img/system/resource_management.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Resource Operations<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Administrators can perform specific operations on different types of resources, including but not limited to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Agent</strong>: Supports chat, management, resource authorization, export, deletion, etc.;</li>\n<li><strong>Knowledge Base</strong>: Supports management, vectorization, question generation, configuration settings, resource authorization, exporting as Excel or ZIP, deletion, etc.;</li>\n<li><strong>Tool</strong>: Supports enabling/disabling tools, editing, startup parameters, resource authorization, export, etc.;</li>\n<li><strong>Model</strong>: Supports editing, resource authorization, deletion, etc.;</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resources\" src=\"../../img/system/resource_opt_app.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/resource_management.html#1", "title": "1 View Resources ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/resource_management.html#2", "title": "2 Resource Operations ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/role.html", "title": "Role Management", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Role Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>A role is the identity of a user in the system, used for batch permission management.</p>\n<p>Built-in system roles:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>System Administrator: permission settings for all features in System Management, as well as menu permissions in user information.<ul>\n<li>Can view the permission configurations of all roles (built-in roles and custom roles).</li>\n<li>Can use all features, such as creating or modifying custom role configurations and adding or removing members.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Workspace Administrator: has system administration permission for workspace management, and full functional permissions for agents, knowledge bases, tools, and models.<ul>\n<li>Can view the permission configurations of the Regular User role and custom Regular User roles, but cannot edit permissions.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Regular User: can maintain the resources they create and the resources authorized to them, such as all functional permissions of the agents, knowledge bases, tools, and models they create.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Built-in system roles cannot have their permissions edited; members can only be added/removed.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Role Management\" src=\"../../img/system/role_manage.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Create Role<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Creating a Custom Role:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Role Name: 1-64 characters.</li>\n<li>Inherited roles: System Administrator, Workspace Administrator, and Regular User.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: A System Administrator feature; Workspace Administrators do not have this feature.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"New Role\" src=\"../../img/system/create_role.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2  Permission Configuration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Custom roles are created successfully, and the option to inherit all permissions of a role is unchecked by default. Custom roles can inherit the 3 built-in roles for custom permissions; for example, the permission settings of a custom System Administrator can be edited within the permission scope of the built-in System Administrator.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"New Role\" src=\"../../img/system/create_role_permissions.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Built-in System Administrator Role Permissions:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Role Permissions\" src=\"../../img/system/administrator_permissions.png\" width=\"800px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Built-in Workspace Administrator Role Permissions:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Role Permissions\" src=\"../../img/system/workspace%20_admin_permissions.png\" width=\"800px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Built-in Regular User Role Permissions:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Role Permissions\" src=\"../../img/system/user_permissions.png\" width=\"800px\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Member Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports managing members by role; click [Members] to display the member list of the currently selected role.</p>\n<p>Workspace administrators can see all members under the workspaces where they hold the workspace administrator role.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Member Management\" src=\"../../img/system/role_numberlist.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Add Member:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Add members to the current role. The member dropdown list supports multiple selection.</li>\n<li>When the currently selected role is Workspace Administrator or Regular User, after selecting members during member addition, you also need to select a workspace; the workspace list also supports multiple selection.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: When a Workspace Administrator adds members, the workspace dropdown list only lists workspaces with the Workspace Administrator role.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Member Management\" src=\"../../img/system/add_number.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Remove member:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The role of a user in a workspace. If a user is a member of multiple workspaces, they need to be removed multiple times.</li>\n<li>After a member is removed, they will no longer have the role when logging in to the system.</li>\n<li>The admin user in the built-in System Administrator role cannot be removed.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/role.html#1", "title": "1 Create Role ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/role.html#2", "title": "2 Permission Configuration ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/role.html#3", "title": "3 Member Management ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/shared_resources.html", "title": "Shared Resources", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Shared Resources <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Enterprise Edition supports System Administrators in creating shared resources (knowledge bases, tools, models), which can be authorized to designated workspaces for viewing and use. The Shared Resources page supports editing resources, authorizing applicable workspaces, and viewing associated resources.</p>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Authorized workspaces can see shared resources, but can only view and use them; they cannot edit or delete them.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Shared Resources\" src=\"../../img/system/shared_resources.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Authorizing Workspaces After Creating Resources:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Select whitelist: Allow the selected workspaces to use this shared resource.</li>\n<li>Select blacklist: All workspaces except the selected ones can use this shared resource.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Whitelist is selected by default. If the authorized workspace is empty, no workspace can see this resource. If the user changes the authorization type to blacklist and the authorized workspace is empty, all workspaces can view this resource.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resources\" src=\"../../img/system/authorized_workspace.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Creating a shared knowledge base works the same as creating a knowledge base in a workspace.</p>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: For the Embedding Model, only embedding models of shared models can be selected.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resources\" src=\"../../img/system/shared_knowledgebase0.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Switch to the shared knowledge base list to display all shared knowledge base names; authorized workspaces can view and use the shared knowledge bases.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resources\" src=\"../../img/system/shared_knowledgebase.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The interfaces and features of the shared knowledge base in Documents, Questions, Hit Testing, Chat, and Settings are the same as those of knowledge bases created in a workspace.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resources\" src=\"../../img/system/shared_knowledgebase2.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Tools<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Creating a shared tool works the same as creating a tool in a workspace.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resources\" src=\"../../img/system/shared_tool.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Switch to the shared tool list to display all shared tools; you can also select individual tools and MCPs for creation. Authorized workspaces can view and use the shared tools.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resources\" src=\"../../img/system/shared_tool2.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Creating a shared model works the same as creating a model in a workspace.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resources\" src=\"../../img/system/shared_model.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Switch to the shared model list to display all shared model names; authorized workspaces can view and use the shared models.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resources\" src=\"../../img/system/shared_model2.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/shared_resources.html#1", "title": "1 Overview ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/shared_resources.html#2", "title": "2 Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/shared_resources.html#3", "title": "3 Tools ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/shared_resources.html#4", "title": "4 Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/system_API.html", "title": "System API", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"api\">System API<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#api\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1-api-key\">1 API Key Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1-api-key\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the drop-down menu of the logged-in user icon in the upper-right corner of the page, click the 【API Key Management】 menu to enter the API Key management window, where you can create, enable/disable, delete, and set API Keys.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"API-key\" src=\"../../img/system/apikey.png\"/> </p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>System API Key supports customizing the validity period and cross-origin settings of the API Key, further strengthening the security of API calls and reducing the security risk of key leakage.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Edit API Key\" src=\"../../img/system/edit_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2-api\">2 API Debugging<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2-api\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After opening the API documentation URL, enter the API Key for authorization to debug the API online.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"swagger\" src=\"../../img/system/swagger_api.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Note: When the interface used involves application chat, Authorize must be filled in with the application's API Key (application-0d5722xxxxxxxxx); otherwise, the following error will appear:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"swagger\" src=\"../../img/system/swagger_apinotice.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3-api\">3 Enabling Authenticated API Calls<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3-api\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When authentication is enabled, the Authorize used for API calls is obtained differently from <a href=\"../chat_to_api\">Chatting via API Key</a>; take account login as an example.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Login Authentication\" src=\"../../img/system/api_login.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"31-api\">3.1 Log In API Base URL<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#31-api\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click the user avatar and select 【API Key Management】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Open API Key Management\" src=\"../../img/system/api_open_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Create an API Key, copy it, and open the 【API Service URL】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Open API Documentation\" src=\"../../img/system/api_create_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Authorize】 and enter the system's API Key in 【value】.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Log in to the API Documentation\" src=\"../../img/system/api_login_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"32-authorize\">3.2 Obtaining Authorize<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#32-authorize\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Call the captcha API to obtain a verification code. The returned verification code is Base64-encoded PNG image data.</p>\n<p><strong>Note: You need to decode the Base64 data and convert it into an image file yourself.</strong></p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Log in to the API Documentation\" src=\"../../img/system/api_captcha.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Copy the application's access_token on the application Overview page.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"access_token\" src=\"../../img/system/api_access_token.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>At the API address, find Chat User/Log In, enter the access_token, fill in the account, password, and other information, and generate the login token.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"access_token\" src=\"../../img/system/api_authorize.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"access_token\" src=\"../../img/system/api_authorize1.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"33-api\">3.3 API Invocation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#33-api\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Go to the API documentation address in the application's [Overview], fill the obtained token into [Authorize], and then you can use <a href=\"../chat_to_api\">Chatting via API Key</a> to communicate via the API normally.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"API Login\" src=\"../../img/system/api_login_auth.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"API Login\" src=\"../../img/system/api_login_auth1.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/system_API.html#1-api-key", "title": "1 API Key Management ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/system_API.html#2-api", "title": "2 API Debugging ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/system_API.html#3-api", "title": "3 Enabling Authenticated API Calls ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/system_API.html#31-api", "title": "3.1 Log In API Base URL ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/system_API.html#32-authorize", "title": "3.2 Obtaining Authorize ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/system_API.html#33-api", "title": "3.3 API Invocation ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/theme_settings.html", "title": "Appearance Settings", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Appearance Settings <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>You can configure the system theme color, website logo, login logo, login background image, website name, welcome message, and the display settings for platform information such as User Manual, Forum Support, and Project Address in the upper-right corner of the home page.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Theme Settings\" src=\"../../img/system/theme.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Theme Settings\" src=\"../../img/system/theme2.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/user.html", "title": "User Management", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">User Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 User List<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports a multi-user system; the system administrator can create and manage users.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/userlist.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Create User<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports the system administrator creating users:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Username: the user account information, cannot be modified;</li>\n<li>Name: the user's name;</li>\n<li>Email: The user's email.</li>\n<li>Phone number: the user's phone number;</li>\n<li>Default password: defaults to <code>MaxKB@123..</code>;</li>\n<li>Role Settings:<ul>\n<li>A user can set multiple roles, with at least 1 role set;</li>\n<li>When selecting a regular user and a workspace role, you need to set the workspace.</li>\n<li>There is no workspace option for the System Administrator role.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/create_user.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When the created user is a Regular User or inherits the Regular User role, default permissions can be set, that is, the default permissions for all resources under the selected workspace can be configured.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/create_user1.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Set Role<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select users and click 【Set Role】 to batch-assign roles to users.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Set Role\" src=\"../../img/system/set_user_role.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Editing a User<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The username cannot be edited; other attributes can be edited.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/edit_userinfo.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>If the user status is disabled, the user cannot log in to MaxKB.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/forbid_user.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"5\">5 Reset Password<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>System Administrators can change the password for every user. In the user list, click [Change Password]; the change password dialog pops up, and the change succeeds after saving.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/edit_usermessges.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"6\">6 Delete User<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#6\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the user list, click the 【Delete】 button individually, and a prompt box will appear. After confirmation, only the current user is deleted, without affecting the workspace resources they created. <br/>\n<strong>Note</strong>: the built-in admin user cannot be deleted.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/delete_user.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select users and click the 【Delete】 button; a confirmation dialog will appear. Confirm to batch-delete users without affecting the workspace resources they created.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/delete_user1.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"7\">7 Query User<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#7\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports searching users by username, name, email, status, and user source.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"User List\" src=\"../../img/system/search_user.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/user.html#1", "title": "1 User List ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/user.html#2", "title": "2 Create User ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/user.html#3", "title": "3 Set Role ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/user.html#4", "title": "4 Editing a User ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/user.html#5", "title": "5 Reset Password ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/user.html#6", "title": "6 Delete User ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/user.html#7", "title": "7 Query User ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/workspace.html", "title": "Workspace", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Workspace<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>A workspace is an organizational unit of MaxKB, used for the centralized management of related personnel, resources, roles, and more.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Workspaces are isolated from each other; public resources can be shared through Shared Resources.</li>\n<li>The Enterprise Edition has no limit on the number of workspaces created.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Workspace Management\" src=\"../../img/system/workspace.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Space Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Creating a workspace: open the Create Workspace dialog and fill in the workspace name (required, 1-64 characters, unique and cannot be duplicated).</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Workspace Management\" src=\"../../img/system/%20create_workspace.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Rename workspace: Select the target workspace and click [Rename] to modify it.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Workspace Management\" src=\"../../img/system/rename_workspace.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Deleting a workspace: select the target workspace and click 【Delete】.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A workspace cannot be deleted when it contains resources (knowledge bases, agents, tools, models); it can be deleted when it has no resources.</li>\n<li>The built-in default workspace cannot be deleted, but it can be renamed.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Workspace Management\" src=\"../../img/system/delete_workspace.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Member Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When adding members, you need to select a role; you can add multiple members and multiple roles at the same time.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>System Administrators can add members to all workspaces; Workspace Administrators only see the workspaces where the current user has the Workspace Administrator role.</li>\n<li>The role list for workspace administrators only shows the Regular User role and custom roles that inherit the Regular User role.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Workspace Management\" src=\"../../img/system/create_workspacenumber.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Removing a member: after clicking [Remove], the member's current role is removed.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Workspace Management\" src=\"../../img/system/delete_workspacenumber.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/workspace.html#1", "title": "1 Space Management ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/X-Pack/workspace.html#2", "title": "2 Member Management ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app-view.html", "title": "Agent Overview", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Agent Overview <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After creating an agent, on the Overview page you can enable/disable and regenerate the public access link, run a demo, embed it in third-party sites, set access restrictions, and manage API Keys.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Agent Overview\" src=\"../../img/app/overview.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Public Access Link<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The public access link supports enable/disable settings and regeneration. Click Demo, or copy the public access link into your browser, to enter the Q&amp;A page.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Q&amp;A\" src=\"../../img/app/QA.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Q&amp;A\" src=\"../../img/app/QA_asker.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After chatting, you can click the export button in the upper-right corner to export the current conversation history as Markdown, HTML, or PDF files.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Q&amp;A\" src=\"../../img/app/QA_down.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When exporting to PDF is selected, you can choose to export as PDF or as an image.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Q&amp;A\" src=\"../../img/app/QA_down1.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports copying, regenerating an answer, approving, disapproving, and sharing chat records.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Q&amp;A Sharing\" src=\"../../img/app/QA_share.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For an already-opened public link, if the current public link is disabled or a new public access link is regenerated, accessing it at that time will show the message: Sorry, the service is currently under maintenance and unavailable. Please try again later!</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Stop Service\" src=\"../../img/app/closed.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Third-Party Embedding<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB agents support zero-code embedding into an enterprise's third-party systems.   <br/>\nOn the agent overview page, click [Embed in Third Party], copy the full-screen, mobile, or floating-window mode code, and embed it into the third-party system to conduct Q&amp;A in that system.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Embed in Third-Party\" src=\"../../img/app/embed.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Access Restrictions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB supports setting a per-client question count limit for agents and embedding a third-party whitelist to prevent hotlinking.</p>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Authentication is an X-Pack feature.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Access Restrictions\" src=\"../../img/app/Accessrestrictions.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Display Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Community Edition Agent supports settings for language and for displaying execution details. For more X-Pack feature settings, see: <a href=\"../X-Pack/app_logo_settting.html\">Agent Display</a></p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Access Restrictions\" src=\"../../img/app/display_config.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"5-api\">5 API Access Credentials<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5-api\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>If an external system needs to be invoked via API, you need to view the API documentation and the current agent's API Key. Click 【API Key 】 to open the API Key management dialog, which supports creating, enabling/disabling, and deleting API Keys.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"API key\" src=\"../../img/app/app_apikey.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app-view.html#1", "title": "1 Public Access Link ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app-view.html#2", "title": "2 Third-Party Embedding ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app-view.html#3", "title": "3 Access Restrictions ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app-view.html#4", "title": "4 Display Settings ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app-view.html#5-api", "title": "5 API Access Credentials ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html", "title": "Agent Overview", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Agent Overview <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Feature Overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB provides preconfigured templates and components, enabling you to quickly create a basic Q&amp;A agent or perform advanced orchestration of complex business processes to build a dedicated AI assistant.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Agent Overview\" src=\"../../img/app/create.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>Folder management: Agents are managed through folders. Up to three levels of subfolders can be created under the root directory. Corresponding agents can be created in each level of folder. Folders support resource authorization; regular users can only view authorized folders, and when authorizing a folder, the existing sub-resources under it can also be authorized.</li>\n<li>Status feature: the agent displays 【Unpublished】 or 【Published】 status (the first time an agent is created it is saved as unpublished, which is the unpublished status), as well as the publication time.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Agent Overview\" src=\"../../img/app/applist1.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the agent is created, go to the agent page to view the agent overview and perform related settings and connections.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Agent Overview\" src=\"../../img/app/app_overview.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Agent access and chat users are X-Pack features.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Agent Types<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Simple Agent: provides relatively basic features and setting options, with complete basic functionality that meets most basic Q&amp;A needs; it is suitable when you need to launch an Agent quickly.</p>\n<p>Advanced Agent: Supports users in creating workflows that conform to business logic, including but not limited to judgment components, question optimization, function libraries, and built-in tags, to meet various needs such as question classification and sensitive word retrieval. It is suitable for scenarios that require complex logic and custom workflows.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Simple Agent\" src=\"../../img/app/simple_view.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Advanced Orchestration\" src=\"../../img/app/advanced.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Template Center<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the 【Template Center】, you can select the desired agent. You only need to configure basic parameters such as the model and knowledge base in the orchestration interface to quickly complete the agent's workflow deployment and realize the intelligent implementation of typical business scenarios.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>To enrich template resources and drive the sustainable development of the product ecosystem, MaxKB sincerely invites community users to participate in building the Template Center and share technical achievements;</p>\n<p>Contribution path: Refer to the template development guidelines provided by the official team to develop agent or knowledge base workflow templates for MaxKB;</p>\n<p>Submission method: After development is complete, submit the template to <a href=\"https://github.com/1Panel-dev/MaxKB-toolstore\">GitHub Official Repository</a>. The project team will review it according to the process, and once approved it will be listed on the MaxKB Template Center for all community users to use.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Template Center\" src=\"../../img/app/app_template_center.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Agent Operations<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"41\">4.1 Going to Chat<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#41\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the agent panel, click the Go to Chat button to jump to the chat page.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Chat\" src=\"../../img/app/app_tochat.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Q&amp;A\" src=\"../../img/app/QA_asker.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"42\">4.2 Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#42\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Settings】 on the agent panel to go to the agent settings page and configure the agent.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Agent Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/app_to_setting.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Agent Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/app_setting.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"43\">4.3 Resource Authorization<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#43\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Resource Authorization】 on the agent panel to authorize the application to the corresponding users.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Agent Resource Authorization\" src=\"../../img/app/app_resource.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"44\">4.4 Viewing Related Resources<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#44\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【View Related Resources】 on the agent panel to view the related resources of the agent. You can search by name, creator, and type.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Agent Resource Authorization\" src=\"../../img/app/app_related_resources.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"45\">4.5 Triggers<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#45\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Trigger】 on the agent panel to add a scheduled or event-triggered trigger for the agent.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Trigger\" src=\"../../img/app/add_trigger_app.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Creating a Trigger: click 【Add】 to create a trigger.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Trigger Name: the name of the trigger, used to identify different triggers and their trigger conditions.</li>\n<li>Description: Detailed description of the trigger and usage notes.</li>\n<li>Type:<ul>\n<li>Scheduled Trigger: tasks can be executed monthly, weekly, daily, or at intervals, and can also be triggered based on Cron expressions.</li>\n<li>Event trigger: that is, a Webhook trigger. When you create an event trigger, the system automatically generates a URL and Bearer Token, allowing the caller to send HTTP requests (with the Token in the Header) carrying request parameters to trigger the corresponding workflow.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Task execution: the task executed by the trigger, which requires entering the corresponding parameter content.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create Trigger\" src=\"../../img/app/trigger_app.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Create Trigger\" src=\"../../img/app/webhook_trigger_app.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"46\">4.6 Transfer To<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#46\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Move to】 on the agent panel to move the agent to another folder of agents under the same workspace.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Move To\" src=\"../../img/app/move_app.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"47\">4.7 Copy<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#47\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Copy】 on the agent panel, set the name and description of the copied agent, then save to copy the agent.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Copy\" src=\"../../img/app/copy_app.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"48\">4.8 Export/Import<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#48\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The agent supports export. After export, the file name is: Agent Name <code>.mk</code>.</p>\n<p>For agents of the advanced orchestration type, the exported content includes the parameter settings of all nodes in the workflow and the function contents; the knowledge base and model information selected in workflow nodes are not exported.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Export Agent\" src=\"../../img/app/app_export.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>On the Agent page, click 【Import Agent】 to import an agent file (with the .mk file extension).</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Import\" src=\"../../img/app/app_import.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"49\">4.9 Delete<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#49\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click the 【Delete】 button on the tool panel to delete the agent. After clicking Delete, a confirmation dialog appears; click OK and the agent is deleted.</p>\n<p><strong>Note: After a tool is deleted, it cannot be recovered.</strong></p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Delete\" src=\"../../img/app/del_app.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"5\">5 Batch Select<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click batch selection to select multiple agents for move or delete operations.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Batch Operations\" src=\"../../img/fx/batch_operation_app.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#1", "title": "1 Feature Overview ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#2", "title": "2 Agent Types ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#3", "title": "3 Template Center ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#4", "title": "4 Agent Operations ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#41", "title": "4.1 Going to Chat ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#42", "title": "4.2 Settings ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#43", "title": "4.3 Resource Authorization ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#44", "title": "4.4 Viewing Related Resources ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#45", "title": "4.5 Triggers ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#46", "title": "4.6 Transfer To ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#47", "title": "4.7 Copy ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#48", "title": "4.8 Export/Import ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#49", "title": "4.9 Delete ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/app.html#5", "title": "5 Batch Select ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/hit-testing.html", "title": "Hit Testing", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Hit Testing<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Application Hit Testing feature is a simulated test for user questions in simple configuration applications, used to adjust segment content and related questions to improve the matching of segment content and thus enhance answer quality. Enter a test question and the system searches the knowledge bases associated with the current application based on the retrieval mode, then filters and returns the segments that meet the conditions by similarity and the top-N segments returned. If necessary, you can edit the returned segment content again.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Hit Testing\" src=\"../../img/app/app_hittesting.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/app/log.html", "title": "Chat Log", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Chat Log</h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Chat Log records the Q&amp;A details of all user conversations, including users' feedback on AI answers. Maintenance personnel can further refine the answers by viewing the chat log details and referencing user feedback.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Log Selection Search\" src=\"../../img/app/log_select.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the chat log, you can query by summary or user, and you can also query conversation content from the past 7 days, 30 days, 90 days, the past six months, or a custom time range.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Log Details\" src=\"../../img/app/loglist.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Log Details<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Log Details show the real Q&amp;A scenarios of each user. The user feedback in the conversation can only be viewed, not modified.</p>\n<p>Click the summary in the log list to view the detailed chat content and user feedback.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Cited Segment\" src=\"../../img/app/log_detail.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Operations staff can edit and annotate based on user questions, AI answers, and user feedback, and save the results to the knowledge base to further improve and enhance the effect.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Cited Segment\" src=\"../../img/app/log_details_edit.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Clear Policy<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Application conversation records and attachments uploaded during conversations are kept for 180 days by default. To retain them longer, modify this parameter. After setting the cleanup policy period, the system creates an automatic cleanup task that runs at 0:00 the next day.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Cited Segment\" src=\"../../img/app/clear_log.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Log Export<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports exporting chat logs to view detailed conversation details.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Cited Segment\" src=\"../../img/app/export_log.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/app/log.html#1", "title": "1 Log Details ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/log.html#2", "title": "2 Clear Policy ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/log.html#3", "title": "3 Log Export ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/serialization.html", "title": "Application Export and Import", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Application Export and Import<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Application Export<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Applications support export. After export, the file name is: Application Name.mk.\nFor advanced orchestration applications, the exported content includes the parameter settings of all nodes in the workflow and the function content; the knowledge base and model information selected in process nodes is not exported.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Application Export\" src=\"../../img/app/app_export.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Application Import<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>On the Application page, click 【Import Application】 to import an application file (with the .mk file extension).</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Application Import\" src=\"../../img/app/app_import.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/app/serialization.html#1", "title": "1 Application Export ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/serialization.html#2", "title": "2 Application Import ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/simple_app.html", "title": "Simple Agent Configuration", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Simple Agent Configuration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Create Agent】, enter the agent name and description, select 【Simple Configuration】, and click 【Create】 to enter the simple agent configuration settings page.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Select Agent Type\" src=\"../../img/app/selectAppType.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The agent information is on the left, and the debug preview interface is on the right.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Name: the title and name of the dialog box shown when users ask questions.</li>\n<li>Description: a description of the agent's scenarios and use cases.</li>\n<li>AI Model: a large language model added under [System Settings] - [Model Management].</li>\n<li>System Prompt: the role or identity setting for the large model's responses.</li>\n<li>User Prompt: a detailed description that guides the model to generate specific output. The prompt can reference the parameter output of preceding nodes, such as the retrieval result of a preceding knowledge base retrieval and the question variable of the Start Node.</li>\n<li>Conversation History: the last N messages of the current session are submitted to the LLM. If set to 0, only the current question is submitted to the LLM.</li>\n<li>Long-term memory: After the long-term memory feature is enabled, the system automatically extracts key information such as the user's preferences, background, goals, and rule conventions from the conversation history, and persistently stores it in the database by user.<ul>\n<li>Trigger mechanism: supports setting the memory generation to be triggered by conversation rounds or by time period.</li>\n<li>Usage: in subsequent conversations, administrators can inject the current user's memory content into the system prompt or chat context by referencing the {memory} variable, enabling the agent to continuously understand the user without asking again, effectively improving conversation coherence and the personalized experience.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Knowledge Base:<ul>\n<li>User Prompt: a detailed description that guides the model to generate specific output. The prompt can reference the parameter output of preceding nodes, such as the retrieval result of a preceding knowledge base retrieval and the question variable of the Start Node.</li>\n<li>Associated Knowledge Base: after the user asks a question, segments will be retrieved from the associated knowledge base.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Skills: supports calling MCP, tools, skills, and agents.</li>\n<li>Opening remark: the greeting that pops up when a user opens a conversation. Markdown format is supported; the content after [-] is quick questions, one per line.</li>\n<li>Output reasoning: Configure whether the reasoning process of the large language model is output.</li>\n<li>Voice input: When enabled, questioning by voice is supported, which requires speech recognition model support.</li>\n<li>Voice playback: When enabled, the answer can be played by voice. It can be played through the browser, or you can also select a speech synthesis model.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>After the agent information is set up, click [Save and Publish] for the agent settings to take effect.</strong></p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Agent Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/app_setting.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Agent Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/app_setting1.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Agent Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/app_setting2.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The prompt is a context instruction injected at the start of each conversation, used to establish prerequisite rules such as the model's identity, tone, knowledge boundary, and output format, thereby ensuring accurate, consistent, and controllable responses.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Supported Variables: for example, {data} automatically inserts knowledge base segments, and {question} references the user's question, enabling accurate, controllable, low-hallucination intelligent replies.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Typical Configuration Example</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Role Anchoring: You are a professional data analysis expert, proficient in MySQL database SQL, able to skillfully use the mcp-mysql tool for SQL verification and queries, and able to use the quickchart-server tool to draw charts and conduct in-depth analysis and explanation of the relevant data.</li>\n<li>Output format: Present the answer in a Markdown table and provide a summary of no more than 20 characters at the end.</li>\n<li>Skills: generate and validate SQL, draw charts, and analyze and interpret data</li>\n<li>Style and tone: Keep it friendly and concise, and avoid using technical jargon.</li>\n<li>Restrictions: Answer only content related to generating SQL, using tools for query verification, generating images, and analyzing and interpreting data. Refuse to answer topics that do not involve this content.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>By properly orchestrating prompts, administrators can quickly switch between multiple scenarios and roles without changing models, significantly reducing the risk of large language model hallucination and improving the user experience.</p>\n<p>The Simple Agent's System Prompt supports automatically generating high-quality, well-structured System Prompts based on the topic content entered by the user, helping users quickly build prompt text suitable for the current scenario.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Agent Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/app_prompt.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The opening remark serves the dual purpose of \"self-introduction\" and \"operation guidance\", telling users \"who I am, what I can do, and how to ask\" without any intrusion. A well-designed opening remark can significantly lower the barrier to first-time use and improve follow-up Q&amp;A efficiency.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Supports Markdown, and allows inserting bold text, links, and line breaks.</li>\n<li>Supports using <html_rander>Write HTML code for the tag.</html_rander></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Refer to <a href=\"https://kb.fit2cloud.com/?p=14db4420-5ed4-4e49-b500-c36c36883c2d\">MaxKB Opening Remarks Reference Template (written in HTML)</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Agent Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/opening_remarks.png\" width=\"500px\"/><img alt=\"Agent Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/opening_remarks1.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After a user asks a question, the system first performs segment retrieval in the associated knowledge bases, then injects the matched content into the prompt, and finally hands it to the LLM to generate an answer. Retrieval behavior can be controlled in the agent settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Retrieval Mode</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Vector retrieval: based on vector similarity, suitable for large data volumes and semantic matching scenarios.</li>\n<li>Full-Text Search: based on text similarity, suitable for small data volumes and keyword-matching scenarios.</li>\n<li>Hybrid Retrieval: Enables both vector + full text at the same time, balancing precision and recall, suitable for medium data volumes.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Similarity Threshold: only return paragraphs above the set score (default 0.60), filtering out low-relevance results.</p>\n</li>\n<li>Cited Segments Top-N: controls the maximum number of highly relevant segments submitted to the LLM, preventing the context from becoming too long.</li>\n<li>Maximum cited characters: truncate the selected paragraphs again by characters to ensure the total length does not exceed the set limit (default 5,000 characters).</li>\n<li>Answer policy when there are no citations: allow the LLM to answer based on general knowledge, or specify a unified reply (such as \"No relevant information is available\"), refusing to fabricate.</li>\n<li>Question Optimization Toggle: When enabled, the system first rewrites the user's question into a form more conducive to retrieval, then performs the retrieval, improving the hit rate.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Agent Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/base_parameter_settings.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Output reasoning: When enabled, before generating the final answer, the model first outputs a reasoning process enclosed in tags and then provides the formal reply.</p>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Some models only output a single label and cannot be toggled off for control; the model needs configuration optimization. For example, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Agent Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/ctr_thkpro.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html", "title": "Advanced Agent", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Advanced Agent<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Create】, select 【Advanced Agent】, enter the agent name, and choose a template as needed; then click 【Create】 to enter the workflow orchestration page.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Select Agent Type\" src=\"../../img/app/app_workflow.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Advanced Agent uses a visual workflow to freely combine nodes such as AI models, knowledge bases, business logic, and external tools for debugging and publishing.</p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Nodes on the canvas must be in the workflow; there cannot be isolated nodes outside the flow, otherwise validation will fail during publishing.<br/></li>\n<li>Each node can be renamed according to its purpose; double-click a node name to rename it, but node names cannot be duplicated within the same workflow.<br/></li>\n<li>The downstream node of a connection can reference the output parameters of the upstream node. If the node name changes, you need to re-copy the variable. The parameter reference syntax is <code>{{节点名称.变量名称}}</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>After completing the workflow design, use the canvas control bar in the lower-left corner to make overall adjustments to the canvas, including canvas zoom, node collapse, and one-click workflow optimization.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Default Canvas\" src=\"../../img/app/defult_workflow.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Basic Node<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Each workflow consists of two basic nodes, 【Basic Information】 and 【Start】, and neither can be deleted or duplicated.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Basic Information: used to configure the agent's basic data, including the agent name, agent description, opening remarks, and voice switch. Each agent has only one such node.</li>\n<li>Start: serves as the starting point of workflow execution; all subsequent nodes begin their flow from this node. Each agent has only one such node.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h4 id=\"11\">1.1 Basic Information<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#11\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: The start node of the workflow, unique and the only one, which cannot be deleted or copied. The question entered on the Q&amp;A page will be used as the output parameter {question} of this node. If subsequent nodes need to reference it, you can copy the output parameter or select a variable: <code>开始节点-&gt;用户问题</code>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Base Information\" src=\"../../img/app/start_node.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Long-term memory: After the long-term memory feature is enabled, the system automatically extracts key information such as the user's preferences, background, goals, and rule conventions from the conversation history, and persistently stores it in the database by user.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Trigger mechanism: supports setting the memory generation to be triggered by conversation rounds or by time period.</li>\n<li>Usage: in subsequent conversations, administrators can inject the current user's memory content into the system prompt or chat context by referencing the {memory} variable, enabling the agent to continuously understand the user without asking again, effectively improving conversation coherence and the personalized experience.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Long-term Memory\" src=\"../../img/app/longtime_memory.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>File upload: When enabled, the agent will support uploading documents during chat.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Documents: TXT, MD, DOCX, HTML, CSV, XLSX, XLS, PDF;</li>\n<li>Images: JPG, JPEG, PNG, GIF;</li>\n<li>Audio: MP3, WAV, OGG, ACC, M4A;</li>\n<li>Video: MP4, AVI, MKV, MOV, FLV, WMV;</li>\n<li>Other Files: files with other custom extensions must be parsed manually.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Upload up to 10 files at a time, with each file no larger than 100 MB; the uploaded files can be processed in subsequent nodes. By default, 3 files are allowed, with each file no larger than 50 MB.</p>\n<p>Upload methods: supports two upload methods: local file upload and URL upload.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Start Node - File Upload\" src=\"../../img/app/upload_config.png\" width=\"500px\"/>\n<img alt=\"Start Node - File Upload\" src=\"../../img/app/upload_config1.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>User Input: the necessary information that needs to be provided on the user side at the start of the session, such as job role, model, knowledge base, etc., so that subsequent flows can be designed differently based on different inputs.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The component types for adding parameters to User Input support text box, password box, radio button, checkbox, tab, date, switch, single-row tab, multi-line text box, single-row multi-select card, model, knowledge base, and tree selector.</li>\n<li>Visibility Settings: a new tab specifically for configuring linkage rules.\n     Display Condition: the current parameter is shown only when all / any of the conditions are met; otherwise it is hidden directly.\n     Hide Condition: the current parameter is hidden directly when all / any of the conditions are met; otherwise it is shown normally.</li>\n<li>Each condition uses a fixed three-part dropdown:\n  【Variable Source】 → 【Operator】 → 【Match Value】\n  1. Selectable range of the Variable Source dropdown (strictly limited to avoid circular references):\n     Other user input parameters that are ordered before this parameter and have been fully configured\n  2. Full set of operators:\n     Equals / Not equals / Contains / Does not contain / Is true / Is not true / Greater than / Greater than or equal / Less than / Less than or equal     <br/>\n  3. Cascading Match Value dropdown:\n     If the source parameter is single-select / tree single-select / multi-select: the Match Value dropdown directly displays all configured option labels and option values of that parameter;\n     If the source parameter is a text type: manual input of the matching content is supported, along with the variable reference syntax {{Parameter Name}}</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Start Node - User Input\" src=\"../../img/app/user_input.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>API parameters: parameters that can be configured when accessing the agent via a public access link. After adding API parameters, they will be automatically appended to the public access URL when integrating with third-party systems.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>- 注意：token 字段作为内部字段，不能添加为参数。\n\n</code></pre></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Session variable: the variable remains valid throughout the current chat flow and is used for data transfer between nodes and logical judgment.</li>\n<li>Voice input: When enabled, questions can be input by voice, which requires a speech recognition model.</li>\n<li>Voice playback: When enabled, the answer content will be played as voice. You can use the browser's built-in playback, or use a speech synthesis model for playback.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Chat Variable\" src=\"../../img/app/chat_var.png\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"12\">1.2 Getting Started<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#12\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>It serves as the starting point of workflow execution, and all subsequent nodes flow from this node.</p>\n<p>Global Variables:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Current time {time}: the time of the current conversation.</li>\n<li>Conversation History {history_context}: the chat history of the conversation.</li>\n<li>Chat ID {chat_id}: the conversation identifier.</li>\n<li>Chat User ID {chat_user_id}: the chat user identifier.</li>\n<li>Chat User Type {chat_user_type}: the chat user type.</li>\n<li>Chat User Group {chat_user_group}: the chat user group.</li>\n<li>Chat User {chat_user}: the default chat user is a guest. Based on the chat user name, further logical decisions can also be made in the workflow.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Session Variable:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Session variable name {session variable parameter}: the session variable created in Basic Information.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>User Question {question}: the question information entered by the client.\nOther parameter outputs: if file upload is enabled, the output parameters may also include:</li>\n<li>Document {document}: The document file uploaded by the client.</li>\n<li>Image{image}: the image file uploaded by the client.</li>\n<li>Audio {audio}: The audio file uploaded by the client.</li>\n<li>Video{video}: the video file uploaded by the client.</li>\n<li>Other Files {other}: other files uploaded by the client.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Start Node\" src=\"../../img/app/app_start.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Add Component】 in the upper right corner of the canvas to add the required nodes to the workflow by clicking or dragging. Components are divided into three major categories by function, described as follows:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Basic</strong>: Covers AI capabilities, knowledge bases, business logic, etc.</li>\n<li><strong>Tool</strong>: Handles complex requirements flexibly through functions.</li>\n<li><strong>Agent</strong>: One-click import of other published agents as sub-flows, directly reusing their Q&amp;A results to achieve rapid assembly and capability reuse.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Orchestration Canvas\" src=\"../../img/app/workflow.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Basic Components<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"21-ai\">2.1 AI Capabilities<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#21-ai\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<h4 id=\"211-ai\">2.1.1 AI Chat<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#211-ai\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: If the Agent needs to chat with an AI model, an AI Chat component needs to be added to the orchestration.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>AI Model: supports referencing a variable or selecting a custom model; the referenced variable source is the model parameter added in the user input.</li>\n<li>System Prompt: the role or identity setting for the large model's responses.</li>\n<li>User Prompt: a detailed description that guides the model to generate specific output. The prompt can reference the parameter output of preceding nodes, such as the retrieval result of a preceding knowledge base retrieval and the question variable of the Start Node.</li>\n<li>\n<p>Conversation History: the content of historical sessions related to the current conversation. For example, if Conversation History is set to 1, the current question and the content of the previous conversation are sent to the LLM together.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Select node: Uses the prompt information of the current AI chat node and the content returned by the node as context.</li>\n<li>Select workflow: Uses the user's question entered in the dialog and the content of the final reply as context.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Vision: The AI Chat node of the Advanced Agent fully supports multimodal input. During the conversation, users can simultaneously input text, images, and other forms of content, and the model will integrate the multimodal information for understanding and answering.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Default state: the feature is disabled; the node runs only on pure-text LLM logic, with no multimodal parsing capability;</li>\n<li>When enabled: images and videos can be uploaded in the conversation, and the node switches to multimodal model execution logic.</li>\n<li>Note: If the vision feature is enabled but the selected model does not support multimodal capabilities, an error will be triggered when the workflow runs. Please make sure to use a multimodal large model.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Skills: agents support automatically calling MCP, tools, Skills, and other agents, and you can choose whether to output the execution process of the skill.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>MCP: supports adding multiple MCPs. MCPs can be invoked in two ways: by referencing an MCP or by configuring a custom MCP Server Config. The large language model will proactively call the appropriate tool based on the prompt content.</li>\n<li>Tool: Custom tools can be flexibly selected based on actual scenarios. The system automatically encapsulates tool capabilities as MCP services and connects them to models, allowing AI to intelligently determine whether to call tools based on the conversation context.</li>\n<li>Skills: supports autonomously analyzing the need and matching the appropriate Skill based on the user's question intent, automatically triggering Skill execution.</li>\n<li>Agent: you can add other agents to directly and quickly call the Q&amp;A results of a sub-agent.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Output reasoning: Settings for enabling the model's reasoning feedback. The default start and end tags are <code>&lt;think&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;/think&gt;</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>Return content: Whether to display the content returned by this node in the conversation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output: you can choose whether to display the exception capture parameter.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Answer content {answer}: the content returned by the large language model based on the role, prompt, and other settings.</li>\n<li>Thinking process {reasoning_content}: the thinking process of the AI model.</li>\n<li>Conversation History {history_message}: outputs the corresponding conversation history according to the configured number of history messages.</li>\n<li>Exception message {exception_message}: supports configuring a dedicated execution flow for exception branches, such as automatic retries or falling back to default values.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Calling MCP tools requires the large language model to support function calling; if it does not, the configuration is invalid.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"AI Chat\" src=\"../../img/app/ai_chat.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The prompt is a context instruction injected at the start of each conversation, used to establish prerequisite rules such as the model's identity, tone, knowledge boundary, and output format, thereby ensuring accurate, consistent, and controllable responses.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Supported Variables: for example, {data} automatically inserts knowledge base segments, and {question} references the user's question, enabling accurate, controllable, low-hallucination intelligent replies.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The AI Chat Node can automatically generate high-quality, well-structured system prompts based on the topic content of the user's input, helping users quickly build prompt text suitable for the current scenario. By properly orchestrating prompts, administrators can quickly switch among multiple scenarios and roles without changing the model, significantly reducing the risk of LLM hallucination and improving the user experience.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Agent Settings\" src=\"../../img/app/ai_chat_prompt.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MCP: reference an MCP and a custom MCP Server Config.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"AI Chat MCP\" src=\"../../img/app/ai_chat_MCP.png\" width=\"500px\"/>\n<img alt=\"AI Chat Custom\" src=\"../../img/app/ai_chat_config.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Tool: Supports adding tools that have been enabled under Tool.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"AI Chat Tool\" src=\"../../img/app/ai_chat_new_tool.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Skills: supports adding Skills that have been enabled in [Tools].</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"AI Chat Skill\" src=\"../../img/app/ai_chat_skills.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Agent: supports adding other already created agents.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"AI Chat Agent\" src=\"../../img/app/ai_chat_agent.png\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"212\">2.1.2 Intent Recognition<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#212\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Classify and recognize the intent based on the input.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>AI Model: the name and parameter controls of the large language model.</li>\n<li>Input: The content to be used for intent recognition.</li>\n<li>Conversation History: the content of historical sessions related to the current conversation. For example, if Conversation History is set to 1, the current question and the content of the previous conversation are sent to the LLM together.</li>\n<li>Intent category: the name of each intent category.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Category {category}: the category name returned based on the type of intent classification.</li>\n<li>Reason {reason}: the reason for judging the intent classification.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"IntentNode\" src=\"../../img/app/intent_classification.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"213\">2.1.3 Text-to-Speech<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#213\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Convert text to audio.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Speech Synthesis Model: select the name of an available speech synthesis model.</li>\n<li>Text content: Select the text content to be synthesized.</li>\n<li>Return content: Whether to display the content returned by this node in the conversation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Result {result}: the audio content converted from the text.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"TTS\" src=\"../../img/app/text2audio.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"214\">2.1.4 Speech-to-Text<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#214\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Convert audio files to text.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Speech Recognition Model: select the name of a speech recognition model.</li>\n<li>Voice file: the uploaded audio file. Supported formats include: mp3, wav, ogg, acc.</li>\n<li>Return content: Whether to display the content returned by this node in the conversation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Result {result}: the text content after speech conversion.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Speech2Text\" src=\"../../img/app/audio2text.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"215\">2.1.5 Image Generation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#215\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Generate the corresponding image based on the text description.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Image generation model: the name of the image generation model.</li>\n<li>Prompt (positive): Text input that guides the model to generate positive, constructive output.</li>\n<li>Prompt (negative): A description of the elements, topics, or features that should not be included in the generated output.</li>\n<li>Return content: Whether to display the content returned by this node in the conversation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>AI Answer Content {answer}: the image generated by the image generation model based on the text input.</li>\n<li>Image {image}: detailed information about the generated image.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Image Generation\" src=\"../../img/app/vision_gen.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"216\">2.1.6 Image Understanding<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#216\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Analyze and understand image files uploaded by the user.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Image understanding model: the name of the image understanding model.</li>\n<li>Role Setting: the role or identity setting for the response.</li>\n<li>Prompt: A detailed description that guides the model to generate specific output.</li>\n<li>\n<p>Conversation history: historical session content related to the current conversation.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Select node: Uses the prompt information of the current image understanding node and the content returned by the node as context.</li>\n<li>Select workflow: Uses the user's question entered in the dialog and the content of the final reply as context.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Select image: The image to be understood and analyzed. You can select a user-uploaded image file or a URL address.</p>\n</li>\n<li>Return content: Whether to display the content returned by this node in the conversation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>AI Answer Content {answer}: the content returned by the image understanding model based on the uploaded image and information such as the role and prompt.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Image Understanding\" src=\"../../img/app/picture_extract.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"217\">2.1.7 Text-to-Video<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#217\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Generate the corresponding video based on the text description.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Text-to-Video Model: select the name of the text-to-video model.</li>\n<li>Prompt (positive): Text input that guides the model to generate positive, constructive output.</li>\n<li>Prompt (negative): A description of the elements, topics, or features that should not be included in the generated output.</li>\n<li>Return content: Whether to display the content returned by this node in the conversation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Video {video}: the video content generated from the text.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Speech2Text\" src=\"../../img/app/text2video.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"218\">2.1.8 Image-to-Video<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#218\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Generate the corresponding video based on the image.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Image-to-video model: select the name of the image-to-video model.</li>\n<li>Prompt (positive): Text input that guides the model to generate positive, constructive output.</li>\n<li>Prompt (negative): A description of the elements, topics, or features that should not be included in the generated output.</li>\n<li>First Frame Image: required, the image from which the video will be generated. You can choose a user-uploaded image file or a URL address.</li>\n<li>End frame image: optional. The image used as the end frame of an image-to-video, which can standardize the generation of the video.</li>\n<li>Return content: Whether to display the content returned by this node in the conversation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Video {video}: the video content generated from the image.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Image-to-Video\" src=\"../../img/app/picture2video.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"219\">2.1.9 Video Understanding<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#219\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Analyze and understand video files uploaded by the user.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Vision Model: the name of the vision model.</li>\n<li>System Prompt: the role or identity setting for the large model's responses.</li>\n<li>User Prompt: a detailed description that guides the model to generate specific output. The prompt can reference the parameter output of preceding nodes, such as the retrieval result of a preceding knowledge base retrieval and the question variable of the Start Node.</li>\n<li>\n<p>Conversation history: historical session content related to the current conversation.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Select node: Uses the prompt information of the current video understanding node and the content returned by the node as context.</li>\n<li>Select workflow: Uses the user's question entered in the dialog and the content of the final reply as context.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Select video: The video to be understood and analyzed. You can select a user-uploaded video file or a URL address.</p>\n</li>\n<li>Return content: Whether to display the content returned by this node in the conversation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>AI Answer Content {answer}: the content returned by the vision model based on the uploaded video and information such as the role and prompt.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Video Understanding\" src=\"../../img/app/video_extract.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"2110\">2.1.10 Question Optimization<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2110\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Intelligently optimize the current question based on the conversation history of the current session, as well as the large language model and prompt set in the node settings.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>AI Model: the name and parameter controls of the large language model.</li>\n<li>Role Setting: the role or identity setting used by the large language model for responses.</li>\n<li>Prompt: A detailed description that guides the model to generate specific output.</li>\n<li>Conversation History: the content of historical sessions related to the current conversation. For example, if Conversation History is set to 1, the current question and the content of the previous conversation are sent to the LLM together.</li>\n<li>Return content: Whether to display the content returned by this node in the conversation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Question optimization result {answer}: The question optimized by the large model.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Question Optimization\" src=\"../../img/app/question_opt.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"22\">2.2 Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#22\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<h4 id=\"221\">2.2.1 Knowledge Base Retrieval<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#221\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: If the Agent needs to be linked to a knowledge base, a Knowledge Base Retrieval node needs to be added to the orchestration, and then select the knowledge base, set the retrieval parameters, and select the question to retrieve.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Retrieval scope: the scope of the knowledge base or list of knowledge bases to be retrieved.<ul>\n<li>Manual: add an associated knowledge base.</li>\n<li>Reference variable: select an existing \"Knowledge Base List\" or \"Document List\" variable in the workflow.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Retrieval parameters: include the retrieval mode, similarity threshold, the number of cited segments, and the maximum cited characters.</li>\n<li>Retrieval question: generally the user question from the Start Node.</li>\n<li>Show results in knowledge sources: off by default; when enabled, the knowledge source can be shown in the answer results.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The segment list of the retrieval result {paragraph_list}: an array type that refers to the list of segments hit after retrieving according to the retrieval question and retrieval parameters, containing all attributes of the segments;</li>\n<li>Segment list that satisfies direct answers {is_hit_handling_method_list}: array type, referring to the list of all segments that satisfy direct answers among the segments hit after retrieval based on the query question and retrieval parameters, including all attributes of the segments;</li>\n<li>Retrieval result {data}: a string type that refers to the segment content hit after retrieving according to the retrieval question and retrieval parameters;</li>\n<li>Segment content that satisfies direct answers {directly_return}: string type, referring to all segment content that satisfies direct answers among the segments hit after retrieval based on the query question and retrieval parameters.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Knowledge Retrieval\" src=\"../../img/app/dataset_search.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"222\">2.2.2 Document Tag Retrieval<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#222\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Retrieve documents that meet the criteria based on the configured document tag filter conditions.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Retrieval scope: the scope of the knowledge base or list of knowledge bases to be retrieved.<ul>\n<li>Manual: add an associated knowledge base.</li>\n<li>Reference variable: select an existing \"Knowledge Base List\" or \"Document List\" variable in the workflow.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Retrieval Settings:<ul>\n<li>Automatic: When a retrieval question is selected, the system automatically matches document tags based on the question.</li>\n<li>Manual: add tag conditions as filters; you need to add the corresponding tag content.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Knowledge Base List {knowledge_list}: array type, refers to the list of knowledge bases that match the tag condition.</li>\n<li>Document List {document_list}: An array type referring to the list of documents matching the tag condition.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Document Tag Retrieval\" src=\"../../img/app/doc_tag_search.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>This node works with the [Knowledge Base Retrieval] node to retrieve segmented content, further narrowing the retrieval scope and making the retrieval results more accurate.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Document Tag Retrieval\" src=\"../../img/app/doc_tag_replay.png\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"223\">2.2.3 Multi-Path Recall<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#223\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Perform multi-path recall based on the content to be reranked, the retrieval question, and the retrieval parameters.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Rerank content: The multiple pieces of content to be reranked, generally the retrieval results from several different knowledge bases.</li>\n<li>Retrieval parameters: include the score threshold, the number of cited segments, and the maximum cited characters.</li>\n<li>Retrieval question: rerank according to the retrieval question, generally the user question or the result after question optimization.</li>\n<li>Rerank model: The name of the rerank model to use.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Rerank result list {result_list}: Array type, referring to the list of reranked results.</li>\n<li>Rerank result {result}: String type, referring to the rerank result based on the retrieval parameters.</li>\n<li>Segment list that satisfies direct answers {is_hit_handling_method_list}: array type, referring to the retrieval list based on the retrieval parameters.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Multi-path Recall\" src=\"../../img/app/rerank.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"23\">2.3 Business Logic<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#23\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<h4 id=\"231\">2.3.1 Judger<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#231\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Perform logical judgment based on different conditions. Each branch must have a subsequent execution node.</p>\n<p>Judger Node output parameter description:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Branch name{branch_name}: the name of each judgment branch.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Conditional Branch\" src=\"../../img/app/condition_statement.png\" width=\"450px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"232\">2.3.2 Form Collection<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#232\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Actively obtain necessary information in a guided way through form design, suitable for scenarios where the Agent needs to ask multiple questions.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Form output content: the form prompt description and the form content. You can input a single item or multiple items of information.</li>\n<li>Form Configuration: design the form by adding different components.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>All form content {form_data}: all the content of the form.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>All form content will be output as a fixed output, and each form item is also output as a parameter.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Form Input\" src=\"../../img/app/form.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The component types for adding form parameters include single-line text box, multi-line text box, JSON text box, password box, radio button, checkbox, tab, single-line tab, single-line multi-select card, slider, switch, date, file upload, model, knowledge base, and tree selector.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"File Upload\" src=\"../../img/app/form_fileup.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Form parameters support referencing variables or parameter input:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When the component type is [Radio, Checkbox, Tabs, Single-line Tabs, Single-line Multi-select, JSON Text Box], the assignment method can be set to Custom or Reference Variable; the default is Custom. For the format of referencing a variable, refer to the tooltip next to [Reference Variable].</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Parameter Format\" src=\"../../img/app/form_parameters_format.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>The default values of the 【Text Box, Multi-line Text Box, Password Box】 components support parameter input. For the parameter format, refer to: {{开始.question}}</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Parameter Input\" src=\"../../img/app/input_parameter.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>【Show/Hide Settings】You can dynamically control whether the current parameter is displayed or hidden based on the values of input parameters earlier in this form, global/session variables, and output variables of preceding nodes.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Parameter Input\" src=\"../../img/app/show_hide.png\" width=\"500px\"/> </p>\n<h4 id=\"233\">2.3.3 Specified Reply<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#233\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Specify the output text content. When the relevant content retrieved from the knowledge base meets the requirements for a direct answer, the retrieved content can be output; when no related content is retrieved from the knowledge base, a reply content can be specified.</p>\n<p>Output parameters:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Content{answer}: specifies the content of the reply output.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Specified Reply\" src=\"../../img/app/direct_reply.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"234\">2.3.4 Loop Node<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#234\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Repeatedly execute a task sequence until specific conditions are met, by setting the loop type and loop body. After adding a loop node, a loop node and its corresponding loop body canvas are generated.</p>\n<p>Loop type: the loop type is the running mode of the loop node, supporting Array Loop, Fixed-Count Loop, and Infinite Loop.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Array loop: A data-driven loop based on arrays, supports traversing each element in the array to execute tasks in sequence, suitable for scenarios of batch processing by data volume;<ul>\n<li>Loop array: select the array content to iterate over.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Fixed-Count Loop: the loop runs a preset fixed number of times. Users can directly set the specific number of times a task repeats (e.g., 5 or 10 iterations), which meets the requirement of \"repeated operations with a specific count\".<ul>\n<li>Loop count: sets the number of iterations; if it is less than 1, it is set to 1.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Infinite Loop: there is no fixed termination condition. The task keeps repeating until the stop condition is met. By default, the maximum number of loops is 500. It is suitable for scenarios that \"require long-term running and waiting for a specific event to be triggered.\"</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Circular Array\" src=\"../../img/app/loop_array.png\" width=\"300px\"/>\n<img alt=\"Loop Number\" src=\"../../img/app/loop_count.png\" width=\"300px\"/>\n<img alt=\"Infinite Loop\" src=\"../../img/app/loop_infinite.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Output parameters: The loop variable set in [Loop Start] within the loop body can serve as the output parameter of the loop node for use by each workflow node.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Output Parameters\" src=\"../../img/app/loop_output.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Loop body: the loop body canvas is used to orchestrate the loop logic. On each iteration, the workflow executes the workflow in the loop body canvas.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Loop\" src=\"../../img/app/loop.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Loop Start</strong>: Acts as the starting point of loop execution; all subsequent nodes in the loop body start flowing from this node.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Loop variable: loop variables can be set in the loop body and apply to each iteration. Loop variables are usually used together with variable assignment: after each iteration, a new value is set for an intermediate variable, and the new value is used in the next iteration. The loop variable can be used as an output parameter of the loop node and be called by nodes in the workflow outside the loop body.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Loop variable: the loop variable added in [Node Settings] can be referenced in the loop body.</p>\n<p>Output parameters:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Subscript {index}: the position of the element in the array. Indexing starts at 0, meaning the first loop; 1 means the second loop; 2 means the third loop; and so on. The index of the last loop is n-1, where n is the number of loops.</li>\n<li>\n<p>Loop item {item}: a single piece of data in the array. An array consists of multiple items, and each item can be a data type such as a number, character, or string.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>例如：数组 array=[23,26,37,88,90]，array[0]的 index 是 0，item 为 23； array[4]的 index 是 4，item 为 90。\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Loop Start\" src=\"../../img/app/loop_begins.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Continue</strong>: Used to terminate the current loop and execute the next loop.</p>\n<p>Add Condition: Add a condition to terminate the current loop; when the condition is met, terminate the current loop and proceed to the next loop.</p>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Continue cannot be used as the End Node.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Loop continue\" src=\"../../img/app/continue.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Break</strong>: Terminates the current loop and exits the loop body.</p>\n<p>Add Condition: Add a condition to terminate the current loop; when the condition is met, terminate the current loop, break out of the loop body, and continue the workflow.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Loop break\" src=\"../../img/app/break.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Note</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Loop nodes cannot be added inside the loop body, to avoid infinite loops;</li>\n<li>When the loop type is Infinite Loop, the default maximum is 1000 iterations. To modify the configuration parameter, you need to edit the ${MAXKB_BASE}/maxkb/.env file (default: /opt/maxkb/.env), and after making the changes, run the <code>mkctl reload</code> command to reload the configuration file.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"24\">2.4 Data Processing<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#24\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<h4 id=\"241\">2.4.1 Variable Assignment<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#241\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Update the value of a global variable.</p>\n<p>Variable: the target global variable to be assigned.</p>\n<p>Assignment: Content for assigning values to variables. You can reference variables, customize, or set the value to empty.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Variable Assign\" src=\"../../img/app/reset_var.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"242\">2.4.2 Variable Aggregation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#242\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Integrate multiple variables into one parameter for output.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Aggregation strategy:<ul>\n<li>Return the first non-empty value of each group: Take the first non-empty item of each group as the group result and discard the rest.</li>\n<li>Return an array (Array) of each group of variables: Assemble all variables in the same group by field name and output the complete structure.</li>\n<li>Return a dictionary (Dict) of each group of variables: Assemble all variables in the same group as a dictionary type. You need to enter the Key value.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Group: add variables that need to be aggregated into the same parameter. The group name can be modified, and multiple groups can be added.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Output parameters:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Display Name {Variable}: the aggregated parameter name, updated with the aggregated variable.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Variable Aggregation\" src=\"../../img/app/aggregate_var.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The main function of variable aggregation is to combine multiple variables into a single parameter for output, reducing the complexity of variable passing in the workflow.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Variable Aggregation\" src=\"../../img/app/aggregate_var1.png\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"243\">2.4.3 Variable Split<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#243\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Use JSON Path expressions to split the input JSON variable into multiple independent variables at once.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Input variable: Select the JSON variable in the workflow to be split.</li>\n<li>Split variables: set the variable name, display name, and JSON Path expression after splitting. Reference format of the JSON Path expression: <code>$.store.book</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Output parameters:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Result{result}: outputs the content of all split variables.</li>\n<li>Display Name {Split Variable}: the content of a single split variable, updated with the split variable.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Variable Splitting\" src=\"../../img/app/split_var.png\" width=\"300px\"/>\n<img alt=\"Variable Splitting\" src=\"../../img/app/split_var1.png\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"244\">2.4.4 Parameter Extraction<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#244\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Extract structured parameters from unstructured or semi-structured text.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>AI Model: a large language model used to extract structured parameters.</li>\n<li>Input variable: Structured text or unstructured text.</li>\n<li>Extraction parameter: Set the extraction parameter, display name, parameter type, and description.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Output parameters:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Result{result}: outputs the content of all extracted parameters.</li>\n<li>Extraction Parameter {parameter name}: The content of a single extraction parameter, updated as the extraction parameter changes.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Parameter Extraction\" src=\"../../img/app/parameter_extraction.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Parameter extraction mainly uses AI models to extract structured parameters from unstructured or semi-structured text. For example, when processing contract documents, you can use it to automatically extract key parameters such as \"signing date\", \"contract amount\", and \"service content\".</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Parameter Extraction\" src=\"../../img/app/parameter_extraction1.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"25\">2.5 Others<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#25\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<h4 id=\"251-mcp\">2.5.1 MCP Call<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#251-mcp\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Call tools in the MCP service via the SSE/Streamable_HTTP protocol.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>MCP Server Config: supports referencing an MCP and also supports custom MCP services (fill in the MCP Server configuration parameters in JSON format).</li>\n<li>Tool: the tool list under the corresponding MCP Server.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Tool Parameters: the request parameters corresponding to the MCP tool, which can be customized or reference variables.</p>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Result {result}: the result returned by the MCP tool execution.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"MCP Node\" src=\"../../img/app/mcp.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>MCP Server Config 格式参考如下\n\n{\n\n    \"amap-maps\": {\n\n      \"url\": \"http://IP:端口/MCPserver名称\",\n\n      \"transport\":\"sse\"               # 如果使用 Streamable_HTTP 协议，需将\"sse\"替换成\"streamable_http\"\n\n    }\n\n}\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<h4 id=\"252\">2.5.2 Document Content Extraction<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#252\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Node Description: Summarize the content of documents uploaded by the user.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Select document: This is the user-uploaded document. You need to enable file upload support in the Basic Information node.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Document Output {content}: a summary output of the user-uploaded file.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Document Content Extraction\" src=\"../../img/app/doc_extract.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"253\">2.5.3 Custom Tools<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#253\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the advanced orchestration workflow, you can write Python code and add parameters to create a tool as a processing node in the workflow to flexibly handle complex requirements. Custom tools are created the same way as tools; for detailed instructions, see: <a href=\"../tool/tool#2\">Tool</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Add Function\" src=\"../../img/app/app_function.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"26\">2.6 Tools<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#26\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the advanced orchestration workflow, you can add tools from Tool as component nodes to flexibly handle complex requirements. For detailed instructions on creating tools, see: <a href=\"../tool/tool\">Tool</a>.</p>\n<p>Node Settings: i.e., the input parameters of the tool.</p>\n<p>Parameter Output: the return result of the tool.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Add Function\" src=\"../../img/app/app_function2.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"27\">2.7 Agent<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#27\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the advanced orchestration workflow, you can add other agents (Simple Agent and workflow orchestration agents) as a processing node in the workflow, directly and quickly leveraging the Q&amp;A results of the sub-agents.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>User Question: the question information for the sub-agent.</li>\n<li>Return content: After enabling, the sub-agent's return result is included in the conversation.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Parameter Output:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Result: that is, the return result of the sub-Agent.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Add Function\" src=\"../../img/app/app_subapp.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Other Notes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"31\">3.1 Execution Conditions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#31\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB workflows support multiple outputs and multiple inputs. In this case, the aggregation node can choose the execution condition based on its logical relationship with the preceding nodes.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>All: the current node can be executed only after all preceding connected nodes have completed execution.</li>\n<li>Any: as long as any preceding connected node completes execution, the current node can be executed.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Execution Condition\" src=\"../../img/app/node_condition.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"32\">3.2 Disabling/Enabling<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#32\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The agent orchestration canvas supports the node disable/enable feature. Without deleting nodes, users can temporarily disable specific nodes to debug the flow or mask part of the logic, greatly improving workflow debugging efficiency and orchestration flexibility.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Disabled nodes and their subsequent nodes will not be executed; after they are re-enabled, they will execute normally.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Disable/Enable\" src=\"../../img/app/on_off.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"33\">3.3 Debugging<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#33\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After completing all the orchestration design, click [Debug] to first verify whether the workflow is compliant. After the verification passes, you can test the conversation on the current page.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Debug Preview\" src=\"../../img/app/workflow_view.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Ask questions in the debug dialog. After the AI finishes answering, 【Execution Details】 will be displayed. Click 【Execution Details】, and in the execution details dialog that pops up, you can view the execution status, time consumption, and other execution information of each workflow node.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Execution Details\" src=\"../../img/app/exec_detail.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"34\">3.4 Release History<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#34\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In agent advanced orchestration, you can view the workflow, time, and user of published historical versions.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Release History\" src=\"../../img/app/public_history.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The agent supports editing the name of a historical published version. The default publish name is the time of publication, and the workflow of historical versions can also be restored.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Release History\" src=\"../../img/app/public_history_edit.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"35\">3.5 Auto Save<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#35\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Advanced orchestration flows are saved manually by default, and can also be set to auto-save. Once auto-save is enabled, the flow is saved locally every 1 minute, and after a successful publish the configuration is synced to the backend database.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Auto Save\" src=\"../../img/app/auto_save.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"36\">3.6 Publishing<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#36\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After clicking 【Publish】, the system first checks whether the current workflow conforms to the rules; if it does, it will be published successfully, otherwise the publish fails. Only after a successful publish do all node configuration changes take effect on the Q&amp;A page.</p>\n<p>You can click 【Go to Chat】 to ask AI questions, and you can also view the publish history and restore versions.</p>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#1", "title": "1 Basic Node ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#11", "title": "1.1 Basic Information ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#12", "title": "1.2 Getting Started ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#2", "title": "2 Basic Components ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#21-ai", "title": "2.1 AI Capabilities ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#211-ai", "title": "2.1.1 AI Chat ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#212", "title": "2.1.2 Intent Recognition ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#213", "title": "2.1.3 Text-to-Speech ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#214", "title": "2.1.4 Speech-to-Text ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#215", "title": "2.1.5 Image Generation ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#216", "title": "2.1.6 Image Understanding ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#217", "title": "2.1.7 Text-to-Video ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#218", "title": "2.1.8 Image-to-Video ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#219", "title": "2.1.9 Video Understanding ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#2110", "title": "2.1.10 Question Optimization ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#22", "title": "2.2 Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#221", "title": "2.2.1 Knowledge Base Retrieval ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#222", "title": "2.2.2 Document Tag Retrieval ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#223", "title": "2.2.3 Multi-Path Recall ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#23", "title": "2.3 Business Logic ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#231", "title": "2.3.1 Judger ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#232", "title": "2.3.2 Form Collection ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#233", "title": "2.3.3 Specified Reply ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#234", "title": "2.3.4 Loop Node ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#24", "title": "2.4 Data Processing ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#241", "title": "2.4.1 Variable Assignment ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#242", "title": "2.4.2 Variable Aggregation ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#243", "title": "2.4.3 Variable Split ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#244", "title": "2.4.4 Parameter Extraction ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#25", "title": "2.5 Others ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#251-mcp", "title": "2.5.1 MCP Call ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#252", "title": "2.5.2 Document Content Extraction ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#253", "title": "2.5.3 Custom Tools ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#26", "title": "2.6 Tools ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#27", "title": "2.7 Agent ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#3", "title": "3 Other Notes ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#31", "title": "3.1 Execution Conditions ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#32", "title": "3.2 Disabling/Enabling ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#33", "title": "3.3 Debugging ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#34", "title": "3.4 Release History ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#35", "title": "3.5 Auto Save ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/app/workflow_app.html#36", "title": "3.6 Publishing ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html", "title": "Knowledge Base", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>An enterprise-owned professional knowledge base containing various types of data. It supports creating and managing knowledge bases, providing a source of knowledge for Q&amp;A conversations and powering intelligent Q&amp;A.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Shared knowledge base: after the System Administrator creates a share in [Shared Resources], it can be authorized to specified workspaces.</li>\n<li>All knowledge bases: users can create knowledge bases. Other users can view, use, and maintain them after <a href=\"../X-Pack/authorization_resources.html\"><strong>Resource Authorization</strong></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Knowledge bases are managed through folders. Up to three levels of subfolders can be created under the root directory. Corresponding knowledge bases can be created in each level of folder. Folders support resource authorization. Regular users can only view authorized folders, and when authorizing a folder, the existing sub-resources under the folder can also be authorized.</p>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Shared Resources is an X-Pack feature of the Enterprise Edition.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"dataset\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Create Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Open the [Knowledge Base] page and click [Create Knowledge Base] to enter the Create Knowledge Base page. <br/>\nKnowledge base type:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>General knowledge base: Manages the upload of offline documents. The supported text document formats include Markdown, TXT, PDF, DOCX, and HTML, as well as QA pairs in Excel and CSV formats.</li>\n<li>Web Site Knowledge Base: used for online static text data management. After entering a Web Root Address, it automatically syncs the text data of the root address and its subordinate addresses.</li>\n<li>Feishu Knowledge Base: Supports connecting to Feishu cloud documents and spreadsheet documents, and importing Feishu document content into MaxKB for management.</li>\n<li>Workflow Knowledge Base: allows users to freely orchestrate the entire process from different data sources to writing into the knowledge base by dragging and dropping nodes, meeting the individualized knowledge management needs of enterprises.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: The Feishu knowledge base is an X-Pack feature; for specific usage, refer to <a href=\"../X-Pack/feishu_doc\"><strong>Feishu Document</strong></a>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"dataset\" src=\"../../img/dataset/create_dataeset.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"11\">1.1 General Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#11\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select the knowledge base type as general, enter the knowledge base name and description, and select an embedding model.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create a General Knowledge Base\" src=\"../../img/dataset/create_offline_dataset.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After creating a knowledge base, you can create new documents and upload offline documents.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>注意：对话用户为 X-Pack 功能。\n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Upload Document\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_office_document.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Offline documents can be uploaded by dragging and dropping or by selecting files. Document upload requirements:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Text files: Markdown, TXT, PDF, DOCX, HTML, XLS, XLSX, CSV, ZIP;</li>\n<li>Tables: XLS, XLSX, CSV, ZIP;</li>\n<li>QA Q&amp;A pairs: XLS, XLSX, CSV, ZIP;</li>\n<li>By default, up to 50 files can be uploaded at once, with each file not exceeding 100 MB. This is configurable: the maximum number of uploaded files is 1000, and a single document is up to 1000 MB;</li>\n<li>Supports selecting a folder and uploading the files under it that meet the requirements.</li>\n<li>\n<p>ZIP files come in two forms:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Markdown document + image files: reference the corresponding images in the Markdown document and package both in a ZIP.</li>\n<li>XLS/XLSX files + image files: reference the corresponding images in the XLS/XLSX files and package both in a ZIP.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Upload Document\" src=\"../../img/dataset/upload_document.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Document segmentation:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Select Segmentation Rules</strong> supports two segmentation methods: Intelligent Segmentation and Advanced Segmentation:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Intelligent Segmentation: segments hierarchically by Markdown format (up to 6 heading levels), with a maximum of 4096 characters per segment;</li>\n<li>Advanced Segmentation: Supports customizing the segment identifier, segment length, and automatic cleaning. Segment identifiers also support using regular expressions to process documents with complex structures.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Add segment titles as associated questions upon import</strong>: When checked, the titles of all segments will be set to the segments' associated questions.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Preview</strong>: View the segmentation effect based on the segmentation rules and settings.</p>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Segment Operations</strong>: In the segment preview, re-edit unreasonable segments and delete meaningless segments.</li>\n<li><strong>Step Operations</strong>: You can go back to the previous step to re-upload the document, or confirm the upload to start vectorization.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Upload Document\" src=\"../../img/dataset/upload_document2.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Intelligent Segmentation and Advanced Segmentation</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>Intelligent Segmentation</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Intelligent Segmentation Rules for MarkDown Files<br/></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Hierarchical segmentation by heading (up to 6 heading levels), with a maximum of 4096 characters per segment;</li>\n<li>When the character count of the lowest-level text paragraph exceeds the configured segment length, the system looks for a line break within the segment length to truncate the text.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Intelligent Segmentation Rules for HTML and DOCX Files</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Recognize heading formats and convert them to Markdown heading styles;</li>\n<li>Segment by drilling down level by level (up to 6 levels of headings), with each segment up to 4096 characters.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Intelligent Segmentation Rules for TXT and PDF Files</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Segments are split by the heading #; if there is no # heading, the text is split by 4096 characters.</li>\n<li>Find a line break within the segment length and truncate there.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Advanced Segmentation</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Supported segment identifiers: #, ##, ###, ####, #####, ######, -, blank line, carriage return, space, semicolon, comma, and period. You can also manually enter other segment identifiers or <a href=\"https://kb.fit2cloud.com/?p=bfe242a4-9a77-459c-ac75-4ef078e170c9\"><strong>Regular Expression</strong></a>.</li>\n<li>Segment length: the length of a single segment, ranging from 50 to 4096 characters.</li>\n<li>Auto Clean: When enabled, the system automatically removes duplicate and redundant symbols such as spaces, blank lines, and tabs.</li>\n<li><strong>Documentation Standards Suggestions</strong>:<ul>\n<li>Marker conventions: the segment markers of offline documents should follow a certain convention; otherwise the split segments will be irregular.</li>\n<li>Paragraph completeness: describe one complete piece of content within a single segment.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Advanced Segmentation\" src=\"../../img/dataset/advanced_segmentation.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Add segment titles as associated questions upon import:</strong> When checked, the titles of all segments will be set to the segments' associated questions.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Set Title as Related Question\" src=\"../../img/dataset/titel_set_question.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After clicking 【Start Import】, the system backend will perform auto segmentation -&gt; storage -&gt; vectorization on the documents; when processing finishes, the file status will show as Completed.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Edit Segment\" src=\"../../img/dataset/processing.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"12-web\">1.2 Web Site Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#12-web\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select the knowledge base type as Web site, enter the knowledge base name and description, select an embedding model, and enter the Web root address.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Web Root Address: the root node address of the online static website. The system automatically retrieves data from the web root address and its subordinate addresses. Taking the DataEase V2 online documentation as an example, the Web Root Address can be: <a href=\"https://dataease.io/docs/v2/\">https://dataease.io/docs/v2/</a>.</li>\n<li>Selector: For Web page data, you can specify to retrieve data within a certain div; by default the body data is retrieved. For example, to retrieve only the middle content of the DataEase online documentation, you can right-click to inspect the page, locate the middle inner region and find the div named md-content, then the selector input is: .md-content .</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Web Knowledge Base\" src=\"../../img/dataset/web_dataset.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Alt text\" src=\"../../img/dataset/DataEase_doc.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After clicking 【Create】, you are redirected to the document list page to view the details of the documents under the current Web site; when processing finishes, the file status will show as Completed.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Alt text\" src=\"../../img/dataset/web_doc.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"13\">1.3 Workflow Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#13\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports users independently orchestrating the full process from different data sources to knowledge base writes through node dragging, adapting to enterprises' personalized knowledge management needs.</p>\n<p>Select the knowledge base type as workflow knowledge base, enter the knowledge base name and description, and select an embedding model.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create Workflow Knowledge\" src=\"../../img/dataset/create_workflow_dataset.png\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"131\">1.3.1 Workflow Orchestration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#131\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The basic flow of knowledge base workflow orchestration: data source -&gt; document parsing -&gt; document segmentation -&gt; knowledge base write.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Set Workflow Knowledge Base\" src=\"../../img/dataset/set_workflow_dataset.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Data Source</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Note: The start node of the workflow, responsible for obtaining raw data. Users only need to develop data source tools according to the standard to connect to the workflow, without waiting for system version updates.</li>\n<li>Settings:<ul>\n<li>Built-in data sources: supports local files and Web sites;</li>\n<li>Tool Extension: supports data source tools to access other enterprise-level data sources.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Data Source Workflow Knowledge Base\" src=\"../../img/dataset/api_workflow_dataset.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Document Parsing</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Note: Convert raw data into plain text or structured text. Users can develop parsing tools according to the standard to connect to the workflow, without waiting for system version updates.</li>\n<li>Settings:<ul>\n<li>Supports automatic parsing of mainstream formats such as TXT, Markdown, DOCX, XLSX, CSV, PDF, and ZIP.</li>\n<li>Supports integrating other parsing tools through tools, such as OCR tools, MinerU, and other professional parsing tools.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Document Parsing Workflow Knowledge Base\" src=\"../../img/dataset/doc_workflow_dataset.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Document Segmentation</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Note: Split long text into retrievable units based on semantics or rules.</li>\n<li>Settings: Supports segmenting/non-segmenting for storage and referencing third-party segmentation tools.<ul>\n<li>Segmentation and storage:<ul>\n<li>Intelligent Segmentation: segments hierarchically by Markdown format (up to 6 heading levels), with a maximum of 4096 characters per segment;</li>\n<li>Advanced Segmentation: Supports customizing the segment identifier, segment length, and automatic cleaning. Segment identifiers also support using regular expressions to process documents with complex structures.</li>\n<li>QA Q&amp;A pair segmentation: extract \"question-answer\" pairs for ingestion.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Importing without segmentation: delete the “Document Segmentation” node to import documents without segmentation.</li>\n<li>Independently introduce third-party segmentation tools to adapt to complex content splitting needs.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Document Segmentation Workflow Knowledge Base\" src=\"../../img/dataset/docsegmente_workflow_dataset.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Knowledge write</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Note: The end node of the workflow, which completes data persistence and vectorization.</li>\n<li>Settings: After passing through nodes such as document parsing and document segmentation, the content will be automatically written to the knowledge base and vectorization will be performed.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Write to Workflow Knowledge Base\" src=\"../../img/dataset/input_workflow_dataset.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"132\">1.3.2 Debug and Publish<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#132\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After orchestration is complete, click the [Debug] button on the interface, and the system will execute the Workflow according to the flow.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Debug Workflow Knowledge Base\" src=\"../../img/dataset/debug_workflow_dataset.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In 【Execution Details】, users can view the running status of each node, such as whether the data source successfully retrieved the document, whether the parsing tool correctly extracted the content, whether the segmentation result meets expectations, and whether the write was successful.</p>\n<p>After debugging without errors, click [Publish] to make this workflow take effect.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Execution Details - Workflow Knowledge Base\" src=\"../../img/dataset/debug_workflow_dataset1.png\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"133\">1.3.3 Import Document<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#133\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After the workflow is published, users can perform the Import Document operation in the document list. Import Document is the same as the Debug feature on the workflow page.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Workflow knowledge base page\" src=\"../../img/dataset/main_workflow_dataset.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Import a Document Workflow Knowledge Base\" src=\"../../img/dataset/import_workflow_dataset.png\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"134\">1.3.4 Other Operations<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#134\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Template Center</strong></p>\n<p>In a workflow knowledge base, you can directly select the desired knowledge base workflow in the 【Template Center】. You only need to configure basic parameters such as the model and knowledge base in the orchestration interface to quickly complete the workflow deployment of the knowledge base and realize the intelligent implementation of typical business scenarios.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Template Center\" src=\"../../img/dataset/template_center.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>To enrich template resources and drive the sustainable development of the product ecosystem, MaxKB sincerely invites community users to participate in building the Template Center and share technical achievements;</p>\n<p>Contribution path: Refer to the template development guidelines provided by the official team to develop agent or knowledge base workflow templates for MaxKB;</p>\n<p>Submission method: After development is complete, submit the template to <a href=\"https://github.com/1Panel-dev/MaxKB-toolstore\">GitHub Official Repository</a>. The project team will review it according to the process, and once approved it will be listed on the MaxKB Template Center for all community users to use.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Import/Export Workflow</strong></p>\n<p>The workflow knowledge base supports export and import. The exported file has the extension <code>.kbwf</code>; to import a workflow, select a file with the corresponding extension.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Export Workflow\" src=\"../../img/dataset/export_flowdataset.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Execution Record</strong></p>\n<p>Each document import operation is recorded in the workflow's 【Execution Records】; users can search for specific execution records by initiator or status, enabling full-chain traceability of all import operations.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Execution Record - Workflow Knowledge Base\" src=\"../../img/dataset/record_workflow_dataset.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Release History</strong></p>\n<p>In the workflow knowledge base, you can view information such as the workflow, time, and user of published historical versions.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Release History\" src=\"../../img/dataset/release_history.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Auto Save</strong></p>\n<p>In the workflow knowledge base, manual saving is the default; automatic saving can also be enabled. Once automatic saving is enabled, the configuration is saved to the local machine every minute and synced to the backend database after a successful publish.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Auto Save\" src=\"../../img/dataset/auto_save.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Knowledge Base Operations<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB knowledge bases support sync, re-vectorization, question generation, resource authorization, viewing associated resources, transfer to, settings, export, and delete operations.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Knowledge Base Export\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_actions.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"21-web\">2.1 Synchronize Web Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#21-web\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For a Web site-type knowledge base, click [Sync] in the knowledge base panel to synchronously update the content of the Web knowledge base.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Synchronize &amp; Replace: re-fetch the documents from the web site and overwrite the documents in the local knowledge base.</li>\n<li>Full sync: First delete all documents in the local knowledge base, then re-fetch the Web site documents.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Knowledge Base Export\" src=\"../../img/dataset/web_sync.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"22\">2.2 Re-vectorization<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#22\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>If a different embedding model is selected in the knowledge base settings, newly added documents will be vectorized using the newly configured embedding model. To re-vectorize an existing knowledge base, click [Re-vectorize] in the knowledge base panel in the knowledge base card grid to re-vectorize the existing segments in the knowledge base.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Shared Re-vectorize\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_embedding.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"23\">2.3 Generate Questions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#23\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Use an AI model (with configurable model parameters) to summarize the file content based on the prompt and generate corresponding questions, which are automatically associated with segments.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Generate Question\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_create_problem.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"24\">2.4 Resource Authorization<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#24\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Resource Authorization】 on the knowledge base panel to authorize the knowledge base to the corresponding users.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resource Authorization\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_resources.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"25\">2.5 View Associated Resources<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#25\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the knowledge base list, click 【View Associated Resources】 on the knowledge base panel to view the resources associated with the knowledge base. You can search by name, creator, and type.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Dependencies: view the other resources on which the current resource depends (agent, model, knowledge base, tool);</li>\n<li>Depended on: view which other resources (Agent, model, knowledge base, tool) depend on the current resource.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Associated Resources\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_related_resources.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"26\">2.6 Move to<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#26\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the knowledge base list, click 【Move To】 on the knowledge base panel to move the knowledge base to another folder of tools under the same workspace.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Associated Resources\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_move.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"27\">2.7 Set Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#27\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the knowledge base list, click 【Settings】 on the knowledge base panel to enter the knowledge base settings page, where you can modify the basic information of the knowledge base (name, description, embedding model) and the upload rules: the maximum number of files per upload and the maximum size of a single document (MB).</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Knowledge Base Settings Page\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_setting.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"28-excelzip\">2.8 Export Documents Excel/ZIP<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#28-excelzip\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the knowledge base list, click 【Export Excel】/【Export ZIP】 on the knowledge base panel to export the segments of the knowledge base in Excel or ZIP file format. <br/>\nEach document is one Sheet in the Excel file, and each row in the Sheet displays one segment. When exporting as a ZIP file, the referenced images are exported together, named by guid, without format extensions.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Knowledge Base Export\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_export.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Knowledge Base Export\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_zip.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>To import a document Excel/ZIP knowledge base, first create a General Knowledge Base, click [Upload Document], select [QA Pair], upload the documents exported from the knowledge base, and click [Start Import].</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Knowledge Base Export\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_input.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"29\">2.9 Export Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#29\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports exporting all metadata of a knowledge base (documents, tags, questions, workflows) and their associations, supporting cross-environment migration and batch reuse; the exported file extension is <code>.zip</code>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Knowledge Base Export\" src=\"../../img/dataset/export_all_dataset.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Create】 -&gt; 【Import &amp; Create】, select the exported knowledge base file, and open it.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Knowledge Base Import\" src=\"../../img/dataset/input_all_dataset.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"210\">2.10 Delete Knowledge Base<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#210\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the knowledge base list, click 【Delete】 on the knowledge base panel to delete the knowledge base.</p>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: A knowledge base cannot be recovered after deletion. Please proceed with caution.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Knowledge Base Delete\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_del.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Batch Selection<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click batch selection to select multiple knowledge bases for move or delete operations.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Batch Operations\" src=\"../../img/dataset/batch_operation_dataset.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#1", "title": "1 Create Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#11", "title": "1.1 General Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#12-web", "title": "1.2 Web Site Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#13", "title": "1.3 Workflow Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#131", "title": "1.3.1 Workflow Orchestration ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#132", "title": "1.3.2 Debug and Publish ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#133", "title": "1.3.3 Import Document ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#134", "title": "1.3.4 Other Operations ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#2", "title": "2 Knowledge Base Operations ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#21-web", "title": "2.1 Synchronize Web Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#22", "title": "2.2 Re-vectorization ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#23", "title": "2.3 Generate Questions ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#24", "title": "2.4 Resource Authorization ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#25", "title": "2.5 View Associated Resources ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#26", "title": "2.6 Move to ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#27", "title": "2.7 Set Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#28-excelzip", "title": "2.8 Export Documents Excel/ZIP ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#29", "title": "2.9 Export Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#210", "title": "2.10 Delete Knowledge Base ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/dataset.html#3", "title": "3 Batch Selection ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html", "title": "Document", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Document <a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB knowledge base documents support sync, re-vectorization, tag settings, question generation, migration, settings, export, and delete operations.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Upload Document\" src=\"../../img/dataset/document_action.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Document Upload<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For a General Knowledge Base, click [Upload Document] to enter the upload page, where you can drag and drop files or select files/folders to upload.\nSupported file formats include: TXT, Markdown, PDF, DOCX, HTML, XLS, XLSX, CSV, and ZIP. If a folder is selected, files are automatically filtered by file extension. Up to 50 files can be uploaded at a time, and no single file may exceed 100 MB.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Upload Document\" src=\"../../img/dataset/upload_document.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For a Web site knowledge base, click [Import Document] to open the dialog box, enter the document link URL and selector, and the corresponding content will be synchronized.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Import Web Document\" src=\"../../img/dataset/upload_web_doc.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Document Synchronization<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Web Site Knowledge Base supports syncing selected documents. During sync, all segments under the current document are first deleted, and the text data at the document address is retrieved again and re-segmented.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Sync Document\" src=\"../../img/dataset/sysn_dataset.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Hit handling method:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model optimization: when a question hits a segment under this document, a prompt is generated according to the agent's prompt and sent to the model for optimization before returning the answer.</li>\n<li>Direct Answer: when a question hits a segment under this document, if the similarity meets the settings, the segment content is returned directly. For cases where you need to return information such as images and links, this method is recommended.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Allow download in knowledge sources: documents in the General Knowledge Base and the Feishu Knowledge Base support the [Allow download in knowledge sources] setting. After checking it, agents that include documents from this knowledge base will support downloading knowledge sources in their answers.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Document Settings\" src=\"../../img/dataset/doc_setting.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Generating Questions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select a document and click [Generate Question] or perform the generate-question operation. An AI model (with configurable model parameters) is used to summarize the file content and generate corresponding questions, which are automatically associated.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Generate Question\" src=\"../../img/dataset/gen_question.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Generate Question\" src=\"../../img/dataset/gen_question2.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"5\">5 Document Migration<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select a document and click [Migrate] to migrate the document to another knowledge base.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Migration Document\" src=\"../../img/dataset/move_web_doc.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"6\">6 Tag<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#6\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Tag Management: every knowledge base has an independent tag management system.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Tag Management\" src=\"../../img/dataset/Tag_Manage1.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Tag Management】 to create, edit, and delete tags; a knowledge base can have multiple tags, and each tag can have multiple tag values. You can view the documents associated with a tag and add or remove document tags directly from the tag dimension.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Tag Management\" src=\"../../img/dataset/Tag_Manage.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Tag Management supports viewing the documents associated with a tag, and supports directly adding or removing document tags from the tag dimension.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Tag Management\" src=\"../../img/dataset/Tag_association.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Add Tag: Select a document and click 【Add Tag】 to add the created tags to documents in batch; each document supports multiple tags.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Add Tag\" src=\"../../img/dataset/add_tag.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Add Tag\" src=\"../../img/dataset/add_tag1.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Tag Settings: click Tag Settings to view, add, or delete the tags bound to a document.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Tag Management\" src=\"../../img/dataset/tag_setting1.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Tag Management\" src=\"../../img/dataset/tag_setting1.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"7-excelzip\">7 Export Excel/ZIP<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#7-excelzip\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select a document. You can export a single document to Excel or export it as a Zip, and download the document to the local client.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Document Export\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_file_export.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Batch-select documents to batch-export them as Excel/Zip, downloading the documents to the local client.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Document Export\" src=\"../../img/dataset/dataset_file_export1.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"8\">8 Download the Original Document<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#8\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select a document and click [Download Original Document] to download the original document locally while keeping the original file.</p>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: The Download Original Document feature only supports files manually uploaded in【Upload Document】; otherwise, an error will occur: <code>文件不存在，仅支持手动上传的文档</code>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Download Original Document\" src=\"../../img/dataset/doc_down.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"9\">9 Replace the Original Document<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#9\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The general knowledge base supports replacing the original document. Click [Replace Original Document] to manually upload a file and replace the contents of the original document.</p>\n<p>Note:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Replacing the original document only updates the document itself; the vectorized and segmented content remains unchanged;</li>\n<li>After replacement, when the agent enables showing knowledge sources, the document displayed in the cited segment will be the updated document.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Replace Original Document\" src=\"../../img/dataset/replay_doc.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Replace Original Document\" src=\"../../img/dataset/replay_doc1.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"10\">10 Document Deletion<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#10\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select a document and click the delete button or perform the delete operation to delete the selected document.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Document Deletion\" src=\"../../img/dataset/doc_delete.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"11\">11 Enable and Disable Documents<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#11\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the status column of the document list, you can enable or disable a document. Once a document is disabled, the system will not retrieve the segments under that document when users ask questions. The system will retrieve them only after the document is re-enabled.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Enable Document\" src=\"../../img/dataset/doc_enable.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"12\">12 Segment Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#12\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After a document is imported, the system segments it according to the segmentation rules. Click a document in the document list to enter the document Segment Management page, where you can enable/disable, edit, insert above, migrate, move, delete segments, and add associated questions for segments.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Segment Management\" src=\"../../img/dataset/segmentation_management.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"121\">12.1 Add Segment<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#121\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Add Segment】 to open the Add Segment dialog; fill in the segment title, segment content (supports editing segment content in Markdown style), and associated questions, then click 【Submit】 to add a new segment.<br/>\n<strong>Suggestion:</strong> To accurately match segments, it is recommended to set associated questions for each segment, so that the associated questions are matched first and then the segment content is mapped, improving matching efficiency and accuracy.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Add Segment\" src=\"../../img/dataset/add_segmentation.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"122\">12.2 Edit Segment<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#122\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click the segment panel to edit the segmented information and associate questions on the segment details page.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Segment Details\" src=\"../../img/dataset/edit_segmentation.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"123\">12.3 Migrate Segment<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#123\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the segment management panel, you can migrate the selected segment to a document in another knowledge base.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Migrate Segments\" src=\"../../img/dataset/move_segmentation.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"124\">12.4 Move Position<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#124\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the segment management panel, you can move the selected segment to the top or bottom, or move it up or down.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Move position\" src=\"../../img/dataset/upanddown_segmentation.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"125\">12.5 Delete Segment<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#125\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In the segment management panel, you can delete the selected segment.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Delete Segment\" src=\"../../img/dataset/del_segmentation.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#1", "title": "1 Document Upload ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#2", "title": "2 Document Synchronization ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#3", "title": "3 Settings ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#4", "title": "4 Generating Questions ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#5", "title": "5 Document Migration ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#6", "title": "6 Tag ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#7-excelzip", "title": "7 Export Excel/ZIP ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#8", "title": "8 Download the Original Document ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#9", "title": "9 Replace the Original Document ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#10", "title": "10 Document Deletion ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#11", "title": "11 Enable and Disable Documents ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#12", "title": "12 Segment Management ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#121", "title": "12.1 Add Segment ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#122", "title": "12.2 Edit Segment ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#123", "title": "12.3 Migrate Segment ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#124", "title": "12.4 Move Position ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/doclist.html#125", "title": "12.5 Delete Segment ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/hit-testing.html", "title": "Hit Testing", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Hit Testing<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Knowledge base hit testing is an early validation of questions. Click 【Hit Testing】 and enter a test question. The system performs a vector search for segments related to the question in the current knowledge base, then returns the hit results according to parameters such as similarity and the number of returned Top segments. Based on the segment content returned by the hit testing, you can edit the segment again or add related questions to further improve and optimize the answer.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Hit Testing\" src=\"../../img/dataset/hittesting.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Parameter Settings Description</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Retrieval Mode</strong>: Currently supports three retrieval modes: vector retrieval, full-text retrieval, and hybrid retrieval. <br/><ul>\n<li>Vector retrieval: uses an embedding model to find the text segment most similar to the user's question by computing vector distance.</li>\n<li>Full-text search: searches by keyword and returns the text segments containing the most keywords.</li>\n<li>Hybrid Retrieval: Performs full-text retrieval and vector retrieval simultaneously, then reranks to select the best result matching the user's question from the two types of query results.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Similarity</strong>: The higher the similarity, the stronger the correlation between the question and the segment.</li>\n<li><strong>Return Top Segments Count</strong>: Returns the Top N segments that meet the conditions.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Hit Testing\" src=\"../../img/dataset/hittesting_rule.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/problem.html", "title": "Question", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Question<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Users with knowledge base management permission can collect related questions users might ask, create questions and associate them with content in knowledge base documents, and maintain the knowledge base FAQ list to improve the accuracy of Q&amp;A.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Shared question list\" src=\"../../img/dataset/problem_list.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Create Question<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Create Question】 and enter the question list line by line.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create Question\" src=\"../../img/dataset/create_problem.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Question-Associated Segment<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Associate Segments】; after the questions are added, they can be associated with segments in the document. When a user asks a question, the question library is matched first to look up the relevant segments.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Question-Associated Segmentation\" src=\"../../img/dataset/problem_segmentation.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Question Details<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Associated Segment Count】 to view the question details, modify the segment content, or cancel the association.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Question Details\" src=\"../../img/dataset/problem_detail.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Deleting Questions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports deleting questions individually or in batches; after deletion, the question will no longer appear in the associated segments.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Question Delete\" src=\"../../img/dataset/problem_del.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/problem.html#1", "title": "1 Create Question ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/problem.html#2", "title": "2 Question-Associated Segment ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/problem.html#3", "title": "3 Question Details ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/problem.html#4", "title": "4 Deleting Questions ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/word_tokenize.html", "title": "Custom Word Segmentation", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Custom Word Segmentation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Feature Overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Custom Word Segmentation feature allows administrators to add a professional terminology dictionary to the knowledge base, preventing professional terms from being incorrectly split during retrieval, thereby improving the accuracy and recall of full-text search and hybrid search.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Functional Value<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"21\">2.1 Core Issues<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#21\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In Chinese word segmentation, technical terms are often split incorrectly:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Terminology</th>\n<th>Incorrect Segmentation</th>\n<th>Correct Processing</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Xiaomi phone</td>\n<td>Xiaomi, mobile phone</td>\n<td>Xiaomi phone (as a whole)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Apple phone</td>\n<td>Apple, phone</td>\n<td>Apple phone (as a whole)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Artificial Intelligence</td>\n<td>Manual, Intelligent</td>\n<td>Artificial Intelligence (as a Whole)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"22\">2.2 Application Value<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#22\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Exact Match</strong>: Ensures that professional terms are retrieved as complete units</li>\n<li><strong>Improved Recall Rate</strong>: Avoids missed hits caused by term splitting</li>\n<li><strong>Industry Adaptation</strong>: Supports enterprise-customized industry terminology dictionaries</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Operation Guide<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"31\">3.1 Create Word<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#31\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click the 「Create Word」 button and enter the technical terms you want to preserve; you can quickly create multiple terms (one per line).</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"img.png\" src=\"../../img/dataset/create_word.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"32\">3.2 Running Word Segmentation Indexing<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#32\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After adding a term, click the 「Word Segmentation Index」 button, and the system will regenerate the document's word segmentation index.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"img.png\" src=\"../../img/dataset/word_index.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"33\">3.3 Precautions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#33\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<ul>\n<li>Custom word effective scope: applies only to <strong>Full-text Search</strong> and <strong>Hybrid Search</strong></li>\n<li>After adding a new term, you need to rerun word segmentation indexing for it to take effect.</li>\n<li>Word support scope: It is recommended to use purely Chinese terms and to avoid spaces and special characters</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Technical Principles<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"41\">4.1 Retrieval Process<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#41\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>User question → Read term library → Configure tokenizer → Tokenize → Match and retrieve</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"42\">4.2 Applicable Retrieval Modes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#42\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Retrieval Mode</th>\n<th>In Effect</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Full-text Search</td>\n<td>✓</td>\n<td>Based on keyword matching, using a tokenizer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hybrid Search</td>\n<td>✓</td>\n<td>Full-text search uses a tokenizer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vector Search</td>\n<td>✗</td>\n<td>Based on semantic similarity, without word segmentation</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/word_tokenize.html#1", "title": "1 Feature Overview ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/word_tokenize.html#2", "title": "2 Functional Value ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/word_tokenize.html#21", "title": "2.1 Core Issues ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/word_tokenize.html#22", "title": "2.2 Application Value ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/word_tokenize.html#3", "title": "3 Operation Guide ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/word_tokenize.html#31", "title": "3.1 Create Word ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/word_tokenize.html#32", "title": "3.2 Running Word Segmentation Indexing ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/word_tokenize.html#33", "title": "3.3 Precautions ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/word_tokenize.html#4", "title": "4 Technical Principles ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/word_tokenize.html#41", "title": "4.1 Retrieval Process ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/word_tokenize.html#42", "title": "4.2 Applicable Retrieval Modes ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/dataset/workflow.html", "title": "Workflow", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Workflow<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The General Knowledge Bases, Web Knowledge Bases, and Feishu Knowledge Bases (X-Pack) in MaxKB all support direct conversion to workflow knowledge bases, and the original documents are preserved after conversion.</p>\n<p><strong>Note: This conversion operation is irreversible and cannot be undone. After a Web Knowledge Base is converted to a Workflow Knowledge Base, the document list no longer has the document synchronization feature.</strong></p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Knowledge Base Transformation Workflow\" src=\"../../img/dataset/to_workflow.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html", "title": "Workspace Home", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Workspace Home<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Workspace Home statistics feature provides comprehensive resource management and operational data visualization. The home page consists of four major modules: <strong>Quick Create</strong>, <strong>Resource Overview</strong>, <strong>Monitoring Statistics</strong>, and <strong>Usage Leaderboard</strong>, providing administrators with resource scheduling and operational decision-making support.</p>\n</div>\n<hr/>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Page Layout<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The home page uses a modular design and mainly contains four core areas:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Module</th>\n<th>Function Positioning</th>\n<th>Core Content</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Quick Create</strong></td>\n<td>Quick Action Entry</td>\n<td>One-click creation of Agents, Knowledge Bases, Tools, and Models</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Resource Overview</strong></td>\n<td>Resource Statistics Display</td>\n<td>Total counts and categories of Agents, Knowledge Bases, Tools, and Models</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Monitoring Statistics</strong></td>\n<td>Operational Data Tracking</td>\n<td>Trends of active users, chat volume, Token consumption, and satisfaction</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Usage Leaderboard</strong></td>\n<td>Data Ranking Statistics</td>\n<td>Token consumption and chat counts of TOP Agents and TOP Users</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<hr/>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Quick Create<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"31\">3.1 Feature Description<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#31\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Quick Create module provides one-click creation entry points for commonly used resources, supporting quick creation or import of Agents, Knowledge Bases, Tools, and Models.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"first\" src=\"../../img/first/quick_create.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Resource Overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"41\">4.1 Feature Description<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#41\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Resource Overview module displays the total statistics and category information of various types of resources in the workspace, helping administrators quickly understand the resource distribution.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"first\" src=\"../../img/first/source_show.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"42\">4.2 Statistics Content<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#42\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<h2 id=\"5\">5 Monitoring Statistics<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"51\">5.1 Feature Description<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#51\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Monitoring Statistics module tracks the operational data of the workspace, including trend charts of active users, chat volume, Token consumption, and user satisfaction.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"first\" src=\"../../img/first/see.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"52\">5.2 Statistical Metrics and Trend Charts<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#52\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<h4 id=\"_2\">Core Metric Cards<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Metric</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Active Users</strong></td>\n<td>Number of active users within the statistics period and its period-over-period change</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Chat Count</strong></td>\n<td>Total number of chat interactions within the statistics period</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Total Tokens Used</strong></td>\n<td>Total Tokens consumed within the statistics period</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>User Feedback Metrics</strong></td>\n<td>Statistics of users' satisfied and dissatisfied ratings of chat results</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Chart</th>\n<th>Displayed Content</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Active User Trend</strong></td>\n<td>Daily change trends of active users and new users</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Chat Count Trend</strong></td>\n<td>Daily change trend of chat counts</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Tokens Consumption Trend</strong></td>\n<td>Daily change trend of Tokens consumption</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>User Satisfaction Trend</strong></td>\n<td>Daily change trends of satisfied and dissatisfied ratings</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"53\">5.3 Time Range Selection<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#53\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports selecting different statistics periods, including the past 7 days, 30 days, and 90 days.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"first\" src=\"../../img/first/day.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"54\">5.4 Filtering<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#54\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports filtering statistics by Agent to view the operational status of a specific Agent.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"first\" src=\"../../img/first/agent.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"6\">6 Usage Leaderboard<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#6\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"61\">6.1 Feature Description<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#61\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Usage Leaderboard module separately ranks TOP Agents and TOP Users by Token consumption and chat count, providing administrators with a basis for resource scheduling.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"first\" src=\"../../img/first/top.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"62\">6.2 Ranking Statistics<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#62\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<h4 id=\"tokens-top\">Tokens Consumption - TOP Agents<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#tokens-top\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Rank</th>\n<th>Displayed Content</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Ranking List</td>\n<td>Agents sorted in descending order of Tokens consumed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Consumption Value</td>\n<td>Total Tokens consumed by each Agent</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trend Indicator</td>\n<td>Indicates the trend of increase or decrease period-over-period</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"first\" src=\"../../img/first/token.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<h4 id=\"-top\">Chat Count - TOP Agents<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#-top\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Rank</th>\n<th>Displayed Content</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Ranking List</td>\n<td>Agents sorted in descending order of chat count</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Chat Value</td>\n<td>Chat count of each Agent</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trend Indicator</td>\n<td>Indicates the trend of increase or decrease period-over-period</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"first\" src=\"../../img/first/times.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<h4 id=\"tokens-top_1\">Tokens Consumption - TOP Users<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#tokens-top_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Rank</th>\n<th>Displayed Content</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Ranking List</td>\n<td>Users sorted in descending order of Tokens consumed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Consumption Value</td>\n<td>Total Tokens consumed by each User</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Trend Indicator</td>\n<td>Indicates the trend of increase or decrease period-over-period</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"first\" src=\"../../img/first/user.png\"/></p>\n<h4 id=\"621\">6.2.1 Export<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#621\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h4>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The leaderboard detail page supports exporting the full details as an Excel file after filtering data by a specified time range. The exported data includes all paginated data under the current filter conditions, not limited by the 20 records per page display limit.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"first\" src=\"../../img/first/export.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"first\" src=\"../../img/first/excel.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#1", "title": "1 Overview ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#2", "title": "2 Page Layout ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#3", "title": "3 Quick Create ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#31", "title": "3.1 Feature Description ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#4", "title": "4 Resource Overview ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#41", "title": "4.1 Feature Description ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#42", "title": "4.2 Statistics Content ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#5", "title": "5 Monitoring Statistics ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#51", "title": "5.1 Feature Description ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#52", "title": "5.2 Statistical Metrics and Trend Charts ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#_2", "title": "Core Metric Cards ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#53", "title": "5.3 Time Range Selection ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#54", "title": "5.4 Filtering ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#6", "title": "6 Usage Leaderboard ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#61", "title": "6.1 Feature Description ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#62", "title": "6.2 Ranking Statistics ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#tokens-top", "title": "Tokens Consumption - TOP Agents ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#-top", "title": "Chat Count - TOP Agents ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#tokens-top_1", "title": "Tokens Consumption - TOP Users ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/index/index.html#621", "title": "6.2.1 Export ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/1panel_ai_gateway_model.html", "title": "Connecting the 1Panel AI Gateway", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting the 1Panel AI Gateway</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before connecting the 1Panel AI Gateway, first obtain the external connection address and API Key on the <code>AI</code> &gt; <code>AI 网关</code> &gt; <code>API Key</code> page in 1Panel. Refer to the figure below:</p>\n<p>Select <code>OpenAI</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the model names available in the 1Panel AI Gateway.</li>\n<li>API Base URL: the external connection address of the 1Panel AI Gateway, for example <code>http://&lt;1Panel 服务器 IP&gt;:4000/v1</code>.</li>\n<li>API Key: the Key created on the 1Panel AI Gateway API Key page.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"1Panel AI Gateway API Key\" src=\"../../img/model/1panel_ai_gateway_api_keys.jpg\" width=\"800px\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>OpenAI - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"OpenAI Models\" src=\"../../img/model/openai_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/1panel_ai_gateway_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/1panel_ai_gateway_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/Regolo_model.html", "title": "Connecting Regolo", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Regolo</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before adding a Regolo large model, you first need to create an API Key in <a href=\"https://regolo.ai/\">Regolo AI</a>.</p>\n<p>Select <code>Regolo</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / image generation.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>API Key: obtain the API Key.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Regolo - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Regolo Large Language Model\" src=\"../../img/model/Regolo_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/Regolo_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/Regolo_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/X-Infer_model.html", "title": "Connecting Xorbits Inference", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Xorbits Inference</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select <code>Xorbits Inference</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / rerank model / speech recognition / speech synthesis / vision model / image generation.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>LLMs and rerank models require the API Base URL and API Key, while embedding models require the API Base URL.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>API Base URL: the Xorbits Inference service address, for example: <a href=\"http://192.168.20.242:9997\">http://192.168.20.242:9997</a>.</li>\n<li>API Key: if you do not have an API Key, enter any characters.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Xorbits Inference - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Xorbits Inference\" src=\"../../img/model/xinfo_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Xorbits Inference - Embedding Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Xorbits Inference\" src=\"../../img/model/xinfo_embed.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Xorbits Inference - Rerank Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Xorbits Inference\" src=\"../../img/model/xinfo_reranker.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Xorbits Inference - Speech Recognition Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Xorbits Inference\" src=\"../../img/model/xinfo_asr.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Xorbits Inference - Speech Synthesis Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Xorbits Inference\" src=\"../../img/model/xinfo_tts.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Xorbits Inference - Vision Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Xorbits Inference\" src=\"../../img/model/xinfo_version.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Xorbits Inference - Image Generation Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Xorbits Inference\" src=\"../../img/model/xinfo_version_gen.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/X-Infer_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/X-Infer_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/amazon_bedrock_model.html", "title": "Connecting Amazon Bedrock", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Amazon Bedrock</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select <code>Amazon Bedrock</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Permission: divided into private and public permissions. Private models are available only to the current user, while public models can be used by all users in the system, but other users cannot edit or delete them.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding / rerank / vision model.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the model names supported by Amazon Bedrock. The dropdown options are some commonly used LLM names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>Region Name: the region where the model is enabled.</li>\n<li>Access Key ID/Secret Access Key: Access Key ID and Secret Access Key are credentials used to authenticate programmatic access to AWS services (including Amazon Bedrock).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Amazon Bedrock - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"AWS LLM Model\" src=\"../../img/model/AWS_LLM.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/amazon_bedrock_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/amazon_bedrock_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/anthropic_model.html", "title": "Connecting Anthropic", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Anthropic</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before adding an Anthropic model, you need to register and create an API Key in 【Account Management - API Key】 in the console.</p>\n<p>Select <code>Anthropic</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / vision model.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names of various models supported by Anthropic. The options show some commonly used LLM names supported by Anthropic. Manual input is supported, but it must match the model names supported by Anthropic; otherwise, the verification will fail.</li>\n<li>API URL：<a href=\"https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages\">https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages</a></li>\n<li>API Key: the API Key created in the Anthropic console.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Anthropic - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"anthropic\" src=\"../../img/model/anthropic_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/anthropic_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/anthropic_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/azure_openai_model.html", "title": "Connecting Azure OpenAI", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Azure OpenAI</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before adding an Azure OpenAI large model, you first need to register in <a href=\"https://ai.azure.com/\">Azure AI Studio</a> and obtain the API Base URL, API Key, deployment details, and other information, as shown in the following figure:</p>\n<p>Select <code>Azure OpenAI</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / speech recognition / speech synthesis / vision model / image generation.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the specific base model is determined by the deployment name. See the figure above.</li>\n<li>API Version: model version</li>\n<li>API Base URL: the Azure OpenAI project API service URL; see the figure above.</li>\n<li>API Key: authentication verification information for the Azure OpenAI project API service; see the figure above.</li>\n<li>Deployment name: The deployment name of the model in the Azure AI Studio project playground.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Azure OpenAI Key\" src=\"../../img/model/Azure_APIKey.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Azure OpenAI DemployInfo\" src=\"../../img/model/Azure_deployInfo.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Azure OpenAI - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Azure_LLM Model\" src=\"../../img/model/azure_model.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/azure_openai_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/azure_openai_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/bailian_model.html", "title": "Connecting Alibaba Cloud Bailian", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Alibaba Cloud Bailian</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select <code>阿里云百炼</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / rerank model / speech recognition / speech synthesis / vision model / image generation / text-to-video / image-to-video.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>API Base URL: the access address for the model service API; it is currently required when the model type is a large language model.</li>\n<li>API Key: the access key for the model service API.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Different LLMs have different API Base URLs; please refer to the API call examples of the corresponding Base Model for details.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian API Key\" src=\"../../img/model/aliyun_bailian_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Alibaba Cloud Bailian large language model configuration example is shown below.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Large Language Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Alibaba Cloud Bailian embedding model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Embedding Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_embed.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Alibaba Cloud Bailian rerank model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Rerank Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_reranker.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Alibaba Cloud Bailian speech recognition models support real-time speech recognition (Fun-ASR/Gummy/Paraformer) and recording file recognition (Qwen and Qwen-Omni all-modal non-real-time models). For specific model names, see <a href=\"https://help.aliyun.com/zh/model-studio/qwen-speech-recognition?spm=a2c4g.11186623.help-menu-2400256.d_0_3_3_3.7d011e212E2YgO&amp;scm=20140722.H_2979031._.OR_help-T_cn~zh-V_1\">Alibaba Cloud Bailian Official Documentation</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Speech Recognition Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_asr_support.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Alibaba Cloud Bailian speech recognition model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Speech Recognition Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_asr.png\" width=\"500px\"/>\n<img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Speech Recognition Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_asr1.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Alibaba Cloud Bailian speech synthesis model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Speech Synthesis Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_tts.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Alibaba Cloud Bailian vision model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Vision Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_vision.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The default image size for the Alibaba Cloud Bailian image generation model is 1024 * 1024, the number of images is 1, and the style is &lt;auto&gt;, meaning the model randomly outputs the image style. The configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Image Generation Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_vision_gen1.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Image Generation Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_vision_gen2.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Alibaba Cloud Bailian text-to-video model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Text-to-Video Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_text2video.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Text-to-Video Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_text2video1.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Alibaba Cloud Bailian image-to-video model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Image-to-Video Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_picture2video.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Alibaba Cloud Bailian Image-to-Video Model Configuration\" src=\"../../img/model/bailian_picture2video1.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/bailian_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/bailian_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/deepseek_model.html", "title": "Connecting DeepSeek", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting DeepSeek</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before adding a DeepSeek large model, you first need to create an API Key in <a href=\"https://platform.deepseek.com/\">DeepSeek Open Platform</a>.</p>\n<p>Select <code>DeepSeek</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>API Key: create and view it on the DeepSeek Open Platform.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Kimi Model\" src=\"../../img/model/deepseek_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>DeepSeek - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"DeepSeek Model\" src=\"../../img/model/deepseek_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/deepseek_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/deepseek_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/dockerai_model.html", "title": "Connecting Docker AI", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Docker AI</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select <code>Docker AI</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / rerank model.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>API Base URL: the Docker AI service address, for example: <a href=\"http://192.168.20.242:9999/v1\">http://192.168.20.242:9999/v1</a>.</li>\n<li>API Key: if you do not have an API Key, enter any characters.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Docker AI - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Docker AI LLM Model\" src=\"../../img/model/dockerai_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Docker AI - Embedding Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Docker AI Embedding Model\" src=\"../../img/model/dockerai_embedding.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Docker AI - Rerank Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Docker AI Rerank Model\" src=\"../../img/model/dockerai_reranker.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/dockerai_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/dockerai_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/doubao_model.html", "title": "Connecting Volcano Engine", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Volcano Engine</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select <code>火山引擎</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / speech recognition / speech synthesis / vision model / image generation / text-to-video / image-to-video.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Other connection parameters for the Doubao large language model:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Base Model: the endpoint ID for online inference.</li>\n<li>API Base URL: <a href=\"https://ark.cn-beijing.volces.com/api/v3\">https://ark.cn-beijing.volces.com/api/v3</a></li>\n<li>API Key: Access Point -&gt; API Call -&gt; Authorize via API Key -&gt; select the API Key and copy it, as shown in the figure below</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine LLM Model\" src=\"../../img/model/doubao_jieru.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Volcano Engine LLM Model\" src=\"../../img/model/doubao_llm_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Speech recognition and speech synthesis require the input of App ID, Access Token, and Cluster ID.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>API Base URL: the API base URL for the speech recognition model is <code>wss://openspeech.bytedance.com/api/v2/asr</code>, and the API base URL for the speech synthesis model is <code>wss://openspeech.bytedance.com/api/v1/tts/ws_binary</code></li>\n<li>App ID: the application ID created in Volcano Engine.</li>\n<li>Access Token: the authentication information corresponding to the Volcano Engine application.</li>\n<li>Cluster ID: the service information corresponding to the Volcano Engine application.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine_Speech Recognition\" src=\"../../img/model/doubao_stt.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Volcano Engineo_Speech Synthesis\" src=\"../../img/model/doubao_tts.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Image generation requires entering the Access Key ID and Secret Access Key.</p>\n<p>After logging in to the Volcano Engine console, click the account dropdown in the upper right corner, select the 【API Access Key】 option, and click 【New Key】 to create the API key information.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Access Key ID: the service information in the Volcano Engine API access key.</li>\n<li>Secret Access Key: the authentication information in the Volcano Engine API access key.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine_Image Generation\" src=\"../../img/model/doubao_API.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Volcano Engine - Large Language Model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine LLM Model\" src=\"../../img/model/huoshan_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Volcano Engine - Embedding Model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine Embedding Model\" src=\"../../img/model/huoshan_embedding.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Volcano Engine - Speech Recognition model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine Speech Recognition Model\" src=\"../../img/model/huoshan_asr.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Volcano Engine - Speech Synthesis model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine Speech Synthesis Model\" src=\"../../img/model/huoshan_tts.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Volcano Engine - Vision model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine Vision Model\" src=\"../../img/model/doubao_vision.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Volcano Engine image generation model requires creating a new secret key in 【Console - Access Control - API Access Key】 on Volcano Engine; the example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine Image Generation\" src=\"../../img/model/doubao_gen1.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine Image Generation\" src=\"../../img/model/doubao_gen2.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Volcano Engine - Text-to-Video model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine Text-to-Video\" src=\"../../img/model/doubao_text2video.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine Text-to-Video\" src=\"../../img/model/doubao_text2video1.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Volcano Engine - Image-to-Video model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine Image-to-Video\" src=\"../../img/model/doubao_picture2video.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Volcano Engine Image-to-Video\" src=\"../../img/model/doubao_picture2video1.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/doubao_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/doubao_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/gemini_model.html", "title": "Connecting Gemini", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Gemini</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before adding a Gemini large model, you first need to create an API Key in <a href=\"https://aistudio.google.com/\">Google AI Studio</a>.</p>\n<p>Select <code>Gemini</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / speech recognition / vision model / image generation.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>API Key: obtain the API Key.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> To use the Gemini API, make sure the server where the program runs is located in <a href=\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/available-regions?hl=zh-cn\">Regions Supported by the Gemini API</a>; otherwise, the API cannot be called and Google AI Studio cannot be accessed.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Gemini APIKEy\" src=\"../../img/model/gemini_key.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Gemini - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Gemini Large Language Model\" src=\"../../img/model/gemini_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/gemini_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/gemini_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/hunyuan_model.html", "title": "Connecting Tencent Hunyuan", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Tencent Hunyuan</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before adding a Tencent Hunyuan large model, you first need to enable the Tencent Hunyuan service on Tencent Cloud and create a new secret key.</p>\n<p>Select <code>腾讯混元</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / speech recognition / vision model / image generation.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>APPID: obtain it from [Tencent Cloud - Console - Access Management - API Key Management].</li>\n<li>SecretId: obtain it from [Tencent Cloud - Console - Access Management - API Key Management].</li>\n<li>SecretKey: the SecretKey downloaded when creating a key in [Tencent Cloud - Console - Access Management - API Key Management].</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"tencent apikey\" src=\"../../img/model/tencent_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\"></div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The configuration example for Tencent Hunyuan - Large Language Model is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Hunyuan Large Language Model\" src=\"../../img/model/hunyuan_LLM.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The configuration example for Tencent Hunyuan - Embedding Model is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Hunyuan Embedding Model\" src=\"../../img/model/hunyuan_embed.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The configuration example for Tencent Hunyuan - Speech Recognition is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Hunyuan Embedding Model\" src=\"../../img/model/hunyuan_asr.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The configuration example for Tencent Hunyuan - Vision Model is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Hunyuan Vision Model\" src=\"../../img/model/hunyuan_vision.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For the Tencent Hunyuan - Image Generation Model, the default image size is 768 * 768, the number of images is 1, and the style is 201, i.e., the Japanese anime style. The default configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Hunyuan Image Generation Model\" src=\"../../img/model/hunyuan_vision_gen1.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Hunyuan Image Generation Model\" src=\"../../img/model/hunyuan_vision_gen2.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/hunyuan_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/hunyuan_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/kimi_model.html", "title": "Connecting Kimi", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Kimi</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before adding a Kimi model, you first need to register and create an API Key in <a href=\"https://platform.moonshot.cn/console/account\">Moonshot AI Open Platform</a>.</p>\n<p>Select <code>Kimi</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>API Base URL: <a href=\"https://api.moonshot.cn/v1\">https://api.moonshot.cn/v1</a></li>\n<li>API Key: create and view it under API Key management in the Kimi account center.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"kimi APIkey\" src=\"../../img/model/kimi_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Kimi - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Kimi Model\" src=\"../../img/model/kimi_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/kimi_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/kimi_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/local_model.html", "title": "Connecting a Local Model", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting a Local Model</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Download Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Download the model to the server and mount it in the MaxKB container. The following uses the Embedding Model as an example to explain in detail.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Download the embedding model to the local server.<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 推荐模型下载网址\n\nhttps://huggingface.co/models?other=text-embedding\n\n# 下载后存放在/opt/maxkb/model/local_embedding目录下\n\n</code></pre></div></li>\n<li>Use -v to mount the host model path into the MaxKB container.<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code>-v /opt/maxkb/model/local_embedding:/opt/maxkb/model/local_embedding\n\n# 说明： v 模型所在目录:MaxKB 容器内目录\n\n</code></pre></div></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In Model Management, click the provider 【Local Model】 to go directly to the next step of filling out the local model form.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: embedding model / rerank model.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the absolute path of the model in the MaxKB container.</li>\n<li>Model directory: the directory of the model (when the base model is a name, this directory takes effect; if the base model has an absolute path, this parameter has no effect; it is recommended to keep it consistent with what is entered for the base model).</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Local model - Embedding model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Local Embedding Model\" src=\"../../img/model/local_embed.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/local_model.html#1", "title": "1 Download Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/local_model.html#2", "title": "2 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/local_model.html#3", "title": "3 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/minimax.html", "title": "Connecting MiniMax", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting MiniMax</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select <code>MiniMax</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / speech synthesis / image generation / text-to-video / image-to-video.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>API Base URL: the model service address, for example: <a href=\"https://api.minimaxi.com/v1\">https://api.minimaxi.com/v1</a>.</li>\n<li>API Key: the access key for the model service API.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"MiniMax\" src=\"../../img/model/minimax_platform.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MiniMax - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"MiniMax LLM Model\" src=\"../../img/model/minimax_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MiniMax - Speech Synthesis Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"MiniMax TTS Model\" src=\"../../img/model/minimax_tts.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MiniMax - Image Generation Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"MiniMax Image Generation\" src=\"../../img/model/minimax_create_image.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MiniMax - Text-to-Video Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"MiniMax Image-to-Video\" src=\"../../img/model/minimax_create_video.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MiniMax - Image Generation Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"MiniMax Image-to-Video\" src=\"../../img/model/minimax_img_video.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/minimax.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/minimax.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/model_param.html", "title": "Model Operations", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Model Operations<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Edit<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click the More menu at the lower right of the model, then click 【Edit】 to modify the configuration information of a created model.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Edit Model\" src=\"../../img/model/edit_model.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Edit Model\" src=\"../../img/model/model_edit.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Model Parameter Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click the More menu at the lower right of the model, then click 【Model Parameter Settings】 to view the model parameter configuration, or configure other parameters provided by each platform.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Model Parameter Settings\" src=\"../../img/model/model_para_setting.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Add Model Parameter\" src=\"../../img/model/model_add_para.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Resource Authorization<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click the More menu at the lower right of the model, then click 【Resource Authorization】 to authorize the model to the corresponding users.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resource Authorization\" src=\"../../img/model/model_resource.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Viewing Related Resources<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click the More menu at the lower right of the model, then click 【View Related Resources】 to view the related resources of the model and its dependencies and dependents. You can search by name, creator, and type.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Dependencies: view the other resources on which the current resource depends (agent, model, knowledge base, tool);</li>\n<li>Depended on: view which other resources (Agent, model, knowledge base, tool) depend on the current resource.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Associated Resources\" src=\"../../img/model/model_relate_sresource.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/model_param.html#1", "title": "1 Edit ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/model_param.html#2", "title": "2 Model Parameter Settings ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/model_param.html#3", "title": "3 Resource Authorization ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/model_param.html#4", "title": "4 Viewing Related Resources ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/model_summary.html", "title": "Model Overview", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Model Overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Feature Overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB supports integration with models from multiple vendors and can connect to mainstream large language models. This includes, but is not limited to, locally deployed private models such as Llama 3 and Qwen 2, public model services in China such as DeepSeek, SILICONFLOW, Kimi, Zhipu AI, and Baidu Qianfan, and internationally renowned public model services such as OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, Anthropic, and Gemini. The integrated model types are extensive, covering text generation, embedding analysis, reranking algorithms, speech recognition, speech synthesis, computer vision models, and image generation, meeting diverse business needs and application scenarios.</p>\n<p>【Models】is used to manage various large models and provide model usage for subsequent knowledge bases and applications;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Shared model: after the System Administrator creates a shared model in [Shared Resources], it can be authorized to specified workspaces.</li>\n<li>All models: users can create models. Other users can view, use, and maintain them after <a href=\"../X-Pack/authorization_resources.html\"><strong>Resource Authorization</strong></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Shared Resources is an X-Pack feature of the Enterprise Edition.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Model\" src=\"../../img/model/model_view.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Model Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After selecting All Models on the left, select the corresponding provider and use Add Model to add the model.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Model\" src=\"../../img/model/create_model.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports editing, model parameter settings, resource authorization, viewing associated resources, and deletion.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Model\" src=\"../../img/model/edit_model.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Supports querying by creator, model type, and model name.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Model\" src=\"../../img/model/search_model.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Deleting a model requires a second confirmation; after confirming, the model will be deleted directly.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Model\" src=\"../../img/model/delete_model.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Supported Providers and Models<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For details on the types supported by each provider, see the table below (sorted alphabetically):</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">LLM</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Embedding Model</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Rerank Model</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Speech2Text</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">TTS</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Vision Model</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Image Generation</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Text-to-Video</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">Image-to-Video</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Alibaba Cloud Bailian</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Anthropic</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Amazon Bedrock</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Azure OpenAI</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>DeepSeek</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gemini</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>kimi</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>OpenAI</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SILICONFLOW</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tencent Cloud</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Tencent Hunyuan</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>volcano engine</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Thousand sails large model</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>iFlytek Spark</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>zhipu AI</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>local model</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ollama</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>vLLM</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Xorbits Inference</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Docker AI</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MiniMax</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">✔</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/model_summary.html#1", "title": "1 Feature Overview ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/model_summary.html#2", "title": "2 Model Management ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/model_summary.html#3", "title": "3 Supported Providers and Models ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/ollama_model.html", "title": "Connecting Ollama", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Ollama</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Ollama allows users to run and deploy large language models on local computers. Before adding an Ollama model, you need to install and deploy Ollama yourself and run the model first.</p>\n<p>For details, refer to: <a href=\"../../faq/Offline_install_OllamaModel.html\">Deploying LLM Models with Ollama Offline</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The model provider is <code>Ollama</code>, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog box:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / vision model / rerank model.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names. Custom input is supported, but they must match the model names supported by Ollama; otherwise, the verification will fail. If the model is not available locally, the system will download it automatically.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>LLMs also require the API Base URL and API Key, while embedding models require the API Base URL.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>API Base URL: connection information for the Ollama service address, for example: <a href=\"http://42.92.198.53:11434\">http://42.92.198.53:11434</a>.</li>\n<li>API Key: if no API Key is configured, you can enter any characters.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Click 【Add】; if verification passes, the model is added successfully, and you can then select the model in the application's AI model list.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Ollama - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Ollama Large Language Model\" src=\"../../img/model/ollama_model.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Ollama - Embedding Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Ollama Embedding Model\" src=\"../../img/model/ollama_embedding_model.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Ollama - Vision Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Ollama Vision Model\" src=\"../../img/model/ollama_vision.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Ollama - Rerank Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Ollama Rerank Model\" src=\"../../img/model/ollama_reranker.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/ollama_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/ollama_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/openai_model.html", "title": "Connecting OpenAI", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting OpenAI</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select <code>OpenAI</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / speech recognition / speech synthesis / vision model / image generation.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names. Custom input is supported, but they must match the model names supported by OpenAI; otherwise, the verification will fail.</li>\n<li>API Base URL: the domain of the overseas Open API is <code>https://api.openai.com/v1</code>; the API base URL format for domestic proxies is generally <code>反向代理地址/v1</code>.</li>\n<li>API Key: the Key used to access OpenAI.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>OpenAI - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"OpenAI Models\" src=\"../../img/model/openai_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>OpenAI - Embedding Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"OpenAI Models\" src=\"../../img/model/openai_embed.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>OpenAI - Speech Recognition Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"OpenAI Models\" src=\"../../img/model/openai_asr.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>OpenAI - Speech Synthesis Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"OpenAI Models\" src=\"../../img/model/openai_tts.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>OpenAI - Vision Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"OpenAI Models\" src=\"../../img/model/openai_vision.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>OpenAI - Image Generation Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"OpenAI Models\" src=\"../../img/model/openai_verison_gen.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/openai_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/openai_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/qianfan_model.html", "title": "Connecting Baidu Qianfan", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Baidu Qianfan</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before adding a Qianfan large model, you first need to register and log in in <a href=\"https://qianfan.cloud.baidu.com/\">Baidu AI Cloud Qianfan Large Model Platform</a>. Create the API Key and Secret Key in 【Security Authentication】 in the console.</p>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Qianfan ModelBuilder has launched a v2 inference API compatible with the OpenAI specification, and the v1 inference API will soon be retired. MaxKB is compatible with both the v1 and v2 APIs; when creating a model, you can specify the API version. When using v1, you need to enter the API Key and Secret Key parameters, while the v2 version only requires the API URL and API Key.</p>\n<p>Select <code>千帆大模型</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / rerank model.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the LLM model names supported by Baidu Qianfan. The options show some commonly used LLM names supported by Baidu Qianfan. Manual input is supported, but the names must match the model names supported by the Qianfan platform; otherwise, the verification will fail.</li>\n<li>API Version: the API interface version, v1/v2.</li>\n<li>API URL: an input parameter when API Version is v2; please enter <code>https://qianfan.baidubce.com/v2</code>.</li>\n<li>API Key and Secret Key: input parameters when API Version is v1, that is, the API Key and Secret Key used in the Baidu Qianfan model.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Baidu Application\" src=\"../../img/model/qianfan_app.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Qianfan Large Model v2 - LLM configuration example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Thousand sails large model\" src=\"../../img/model/qianfan_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Qianfan Large Model v2 - embedding model configuration example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Thousand sails large model\" src=\"../../img/model/qianfan_embedding.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Qianfan Large Model - rerank model configuration example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Thousand sails large model\" src=\"../../img/model/qianfan_reranker.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/qianfan_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/qianfan_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/siliconflow_model.html", "title": "Connecting SiliconFlow", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting SiliconFlow</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before adding a SILICONFLOW model, you first need to register and log in in <a href=\"https://siliconflow.cn/\">SILICONFLOW</a>. Create a new API Key in 【Account Management - API Key】 in the console.</p>\n<p>Select <code>SILICONFLOW</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / speech recognition / speech synthesis / image generation / rerank model / vision model.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names of various models supported by SILICONFLOW. The options show some commonly used LLM names supported by SILICONFLOW. Manual input is supported, but the names must match the model names supported by SILICONFLOW; otherwise, the verification will fail.</li>\n<li>API URL：<a href=\"https://api.siliconflow.cn/v1\">https://api.siliconflow.cn/v1</a></li>\n<li>API Key: the secret Key that was created.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"SILICONFLOW\" src=\"../../img/model/siliconflow_model.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"SILICONFLOW\" src=\"../../img/model/siliconflow_model2.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>SILICONFLOW - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"SILICONFLOW\" src=\"../../img/model/siliconflow_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>SILICONFLOW - Embedding Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"SILICONFLOW\" src=\"../../img/model/siliconflow_embedding.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>SILICONFLOW - Speech Recognition Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"SILICONFLOW\" src=\"../../img/model/siliconflow_asr.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>SILICONFLOW - Speech Synthesis Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"SILICONFLOW\" src=\"../../img/model/siliconflow_tts.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>SILICONFLOW - Image Generation Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"SILICONFLOW\" src=\"../../img/model/siliconflow_vision_gen.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>SILICONFLOW - Rerank Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"SILICONFLOW\" src=\"../../img/model/siliconflow_rerank.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>SILICONFLOW - Vision Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"SILICONFLOW\" src=\"../../img/model/siliconflow_vision.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/siliconflow_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/siliconflow_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/spark_model.html", "title": "Connecting iFlytek Spark", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting iFlytek Spark</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before adding an iFlytek Spark large model, you first need to register in <a href=\"https://www.xfyun.cn/\">iFlytek Open Platform</a> and create different applications in the 【Console】 based on the model type. After creating an application, the platform will automatically generate the APP ID, API Secret, API Key, and other information.</p>\n<p>Select <code>讯飞星火</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / speech recognition / speech synthesis.</li>\n<li>Base Model: corresponds to the domain in the API documentation. The dropdown options are commonly used base model names under different model types of iFlytek Spark, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>API Base URL: the API base URL differs for each base model. Enter the API base URL corresponding to the selected base model; for details, please refer to <a href=\"https://www.xfyun.cn/doc/\">iFlytek Open Platform Documentation Center</a>.</li>\n<li>APP ID: the ID of the application created on the iFlytek open platform.</li>\n<li>API Key: the API Key corresponding to the application access on the iFlytek open platform.</li>\n<li>API Secret: the API Secret corresponding to the application access on the iFlytek open platform.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"iFlytek APP\" src=\"../../img/model/xunfei_app.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>When adding an <a href=\"https://maas.xfyun.cn/modelService\">iFlytek Xingchen MaaS Platform</a> model, select Model API Call, create the model service, and view the API URL, APP ID, API Secret, API Key, and other related information in the model service list.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"iFlytek APP\" src=\"../../img/model/xunfei_app1.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"iFlytek APP\" src=\"../../img/model/xunfei_maas.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>iFlytek Spark - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"iFlytek Models\" src=\"../../img/model/xunfei_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>iFlytek Spark - Embedding Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"iFlytek Models\" src=\"../../img/model/xunfei_embed.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>iFlytek Spark - Speech Recognition Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"iFlytek Models\" src=\"../../img/model/xunfei_iat.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>iFlytek Spark - Speech Synthesis Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"iFlytek Models\" src=\"../../img/model/xunfei_tts.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/spark_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/spark_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/tencentcloud_model.html", "title": "Connecting Tencent Cloud", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Tencent Cloud</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before adding the Tencent Knowledge Engine atomic capability, you first need to enable the Knowledge Engine atomic capability service on Tencent Cloud and create a new API Key.</p>\n<p>Select <code>腾讯云</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>API URL：<a href=\"https://api.lkeap.cloud.tencent.com/v1/chat/completions\">https://api.lkeap.cloud.tencent.com/v1/chat/completions</a>。</li>\n<li>API Key: the OpenAI API KEY created in the console.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"tencent apikey\" src=\"../../img/model/tencent_atomicpower_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\"></div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The configuration example for the Tencent Cloud Knowledge Engine atomic capability - Large Language Model is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Knowledge Engine Atomic Capability: Large Language Model\" src=\"../../img/model/tencent_atomicpower_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/tencentcloud_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/tencentcloud_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/tongyi_model.html", "title": "Tongyi model", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Tongyi model</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before adding a Tongyi Qianwen model, you first need to create an API Key in the console of the Alibaba Cloud DashScope model service.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Qwen API Key\" src=\"../../img/model/tongyi_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select <code>通义千问</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Permission: divided into private and public permissions. Private models are available only to the current user, while public models can be used by all users in the system, but other users cannot edit or delete them.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / vision model / image generation.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names supported under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>API Key: create and view it under API Key management of the Alibaba Cloud DashScope Model Studio service.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Qwen large language model configuration example is shown in the figure below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Qwen Large Language Model\" src=\"../../img/model/tongyi_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The Qwen vision model configuration example is shown in the figure below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Qwen Image Model\" src=\"../../img/model/tongyi_vision.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Qwen image generation model: The default image size is 1024 * 1024, the number of images is 1, and the style is <auto>, that is, the model randomly generates the image style, as shown in the configuration example below:</auto></p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Qwen Image Model\" src=\"../../img/model/tongyi_vision_gen1.png\" width=\"500px\"/> </p>\n<p><img alt=\"Qwen Image Model\" src=\"../../img/model/tongyi_vision_gen2.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/tongyi_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/tongyi_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/vllm_model.html", "title": "Connecting vLLM", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting vLLM</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select <code>vLLM</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / embedding model / speech recognition model / vision model / rerank model.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>API Base URL: the vLLM service address, for example: <a href=\"http://192.168.20.242:8000/v1\">http://192.168.20.242:8000/v1</a>.</li>\n<li>API Key: if you do not have an API Key, enter any characters.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>vLLM - Large Language Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"vLLM LLM Model\" src=\"../../img/model/vLLM_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>vLLM - Embedding Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"vLLM Embedding Model\" src=\"../../img/model/vllm_embedding.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>vLLM - Speech Recognition Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"vLLM Speech Model\" src=\"../../img/model/vllm_asr.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>vLLM - Vision Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"vLLM Vision Model\" src=\"../../img/model/vllm_version_gen.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>vLLM - Rerank Model Configuration Example:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"vLLM Rerank Model\" src=\"../../img/model/vllm_reranker.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/vllm_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/vllm_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/zhipu_model.html", "title": "Connecting Zhipu AI", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1>Connecting Zhipu AI</h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Model<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Before adding a Zhipu AI model, you first need to register and create an API Key in <a href=\"https://open.bigmodel.cn/\">Zhipu AI Open Platform</a>.</p>\n<p>Select <code>智谱AI</code> as the model provider, and enter the following required information in the Add Model dialog:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model Name: the model name defined in MaxKB.</li>\n<li>Model Type: large language model / vision model / image generation.</li>\n<li>Base Model: the base model names under different model types. The dropdown options are some commonly used base model names, and custom input is supported.</li>\n<li>API Key: the API Key created on the Zhipu AI open platform.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Zhipu API Key\" src=\"../../img/model/zhipu_apikey.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Configuration Example<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Zhipu AI - Large language model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Zhipu_Large Language Model\" src=\"../../img/model/zhipu_llm.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Zhipu AI - Vision model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Zhipu_Vision Model\" src=\"../../img/model/zhipu_vision.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Zhipu AI - Image generation model configuration example is shown below:</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Zhipu_Image Generation Model\" src=\"../../img/model/zhipu_vision_gen1.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Zhipu_Image Generation Model\" src=\"../../img/model/zhipu_vision_gen2.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/model/zhipu_model.html#1", "title": "1 Add Model ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/model/zhipu_model.html#2", "title": "2 Configuration Example ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/team/team.html", "title": "Team Management", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Team Management<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>In MaxKB, teams can collaboratively maintain knowledge bases and applications. Two built-in roles are provided: Owner and Member. The creator of a knowledge base/application assumes the Owner role, and added member users all have the Member role. The Owner can add and remove members. <br/>\n<strong>Friendly reminder: the Community Edition is limited to 1 team member.</strong></p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Member List\" src=\"../../img/team/teamlist.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Add Member<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Add Member】; you need to enter the full member username or email before adding.<br/>\n<strong>Note:</strong> The member to be added must be an existing user.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Add Member\" src=\"../../img/team/addMembers.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Permission Settings<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After adding a member, you can assign the member permissions for knowledge bases and applications.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Manage permission: after a member logs in to MaxKB, they can manage and operate the corresponding resources.</li>\n<li>Usage permission: after a member logs in to MaxKB, they can only view the corresponding resources.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>After clicking 【Save】, the permission settings take effect.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Permission Settings\" src=\"../../img/team/permission_setting.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Remove Member<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【…】-&gt;【Remove】 in the member list to delete the member. After removal, the member will lose all permissions.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Remove Member\" src=\"../../img/team/del_member.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/team/team.html#1", "title": "1 Add Member ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/team/team.html#2", "title": "2 Permission Settings ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/team/team.html#3", "title": "3 Remove Member ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool.html", "title": "Tool", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Tool<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Feature Overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB allows users to obtain and query data, perform logical decisions, extract information, or handle other scenarios through various tools according to their business needs, and invoke these during agent orchestration to meet various complex business requirements.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Shared tool: after the System Administrator creates a shared tool in [Shared Resources], it can be authorized to specified workspaces.</li>\n<li>All tools: users can create tools. Other users can view, use, and maintain them after <a href=\"../X-Pack/authorization_resources.html\"><strong>Resource Authorization</strong></a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Tools are managed through folders, and up to three levels of subfolders can be created under the root directory. Corresponding tools can be created in each folder level. Folders support resource authorization; regular users can only view authorized folders, and when authorizing a folder, you can authorize the existing sub-resources under it.</p>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Shared Resources is an X-Pack feature of the Enterprise Edition.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Tool\" src=\"../../img/fx/tool.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Creating tools supports creating tools, creating Skills, creating MCP, creating data sources, importing to create, and adding from the tool store.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Tool\" src=\"../../img/fx/tool1.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Create Tool<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"21\">2.1 Dependency Installation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#21\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>If the tool implementation requires installing third-party dependency packages, you can install them using the pip command in the MaxKB container.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><code># 进入 MaxKB 容器中\n\ndocker exec -it maxkb bash\n\n\n\n# pip安装第三方依赖，如 pymysql，执行下面命令\n\npip install pymysql \n\n</code></pre></div>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"22\">2.2 Tool Creation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#22\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Tool】 to open the Create Tool page.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tool Name: the tool's logo and name, for easy identification. The tool logo can be customized and uploaded after saving.</li>\n<li>Description: Detailed description of the tool and usage notes; displayed in the component list of the Advanced Agent.</li>\n<li>Startup parameters: the parameters required for a tool to run, such as an API Key. Separating startup parameters from input parameters lets you focus only on input parameters in the workflow and also prevents sensitive information from being leaked.</li>\n<li>Input parameters: The input parameters of a tool. The data types of the parameters include string, int, dict, float, array, and boolean. You can assign custom values or reference parameters.</li>\n<li>Tool Content: supports custom Python tool code that can reference input variables; also supports automatic tool script generation, which can directly generate the corresponding Python code based on the tool name, description, and parameters.</li>\n<li>Output parameters: The result returned by the Python code execution.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create Function\" src=\"../../img/fx/add_tool.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Create Function\" src=\"../../img/fx/tool_create.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After writing the Python code, click [Debug] to verify the code's functionality. After debugging, click [Create] to complete the creation of the tool. A successfully created tool is [Disabled] by default.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Tool Debugging\" src=\"../../img/fx/tool_debug.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Enabled tools can be called as components in the Advanced Agent by clicking Add Component -&gt; Tool, or through the Tool of the AI Chat component.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Add Tool Node\" src=\"../../img/fx/use_tool.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Creating a Workflow<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Workflow】 and enter the workflow name and description.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Workflow Name: the workflow name, for easy identification.</li>\n<li>Description: Detailed description of the workflow and usage notes; displayed in the component list of the Advanced Agent.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create Workflow\" src=\"../../img/fx/add_workflow.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Enter the workflow editing page, where you can add components or other tools to orchestrate the workflow.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create Workflow\" src=\"../../img/fx/edit_workflow.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Basic Information: used to configure the basic data of the workflow tool, including the tool's input and output parameters. Each workflow tool has exactly one such node.</p>\n<p>Node Settings:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>User Input: the input parameters of the workflow. The parameter data types include string, int, dict, float, array, and boolean. They can be custom assigned or reference parameters.</li>\n<li>Output parameters: The result returned by the workflow execution.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create Workflow\" src=\"../../img/fx/workflow_basicmsg.png\" width=\"500px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Start: serves as the starting point of workflow execution; all subsequent nodes begin their flow from this node.</p>\n<p>Global variables: input parameters set in the workflow basic information, serving as the global variables of the entire workflow.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create Workflow\" src=\"../../img/fx/workflow_action.png\" width=\"300px\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>For other components, refer to: <a href=\"../app/workflow_app#2\">Basic Components</a></p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"4-skills\">4 Creating Skills<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4-skills\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Note: Due to environmental constraints and security considerations, Skills only supports Skills triggered by Python.</strong></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Skills】 to open the Create Skills page.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Name: the name of the Skills, for easy identification.</li>\n<li>Description: detailed description of Skills and usage notes; it will be displayed in the component list of the Advanced Agent.</li>\n<li>Startup parameters: the parameters required for the Skills to run, such as an API Key. Separating startup parameters from input parameters lets you focus only on input parameters in the workflow and also prevents sensitive information from being leaked.</li>\n<li>Skills File: drag and drop or select the Skills ZIP file, up to 100 MB in size. Supports re-upload and download.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create Skills\" src=\"../../img/fx/add_skills.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Newly created Skills are Disabled by default. After enabling a Skill, you can reference it in the Skills of Advanced Agent -&gt; AI Chat.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Skills Usage\" src=\"../../img/fx/use_skills.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"5-mcp\">5 Create MCP<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5-mcp\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【MCP】 to open the Create MCP page.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>MCP Name: the name and Logo of the MCP, for easy identification. The MCP Logo can be customized and uploaded after saving.</li>\n<li>Description: detailed description of MCP and usage notes.</li>\n<li>MCP Server Config: fill in the MCP Server configuration parameters in JSON format. Call the tools in the MCP service via the SSE/Streamable HTTP protocol.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create MCP\" src=\"../../img/fx/add_MCP.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Newly created MCPs are Disabled by default. After enabling an MCP, you can reference it in the MCP of AI Chat, or call it in the Advanced Agent by clicking Add Component -&gt; MCP Call to add it as a component.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"MCP Usage\" src=\"../../img/fx/use_MCP.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"6\">6 Create Data Source<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#6\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Data Source】 to open the Create Data Source page.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Name: the data source logo and data source name, for easy identification. The data source logo can be customized and uploaded after saving.</li>\n<li>Description: Detailed description of the data source and usage notes; displayed in the component list of the Workflow Knowledge Base.</li>\n<li>Startup parameters: the parameters required for a data source to run, such as Token, Secret, etc. Separating startup parameters from input parameters lets you focus only on input parameters in the workflow and also prevents sensitive information from being leaked.</li>\n<li>Input parameters: The input parameters of a data source. The data types of the parameters include string, int, float, and array. You can assign custom values or reference parameters.</li>\n<li>Function content: write custom Python data source code, which can reference input variables.</li>\n<li>Output parameters: The result returned by the Python code execution.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Data Source\" src=\"../../img/fx/data_source.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Newly created data sources are Disabled by default. After enabling a data source tool, you can add the data source to create a knowledge base in the Workflow Knowledge Base by clicking Add Component -&gt; Data Source.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Data Source Usage\" src=\"../../img/fx/data_source_use.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"7\">7 Create from the Tool Store<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#7\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The tool store is a feature module in the MaxKB system that helps users extend the system's capabilities.</p>\n<p>Tools in the tool store are mainly categorized into web search, database query, API tools, content processing, message push, and translation tools, among others.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Tool Store\" src=\"../../img/fx/tool_sho_list.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Users can directly select the tools they need in the store without manual development or complex integration, which significantly improves the efficiency of calling tools.</p>\n<p>To enrich Tool Store resources and drive the sustainable development of the product ecosystem, MaxKB sincerely invites community users to contribute tools and share technical achievements:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Contribution path: Developers can follow the tool development guidelines provided by the official team to develop tools for MaxKB (such as API integration tools and local functionality tools);</li>\n<li>Submission method: After development is complete, submit the tool code to <a href=\"https://github.com/1Panel-dev/MaxKB-toolstore\">GitHub Official Tool Repository</a>. The project team will review it according to the process, and once approved it will be listed on the MaxKB Tool Store for all community users to use.</li>\n<li>Co-building the development ecosystem: tools contributed by the community can not only help more users solve real problems, but also promote the diversified development of the MaxKB tool ecosystem, forming a positive cycle of \"user needs - tool development - ecosystem improvement\".</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>After a tool is added, once you configure the startup parameters (such as database connection information, API Key, etc.) and enable it, it can be called in the Advanced Agent.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Startup Parameters\" src=\"../../img/fx/sartup_parameters.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"parameter configuration\" src=\"../../img/fx/fill_parameters.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Advanced Orchestration\" src=\"../../img/fx/use_tool_shop.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool.html#1", "title": "1 Feature Overview ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool.html#2", "title": "2 Create Tool ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool.html#21", "title": "2.1 Dependency Installation ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool.html#22", "title": "2.2 Tool Creation ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool.html#3", "title": "3 Creating a Workflow ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool.html#4-skills", "title": "4 Creating Skills ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool.html#5-mcp", "title": "5 Create MCP ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool.html#6", "title": "6 Create Data Source ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool.html#7", "title": "7 Create from the Tool Store ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool_param.html", "title": "Tool Operations", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Tool Operations<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Copy Tool<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Copy】 on the tool panel to open the Copy Tool dialog. After editing and modifying the original tool content, click 【Create】 to quickly create a new tool.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Copy Tool\" src=\"../../img/fx/copy_tool.png\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"Copy Tool\" src=\"../../img/fx/copy_tool1.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Resource Authorization<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Resource Authorization】 on the tool panel to authorize the tool to the corresponding users.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Resource Authorization\" src=\"../../img/fx/resource_tool.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Trigger<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Trigger】 on the tool panel to add a scheduled or event-triggered trigger for the tool.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Trigger\" src=\"../../img/fx/add_trigger_tool.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Creating a Trigger: click 【Add】 to create a trigger.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Trigger Name: the name of the trigger, used to identify different triggers and their trigger conditions.</li>\n<li>Description: Detailed description of the trigger and usage notes.</li>\n<li>Type:<ul>\n<li>Scheduled trigger: tasks can be executed monthly, weekly, daily, or at intervals, and Cron expressions are supported.</li>\n<li>Event trigger: that is, a Webhook trigger. When you create an event trigger, the system automatically generates a URL and Bearer Token, allowing the caller to send HTTP requests (with the Token in the Header) carrying request parameters to trigger the corresponding tool.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Task execution: the task executed by the trigger, which requires entering the corresponding parameter content.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Create Trigger\" src=\"../../img/fx/trigger_tool.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Create Trigger\" src=\"../../img/fx/webhook_trigger.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Viewing Related Resources<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【View Related Resources】 on the tool panel to view the associated resources of this model. You can search by name, creator, and type.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"View Related Resources\" src=\"../../img/fx/relate_resource_tool.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"5\">5 View Execution Record<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【View Execution Records】 on the tool panel to view the execution records of the tool. You can filter by trigger source, type, and status to view the corresponding execution records and execution details.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Dependencies: view the other resources on which the current resource depends (agent, model, knowledge base, tool);</li>\n<li>Depended on: view which other resources (Agent, model, knowledge base, tool) depend on the current resource.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"View Execution Records\" src=\"../../img/fx/record_tool.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"6\">6 Move to<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#6\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Move to】 on the tool panel to move the tool to another folder of tools under the same workspace.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Transfer Resources\" src=\"../../img/fx/move_tool.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"7\">7 Tool Export/Import<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#7\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Tools support export and import; the exported file has the extension <code>.tool</code>.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Function Export\" src=\"../../img/fx/import_export_dx.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Import &amp; Create】, select the file with the extension <code>.tool</code>, and open it.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Function Import\" src=\"../../img/fx/import_fx.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>The tool is imported automatically. Imported tools are Disabled by default; you can click a tool to enter tool editing to view and modify it.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Function imported successfully\" src=\"../../img/fx/import_success_fx.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"8\">8 Delete Tool<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#8\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click the 【Delete】 button on the tool panel to delete the tool.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Delete tool\" src=\"../../img/fx/del_tool.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p><strong>Note: After a tool is deleted, it cannot be recovered.</strong> If an agent references this tool, the message 【This tool is unavailable】will be displayed on the orchestration page.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"The agent references a deleted tool.\" src=\"../../img/fx/use_del_tool.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"9\">9 Batch Select<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#9\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\"></div>\n<p>Click batch selection to select multiple tools for move or delete operations.</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Batch Operations\" src=\"../../img/fx/batch_operation_tool.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool_param.html#1", "title": "1 Copy Tool ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool_param.html#2", "title": "2 Resource Authorization ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool_param.html#3", "title": "3 Trigger ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool_param.html#4", "title": "4 Viewing Related Resources ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool_param.html#5", "title": "5 View Execution Record ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool_param.html#6", "title": "6 Move to ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool_param.html#7", "title": "7 Tool Export/Import ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool_param.html#8", "title": "8 Delete Tool ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/tool/tool_param.html#9", "title": "9 Batch Select ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/trigger/trigger.html", "title": "Trigger", "text": "<article class=\"md-content__inner md-typeset\">\n<h1 id=\"_1\">Trigger<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#_1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h1>\n<h2 id=\"1\">1 Trigger Overview<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#1\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>MaxKB allows users to automate agent execution by configuring trigger conditions such as schedules and events according to their business needs, to meet various complex business requirements.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Scheduled trigger: tasks can be executed monthly, weekly, daily, or at intervals.</li>\n<li>Event trigger: that is, a Webhook trigger. When you create an event trigger, the system automatically generates a URL and Bearer Token, allowing the caller to send HTTP requests (with the Token in the Header) carrying request parameters to trigger the corresponding tool.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Community Edition admin account, and the Workspace Administrator role in the Professional/Enterprise Edition, can perform full-lifecycle configuration and management of all Triggers in a workspace.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Trigger\" src=\"../../img/trigger/trigger.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"2\">2 Create Trigger<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#2\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<h3 id=\"21\">2.1 Scheduled Trigger<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#21\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>On the Trigger page, click 【Create】 and fill in the trigger name and description.</p>\n<p>Select the trigger type as <strong>Scheduled Trigger</strong> and select the trigger cycle to execute tasks daily, weekly, monthly, or at interval events.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Scheduled Trigger\" src=\"../../img/trigger/timer_trigger.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select the agent or tool that this scheduled trigger will execute tasks for, and fill in the input parameters of the agent or tool to ensure the trigger can execute the tasks properly.</p>\n<p>A created trigger is disabled by default and needs to be started manually.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Scheduled Trigger\" src=\"../../img/trigger/timer_trigger1.png\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"22\">2.2 Event Trigger<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#22\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h3>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>On the Trigger page, click 【Create】 and fill in the trigger name and description.</p>\n<p>Select the trigger type as <strong>Event Trigger</strong>, copy the corresponding URL and Bearer Token, and the caller can send an HTTP request (with the Token in the Header) carrying the request parameters to trigger the corresponding agent or tool.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Event Trigger\" src=\"../../img/trigger/webhook_trigger.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Select the agent or tool that this scheduled trigger will execute tasks for, and fill in the input parameters of the agent or tool to ensure the trigger can execute the tasks properly.</p>\n<p>A created trigger is disabled by default and needs to be started manually.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Event Trigger\" src=\"../../img/trigger/webhook_trigger1.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"3\">3 Enable/Disable Triggers<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#3\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>On the trigger page, you can enable/disable a single trigger or enable/disable triggers in batches.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Enable/Disable Trigger\" src=\"../../img/trigger/active_trigger.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"4\">4 Editing a Trigger<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#4\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>On the Trigger page, click the 【Edit】 button to modify the trigger content.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Edit Trigger\" src=\"../../img/trigger/edit_trigger.png\"/>\n<img alt=\"Edit Trigger\" src=\"../../img/trigger/edit_trigger1.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"5\">5 Execution Record<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#5\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>On the Trigger page, click the 【Execution Records】 button to view the execution records of the trigger.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Execution Record\" src=\"../../img/trigger/trigger_run_record.png\"/></p>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>Click 【Execution Details】 to view the input/output of the agent's workflow or tool that was executed.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Execution Record\" src=\"../../img/trigger/trigger_run_record1.png\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"6\">6 Delete Trigger<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#6\" title=\"Permanent link\">¶</a></h2>\n<div class=\"admonition abstract\">\n<p>On the trigger page, you can delete a single trigger or delete triggers in batches.</p>\n</div>\n<p><img alt=\"Delete Trigger\" src=\"../../img/trigger/delete_trigger.png\"/></p>\n</article>"}, {"location": "user_manual/trigger/trigger.html#1", "title": "1 Trigger Overview ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/trigger/trigger.html#2", "title": "2 Create Trigger ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/trigger/trigger.html#21", "title": "2.1 Scheduled Trigger ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/trigger/trigger.html#22", "title": "2.2 Event Trigger ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/trigger/trigger.html#3", "title": "3 Enable/Disable Triggers ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/trigger/trigger.html#4", "title": "4 Editing a Trigger ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/trigger/trigger.html#5", "title": "5 Execution Record ¶", "text": ""}, {"location": "user_manual/trigger/trigger.html#6", "title": "6 Delete Trigger ¶", "text": ""}]};
